olve them viaclientLazy. This simplifies loading, avoids repeated remote importoverhead, and ensures shell uses the same component instancesexposed by the auth micro-frontend.","tree":{"sha":"d8d7ebe504b496f39f57bfa9836dfc19748feeb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Its-Satyajit/MFECP/git/trees/d8d7ebe504b496f39f57bfa9836dfc19748feeb2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Its-Satyajit/MFECP/git/commits/9408697a3290240625032454cd839187011d3403","verification":{"payload":"tree d8d7ebe504b496f39f57bfa9836dfc19748feeb2\nparent 3cdd2c11cd5d91bccbe26c48e4155fc37b56b59f\nauthor It''s Satyajit💫 <77627641+Its-Satyajit@users.noreply.github.com> 1779272183 +0530\ncommitter It''s Satyajit💫 <77627641+Its-Satyajit@users.noreply.github.com> 1779272183 +0530\ngitbutler-headers-version 2\nchange-id rrytqskypmnulktonyruylsyrvvvzmnv\n\nchore(vite): mark additional React runtimes as singletonsAdd react/jsx-runtime,/js-dev-runtime and react-dom/client to theite module federation shared configuration so app uses a single of each React runtime across federated modules. This preventsduplicate React runtimes and avoids mismatches that can cause hooks andrendering to behave incorrectly when loading remotes.\n\nrefactor(shell): load auth pages via local re-exportsReplace dynamic imports for LoginPage and RegisterPagedirectly imported re-exports from the auth package and resolve them viaclientLazy. This simplifies loading, avoids repeated remote importoverhead, and ensures shell uses the same component instancesexposed by the auth micro-frontend.","reason":"bad_email","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEERHviHF7QgrzyNLrRf7mT6JcVYAMFAmoNifcACgkQf7mT6JcV\nYAMMFhAAnKtvx05ziDK8o7RSod0yxLyi21ID1p3PNgDJS6WGG+wQVRkCFDwOkrTA\nCt6f/1kMe714ypdfV41UYX929QPslisYYjmV/6VqQjQqsDDTgJI26JxlAliJyGqT\n7QKHBJsnCWkoLqtIzHkbnJnw2vIh6xz1KUsVoZnEHMWPWugsJ00kvtLKMBhC/X8L\nNjE1lWkjSXJgwkrIfsuLE6frKb5FUwaVx6VS0+Mk2HTbdzc4YQOLKaLvOlJlWNcy\nnd7Uw7AIv5EgJbtQX1x5ocEQCkAxWd8Kwi5LfLrLYCIzPT6OOOJe+K