/api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/6b85835503a0f377662b8a22800dce0ddb1d3b12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:52:30Z","email":"57627710+eemaanamir@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Eemaan Amir"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:52:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(announcements): render banner expiry as the picked calendar date (#39)\n\nBackend stores banner_expires_at as end-of-day UTC, so `new Date(iso).toLocaleDateString()` shifted the display to the next day in timezones east of UTC (banner picked as 30 Sep in PKT showed as 1 Oct). Extract the YYYY-MM-DD portion and build a local Date so the list and details modal show the calendar date the admin actually picked.","tree":{"sha":"8ad30f12f239c9931348580c020acdcaa433e714","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/trees/8ad30f12f239c9931348580c020acdcaa433e714"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/commits/6b85835503a0f377662b8a22800dce0ddb1d3b12","verification":{"payload":"tree 8ad30f12f239c9931348580c020acdcaa433e714\nparent b5405626f41a122bcb88dee3e4ab771add51fccb\nauthor Eemaan Amir <57627710+eemaanamir@users.noreply.github.com> 1790761950 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790761950 +0500\n\nfix(announcements): render banner expiry as the picked calendar date (#39)\n\nBackend stores banner_expires_at as end-of-day UTC, so `new Date(iso).toLocaleDateString()` shifted the display to the next day in timezones east of UTC (banner picked as 30 Sep in PKT showed as 1 Oct). Extract the YYYY-MM-DD portion and build a local Date so 