ttps://api.github.com/users/arbirali","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/146c569045d969c67297bb84c0b45efb72a547ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T09:20:56Z","email":"rahat.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Rahat Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T09:20:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(biodata-edit-requests): render the table with Paragon DataTable (#32)\n\nThe hand-written table had no responsive behaviour: on a narrow viewport the\nlast columns spilled off the page instead of scrolling.\n\n- The table is a Paragon DataTable with a Cell per column; its own isLoading\n  spinner and EmptyTable replace the hand-rolled placeholder rows.\n- It keeps a readable minimum width inside a horizontally scrolling wrapper,\n  so the cells scroll rather than squash on a phone.\n- Paragon caps every DataTable cell at `max-width: 20vw` - about 75px on a\n  phone - and clips the overflow, cutting messages and notes mid-word.\n  index.scss replaces that with a fixed 20rem cap for every table, and the\n  duplicate override in reports-styles.scss goes with it.","tree":{"sha":"5e1fdba9cbd591e4b699c2894f1ede240c7ee498","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/trees/5e1fdba9cbd591e4b699c2894f1ede240c7ee498"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/commits/146c569045d969c67297bb84c0b45efb72a547ae","verification":{"payload":"tree 5e1fdba9cbd591e4b699c2894f1ede240c7ee498\nparent 3e6564f8f904d329a4d8aea592b1e16e219c4d7b\nauthor Rahat Ali <rahat.ali@arbisoft.com> 1789723256 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789723256 +0500\n\nfix(biodata-edit-requests): render the table with Paragon DataTable (#32)\n\nThe hand-written table had no responsive behaviour: on a narrow viewport the\nlast columns spilled off the page instead of scrolling.\n\n- The table is a Paragon DataTable with a Cell per column; its own isLoading\n  spinner and EmptyTable replace the hand-rolled placeholder rows.\n- It keeps a readable minimum width inside a horizontally scrolling wrapper,\n  so the cells scroll rather than squash on a phone.\n- Paragon caps every DataTable cell at `max-width: 20vw` - about 75px on a\n  phone - and clips the overflow, cutting messages and notes mid-word.\n  index.scss replaces that with a fixed 20rem cap for every table, and the\n  duplicate override in reports-styles.scss goes with it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrQJ4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhK8QAECM3NNb6noBd+2TfUhEGC1a\nGUY/bq3gW6YJ83EuhzvNdkuiOLnfEkxLG6oJD4E0KIN8vXHD+FfmekfrkOMEV6eC\nYVRt8YzwNGdgyhdWZVQa3mu9GHK10JVkYTC7yQ5LfN8sq1kT/2VpVuoeY4Gv1ly1\nDa+ZQQJn9sUbCGoLtR5WuarbXcVxkpxrU654198g8Yv1KumxOl5ZGVjXsqFqhaEy\nX0WN8Q2RT+AbRh/JEFBB7bVzyktcyHQymfc0BFO1A7aUUw2Zk4rWZSGttFLCIicy\nXQXCU0viuls5c5UsjPitmV77Hos8AES3fMtbC/chwX+hmfd7ufi+YpAyOfj0h+/q\nZQ8r5jegdBwAJyuo5QtPwrMPx+6F91DV+2pz5vD3SjZMiZ7VpGSx/MRHRFUVcUh0\n0GGMEbIr0cTYySGJc5ZKV6upSWM95FZcaDo41BKxGi0+ZQQDCvxOwMzDHXf8voTb\nXCFlqHh0X+xbTDCTgR68PLcakmvIsq2BPwVxGibQV6lxz3xxawdaSBtfMz+mGlej\np9cTTpBRIrV/7WhMaNKgaWLiY0qhyQ3r7UnoI1c/xqmI6JzjMeldGVvvAHrXs2sd\ntzyy6a6EE5KvduGrNSWblVdCbGTPus/NjVhzo4loYq1I88eJC62EgkhlHyf647KX\n2sBLWhSZ7/9SYaYw2yDC\n=34Kh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T09:20:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/146c569045d969c67297bb84c0b45efb72a547ae","node_id":"C_kwDOSir9AdoAKDE0NmM1NjkwNDVkOTY5YzY3Mjk3YmI4NGMwYjQ1ZWZiNzJhNTQ3YWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/3e6564f8f904d329a4d8aea592b1e16e219c4d7b","sha":"3e6564f8f904d329a4d8aea592b1e16e219c4d7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/3e6564f8f904d329a4d8aea592b1e16e219c4d7b"}],"sha":"146c569045d969c67297bb84c0b45efb72a547ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/146c569045d969c67297bb84c0b45efb72a547ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51116673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arbirali","id":51116673,"login":"arbirali","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTE2Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/3e6564f8f904d329a4d8aea592b1e16e219c4d7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T06:57:51Z","email":"rahat.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Rahat Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T06:57:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(admin): correct the paginated count and use the Paragon pager (#29)\n\n* fix(admin): correct the paginated count and use the Paragon pager\n\nThe Biodata Edit Requests and Signup Approvals lists read the total as\n`data.count`, but these endpoints nest it as `data.pagination.count`. The\ntotal fell back to the number of rows in hand, so a 5-row page of 7 records\nreported \"5 requests\", \"Showing 1-5 of 5\" and a single page - the records on\npage 2 were unreachable.\n\nBoth now use the shared `getPaginatedCount`, which reads either envelope.\n\nThe shared PaginationFooter also swaps its hand-rolled prev/next buttons for\nParagon''s `Pagination`, matching the Users table: numbered pages, prev/next\nand ellipsis. Its callers pass the same props as before.\n\n* chore: ignore the generated env.config.js","tree":{"sha":"a63b7c8f4fba7ee3843e0bf6c7786690dfc101ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/trees/a63b7c8f4fba7ee3843e0bf6c7786690dfc101ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/commits/3e6564f8f904d329a4d8aea592b1e16e219c4d7b","verification":{"payload":"tree a63b7c8f4fba7ee3843e0bf6c7786690dfc101ac\nparent af513478b0cb45466ac9f8f1910d1de3b7a1e6cf\nauthor Rahat Ali <rahat.ali@arbisoft.com> 1789714671 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789714671 +0500\n\nfix(admin): correct the paginated count and use the Paragon pager (#29)\n\n* fix(admin): correct the paginated count and use the Paragon pager\n\nThe Biodata Edit Requests and Signup Approvals lists read the total as\n`data.count`, but these endpoints nest it as `data.pagination.count`. The\ntotal fell back to the number of rows in hand, so a 5-row page of 7 records\nreported \"5 requests\", \"Showing 1-5 of 5\" and a single page - the records on\npage 2 were unreachable.\n\nBoth now use the shared `getPaginatedCount`, which reads either envelope.\n\nThe shared PaginationFooter also swaps its hand-rolled prev/next buttons for\nParagon''s `Pagination`, matching the Users table: numbered pages, prev/next\nand ellipsis. Its callers pass the same props as before.\n\n* chore: ignore the generated env.config.js","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrODvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZAEQAAEhcAmU1ze7juy97baqXBMv\nPv96rr/YjfNb6zi8BMutI5LZHjJZ/u4H8S6G+9JQ3oyKwb7y8d9Y/z3JKywU8pOq\nDaKRFOc++9Ita03DtEfhPa9KqB1Yh0p4MYC5gauINWUEq3/cbxrxnuAqZwzF03hj\nvgz4Zu1W94OWqUfJjtJcv6zA1SNCfEW8aaOfIdM88jiuYhEr5FdQq/zQJ3+ZbGuI\nfnLCPQM6RFTbk4LVVB6Fukg4yiasgGDfdZB1OLUPqtK2HEL9fHICi17DK0VWeNBt\nFH8QFiQjgCSkqiwa6BtURL7838xYtqyjfpQHhGF+zpypCq1Yg+hOOtOuqBMErnqT\ni3Wo+Zu3bhzYxEqT7YOMnJCXIdOLUI1ViJy3lZo0cVXuIKmYOH5jLi2Ulg0L1q1Y\nQMCnh2pHBm/ydiDCtGPo4sUJZH2OerCOxo4enQqml1ktc3jgC05MNiqxGzukukua\nAoQe3kM0X2N381yW2zyAd/k/H2kIpgzl10VNLdBYGq3Rs42U/i/MRS1dU6+r8Kue\n/TnDIG57fzR6gvDdQtZJBK2SgAXzej9e2MwYN22kF4pDoTUUajIfSV/4hV8Jnctp\n2eBV0+k8YbjmxwDx8Q56dlkwmirPRLAubIWqTNgn9qk5sLZEZOX6OaADrDSORzpf\nPbjpNZ97cdrNhyzKzYtw\n=DMGU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T06:57:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/3e6564f8f904d329a4d8aea592b1e16e219c4d7b","node_id":"C_kwDOSir9AdoAKDNlNjU2NGY4ZjkwNGQzMjlhNGQ4YWVhNTkyYjFlMTZlMjE5YzRkN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/af513478b0cb45466ac9f8f1910d1de3b7a1e6cf","sha":"af513478b0cb45466ac9f8f1910d1de3b7a1e6cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/af513478b0cb45466ac9f8f1910d1de3b7a1e6cf"}],"sha":"3e6564f8f904d329a4d8aea592b1e16e219c4d7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/3e6564f8f904d329a4d8aea592b1e16e219c4d7b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51116673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arbirali","id":51116673,"login":"arbirali","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTE2Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/af513478b0cb45466ac9f8f1910d1de3b7a1e6cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T06:52:22Z","email":"rahat.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Rahat Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T06:52:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(users): make the Edit action a link to the profile MFE (#30)\n\nEdit was a button that fetched the user''s detail and then called\nwindow.open, so the profile URL could not be copied, middle-clicked or\nopened in a new tab from the context menu.\n\nIt is now a Paragon `Hyperlink` (IconButton renders a <button> only) wearing\nthe icon-button classes, and the kebab menu''s Edit User item takes an\noptional `editHref` and renders as a link too. Both fall back to the click\nhandler when no profile URL is configured.\n\nThe detail request is gone: the detail endpoint returns the same profile id\nthe listing already provides, so the URL is built from the row.","tree":{"sha":"634f89c852dc5a9e78f588e20290b1483182ecaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/trees/634f89c852dc5a9e78f588e20290b1483182ecaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/commits/af513478b0cb45466ac9f8f1910d1de3b7a1e6cf","verification":{"payload":"tree 634f89c852dc5a9e78f588e20290b1483182ecaf\nparent 1235c2b6a64432ebb4fc592eae14e9b49c5ff6cb\nauthor Rahat Ali <rahat.ali@arbisoft.com> 1789714342 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789714342 +0500\n\nfeat(users): make the Edit action a link to the profile MFE (#30)\n\nEdit was a button that fetched the user''s detail and then called\nwindow.open, so the profile URL could not be copied, middle-clicked or\nopened in a new tab from the context menu.\n\nIt is now a Paragon `Hyperlink` (IconButton renders a <button> only) wearing\nthe icon-button classes, and the kebab menu''s Edit User item takes an\noptional `editHref` and renders as a link too. Both fall back to the click\nhandler when no profile URL is configured.\n\nThe detail request is gone: the detail endpoint returns the same profile id\nthe listing already provides, so the URL is built from the row.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrN+mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX94QAETCcUQHyAxzgXLCixf4inRv\nrsF1X6M+gw/SbwzgYCi2AF+oaImkKnWrkrXcGPNcYFCZFu5ZNVUNzO3iju4jyTqt\nPUCNIidvmHLfeR0DU61LvRTYMf3N0yCTy6guGUG6Vn38EFNGk+3G/Lwz067deZHu\n4AqA4Ee0LnQ+vdOnui1Ia5vXsfKSXxOB/isZIX5eyPn/B0ZS7vQO0JWAajElpKH+\nmcNcC1tVD3VaiU4nyQbFcaN9cvxSA+TJnF+CfQNpHICsuNPWh/+gYUASGtTMymZC\ngopPhiF96N2FrDCvrxB2Bpw6Hkx6CfbglIrg95GpFyWfj8TPgaX5L5ARs2F99ipF\nD1lEMpUD1Lq+cZBfTwyd1O4xmWH4jHLelE7cm8qbfDXjgVYrPYuDHDgI2j7BTbdw\n6r+GBQwm8xTvnVoga/TaBfJdZOmExggvVL3NWav6Yuz+erWVi0v5O+/FPyzzsb1/\nh0tZQwghL14pZgfgm3UjtM8tWSAacO2f2v8YLj367/B96yyclkzd6eCAr91LtYFJ\n33oCOIAWw7IoUkwzlFxMHoAqUq2qma8WqjweMJKWoPPIWSs+/p98xg8DpDIQxTwc\nlDwCpDZe4RsqbeUhINmzPcgNAB6u5PANx55P7Ieb9wjSHAAJGlmuMPGVTsRQAKu6\nZROsTjbA9fCVPfVaF+xz\n=8w2U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T06:52:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/af513478b0cb45466ac9f8f1910d1de3b7a1e6cf","node_id":"C_kwDOSir9AdoAKGFmNTEzNDc4YjBjYjQ1NDY2YWM5ZjhmMTkxMGQxZGUzYjdhMWU2Y2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/1235c2b6a64432ebb4fc592eae14e9b49c5ff6cb","sha":"1235c2b6a64432ebb4fc592eae14e9b49c5ff6cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/1235c2b6a64432ebb4fc592eae14e9b49c5ff6cb"}],"sha":"af513478b0cb45466ac9f8f1910d1de3b7a1e6cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/af513478b0cb45466ac9f8f1910d1de3b7a1e6cf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51116673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arbirali","id":51116673,"login":"arbirali","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTE2Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/1235c2b6a64432ebb4fc592eae14e9b49c5ff6cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T06:52:06Z","email":"rahat.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Rahat Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T06:52:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(users): rebuild the view user modal on Paragon ModalDialog (#31)\n\nThe close icon in the modal header did nothing. The modal was a hand-rolled\nfixed overlay, so the header sat in the page''s own stacking context.\n\nIt now uses `ModalDialog`, and both close controls are\n`ModalDialog.CloseButton`, which closes through the modal''s context rather\nthan a passed handler. That also brings a portal, backdrop, Esc-to-close,\nfocus trapping and the mobile fullscreen treatment. The header, body and\nfooter keep their existing markup and styling.","tree":{"sha":"a21a1ece0ff37466be86a711b5d594e582e749c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/trees/a21a1ece0ff37466be86a711b5d594e582e749c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/commits/1235c2b6a64432ebb4fc592eae14e9b49c5ff6cb","verification":{"payload":"tree a21a1ece0ff37466be86a711b5d594e582e749c1\nparent 8b5f799f2777264472ab600a09812e9bb8039351\nauthor Rahat Ali <rahat.ali@arbisoft.com> 1789714326 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789714326 +0500\n\nfix(users): rebuild the view user modal on Paragon ModalDialog (#31)\n\nThe close icon in the modal header did nothing. The modal was a hand-rolled\nfixed overlay, so the header sat in the page''s own stacking context.\n\nIt now uses `ModalDialog`, and both close controls are\n`ModalDialog.CloseButton`, which closes through the modal''s context rather\nthan a passed handler. That also brings a portal, backdrop, Esc-to-close,\nfocus trapping and the mobile fullscreen treatment. The header, body and\nfooter keep their existing markup and styling.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrN+WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD3EQAKUiACLs+7hhC3fUbU1wlidB\nxWqiRnkWJld/QHq2WCLuFC3hBeBUyvAi7uXlyFXF/YA5TsNCY3qNidKiMuisn+bm\nqJzcKMAVYtEO/TqB9Sq/XCuuk1PLw51KJJKG94lBiFZ8gqSAI8BVk8BVElldnQk8\n2ZPtufCtAizltXJDVSzWlmFJlga6pJQtkUFbo5k7eezQwQauYJvpsP+k9xnneiSF\nLNPsFM6IomX0yf7YdFTkKtkRTcKkHpJq+SG1Q89h0wvUgTbTgVnMMqCaZll82ucH\nv