ived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/77c6289fef054fa1bb02396138a08d4eb017d90d","node_id":"C_kwDOSir9AdoAKDc3YzYyODlmZWYwNTRmYTFiYjAyMzk2MTM4YTA4ZDRlYjAxN2Q5MGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/7e7e35d6a0b5c66b0c77c8328d5e001b92a97bc7","sha":"7e7e35d6a0b5c66b0c77c8328d5e001b92a97bc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/7e7e35d6a0b5c66b0c77c8328d5e001b92a97bc7"}],"sha":"77c6289fef054fa1bb02396138a08d4eb017d90d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/77c6289fef054fa1bb02396138a08d4eb017d90d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51116673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arbirali","id":51116673,"login":"arbirali","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTE2Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/7e7e35d6a0b5c66b0c77c8328d5e001b92a97bc7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T16:28:41Z","email":"rahat.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Rahat Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T16:28:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Rahat/admin console paragon pass (#26)\n\n* refactor: move audit log fetching to TanStack Query hooks\n\nAdds src/shared/auditLogApiHooks.js following the existing\nadmin-console data/apiHooks convention: a query-key factory,\nretryExceptClientErrors, and placeholderData carrying the previous page\nthrough, shared by useAuditLogs (table) and useRecordHistory\n(per-record modal).\n\nBoth call sites in AuditLogTable drop their useEffect, cancellation\nflag and four pieces of local state. The derived locals keep the names\nthe JSX already used, so nothing about rendering changes.\n\nThe hooks set staleTime: 0 to opt out of the app-wide one hour\nstaleTime: an audit trail must re-fetch rather than be served from a\nwarm cache, which is what the previous useEffect did on every\nparameter change.\n\nauditLogApi.js is unchanged. AuditLogTable.test.jsx now wraps the\ncomponent in a QueryClientProvider, matching UsersPage.test.jsx.\n\n* feat(users): rebuild the users listing on Paragon DataTable\n\nThe page rendered its own `<table>` and pagination footer. Swapped both\nfor Paragon''s `DataTable` and `Pagination`, keeping every column, the row\nactions, the search and status filters and the loading, empty and error\nstates, and without touching the users API.\n\nThree defects surfaced on the way and are fixed here:\n\n- The total came back as the page length, so the count read \"20\" for 78\n  users and the pager never appeared. These endpoints use edx''s\n  `NamespacedPageNumberPagination`, which nests the total under\n  `pagination.count` rather than putting it at the top level. Added a\n  shared `getPaginatedCount` helper and read the count through it.\n- Selecting page 2 snapped straight back to page 1. The debounced search\n  input re-armed its timer on every parent render, because the effect\n  depended on the `onChange` identity, and then emitted an empty search\n  that reset the page. The effect is now keyed on the typed value alone\n  and the callback is held in a ref.\n- The rows-per-page select showed 5 while fetching 25, because the\n  default page size was missing from the options list.\n\n* refactor(admin): move the remaining chrome onto Paragon and fix the dark theme\n\nHand-rolled controls and hard-coded light colours had spread across the\nadmin console. This replaces them with Paragon components and puts the\nsurfaces back on theme tokens.\n\nParagon components:\n\n- The row action menu was a bespoke dropdown positioned by hand. It is\n  now `Dropdown` + `Dropdown.Toggle as={IconButton}` + `Dropdown.Item`,\n  which also fixes it rendering as bare text in the dark theme: the menu\n  tokens Paragon''s own `Menu` needs are not in the runtime theme, while\n  `.dropdown-menu` is. The menu was clipped because Paragon''s DataTable\n  cells carry `overflow: hidden` for their ellipsis, so the actions\n  column now has a `cellClassName` that opts out of it.\n- The eye and pencil row buttons use Paragon''s `Visibility` and `Edit`\n  icons instead of FontAwesome.\n- The audit log filter row was four raw inputs with their own borders and\n  focus rings; it is now `Form.Control`, with the search magnifier as a\n  real `leadingElement` rather than an absolutely positioned overlay, and\n  the record-filter notice is an `Alert variant=\"info\"`.\n- The list / audit log toggle on the three admin pages is a `ButtonGroup`\n  matching the program tabs, replacing a local nav-tabs override.\n\nDark theme:\n\n- Status pills were built on a fixed `#EDFAF1` tint while their text\n  token flips light, leaving the label at 1.2:1 on a near-white chip.\n- The signup approvals card and the user modals were literal `#fff`, so\n  they stayed white under light-on-dark type - the modal''s name and field\n  values measured 1.06:1.\n- Where a token could carry the surface it now does; where the palette\n  has no dark-aware raised surface, the tints are restated as translucent\n  ink, following the treatment already used by the nav context bar.\n\n* fix(admin): wrap the signup approvals Paragon import across lines","tree":{"sha":"9472ee40a281a87808adcf1cb3bf983cf6628efc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/trees/9472ee40a281a87808adcf1cb3bf983cf6628efc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/commits/7e7e35d6a0b5c66b0c77c8328d5e001b92a97bc7","verification":{"payload":"tree 9472ee40a281a87808adcf1cb3bf983cf6628efc\nparent dbf14a94ad0de30517c356db5b8e929e09e85c81\nauthor Rahat Ali <rahat.ali@arbisoft.com> 1789403321 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789403321 +0500\n\nRahat/admin console paragon pass (#26)\n\n* refactor: move audit log fetching to TanStack Query hooks\n\nAdds src/shared/auditLogApiHooks.js following the existing\nadmin-console data/apiHooks convention: a query-key factory,\nretryExceptClientErrors, and placeholderData carrying the previous page\nthrough, shared by useAuditLogs (table) and useRecordHistory\n(per-record modal).\n\nBoth call sites in AuditLogTable drop their useEffect, cancellation\nflag and four pieces of local state. The derived locals keep the names\nthe JSX already used, so nothing about rendering changes.\n\nThe hooks set staleTime: 0 to opt out of the app-wide one hour\nstaleTime: an audit trail must re-fetch rather than be served from a\nwarm cache, which is what the previous useEffect did on every\nparameter change.\n\nauditLogApi.js is unchanged. AuditLogTable.test.jsx now wraps the\ncomponent in a QueryClientProvider, matching UsersPage.test.jsx.\n\n* feat(users): rebuild the users listing on Paragon DataTable\n\nThe page rendered its own `<table>` and pagination footer. Swapped both\nfor Paragon''s `DataTable` and `Pagination`, keeping every column, the row\nactions, the search and status filters and the loading, empty and error\nstates, and without touching the users API.\n\nThree defects surfaced on the way and are fixed here:\n\n- The total came back as the page length, so the count read \"20\" for 78\n  users and the pager never appeared. These endpoints use edx''s\n  `NamespacedPageNumberPagination`, which nests the total under\n  `pagination.count` rather than putting it at the top level. Added a\n  shared `getPaginatedCount` helper and read the count through it.\n- Selecting page 2 snapped straight back to page 1. The debounced search\n  input re-armed its timer on every parent render, because the effect\n  depended on the `onChange` identity, and then emitted an empty search\n  that reset the page. The effect is now keyed on the typed value alone\n  and the callback is held in a ref.\n- The rows-per-page select showed 5 while fetching 25, because the\n  default page size was missing from the options list.\n\n* refactor(admin): move the remaining chrome onto Paragon and fix the dark theme\n\nHand-rolled controls and hard-coded light colours had spread across the\nadmin console. This replaces them with Paragon components and puts the\nsurfaces back on theme tokens.\n\nParagon components:\n\n- The row action menu was a bespoke dropdown positioned by hand. It is\n  now `Dropdown` + `Dropdown.Toggle as={IconButton}` + `Dropdown.Item`,\n  which also fixes it rendering as bare text in the dark theme: the menu\n  tokens Paragon''s own `Menu` needs are not in the runtime theme, while\n  `.dropdown-menu` is. The menu was clipped because Paragon''s DataTable\n  cells carry `overflow: hidden` for their ellipsis, so the actions\n  column now has a `cellClassName` that opts out of it.\n- The eye and pencil row buttons use Paragon''s `Visibility` and `Edit`\n  icons instead of FontAwesome.\n- The audit log filter row was four raw inputs with their own borders and\n  focus rings; it is now `Form.Control`, with the search magnifier as a\n  real `leadingElement` rather than an absolutely positioned overlay, and\n  the record-filter notice is an `Alert variant=\"info\"`.\n- The list / audit log toggle on the three admin pages is a `ButtonGroup`\n  matching the program tabs, replacing a local nav-tabs override.\n\nDark theme:\n\n- Status pills were built on a fixed `#EDFAF1` tint while their text\n  token flips light, leaving the label at 1.2:1 on a near-white chip.\n- The signup approvals card and the user modals were literal `#fff`, so\n  they stayed white under light-on-dark type - the modal''s name and field\n  values measured 1.06:1.\n- Where a token could carry the surface it now does; where the palette\n  has no dark-aware raised surface, the tints are restated as translucent\n  ink, following the treatment already used by the nav context bar.\n\n* fix(admin): wrap the signup approvals Paragon import across lines","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqCC5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3n4QAF4ucW6LyhZ2lUhLHWWHh5EQ\ni6sRbdaXUfO+SkGiJP5wPjnRxvqE95GKGP0Ap1KUBlkwjYI6t6X/CBJrL2IZ1Sjz\nq+RLp8ZFzOfY4RKB3GXgB9+zgEKR93JCFdop3C93mhQ2K6gc4WTkh7kFldx73eLf\n9ysS9tLMTsgje+GgCIyiQrojkkw8ilwnkeDk0clBLklGpOsGoChXXYNHf4KDd6QZ\nMTjykctDYIruMygMrG0qQqUXx72CYVSZ7vSIaY15O2mvZtphGC/AQUqjYlS8QpH/\nfFBOSHUfmM6ov5Kt28BTvUtkIRKW9nRnYXvrR/NnmJDsq451z4CVIE9L5UCI3EK6\nV12pdTzncylSiVlY9zo3x/gX7880y6joo1WuniKlJXdm2t1FJ7uoE1QSWEsVUuVU\n+wdvIPt6WBtwVOCB2JO+JH2b3ps0W0Tz70+TWrm1ZZwfTRhaEILtPgqqcP5WVc5Z\nXuTnYcCkBmhIKy7nfU+9QSBPtwqAwLwNb+FnRDf+ApAhSsgsQ9XQIHB6wK4JaJpB\n42lh0W7JzXYncepJhs2BSzoFIj4bsLNWEbbtN5vQuliw4kq6V8ovjV46zRhbtkT2\nmPo7s/s4Iqg6eRXt+EO32uGqLF+y0IswgStbYddqo5hfMKYWDHak89KZot2X4E1O\nWpJ/buqhgGRijTeloCcT\n=UhpW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T16:28:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","fo