-logs): fix ESLint errors in AuditLogTable and admin pages\n\n* refactor(audit-logs): replace native button with Paragon Button in ViewUserModal\n\n* refactor(audit-logs): replace all remaining native buttons with Paragon Button","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnockCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhowQAALdqrdpMghAwjyDVeMdUc8U\nWMDn6DU/Gad97PahX6y8g4d9IMLhjeHwhOFs9h7fUwsK+iBFx3t2MPzMWPR5httw\n8DkQh8hqF8BhrzkBM4t7Pqa0gRyufSqPH7HYUwCJvHv+s0YYnnuwNpjR9kWSatmG\nMnJxQU2tGiV73+0AJ50jFhbuqoJE0NpJ/l4dczszqdtn137IPSLO6N95IqRdjHwI\n0zbIJQAHdlXJuc3qlwI0LGhryYbAeUGO5EyhKv6n9X6tHxxFH0TZnRCPliJ775Xb\nuo7bEikSiDSa3fIlJ+4LPpOcZrNZaF405a9IhTH/n+kY0kIIGmOhceTZ9yrO0x1i\nU8ZHcb7xThNT6cwZ85F0hb+hL0V6BFhOivKxJ8A2vZaCRqumhUpY22PbYW6m0JAN\ngbr+yL2hGdke4hS80yxKNNJJUuBiWW9r7Alcdcq3CG/aS2/fYPiSa2nr0AakZGS+\nrSWcK3EubxrQVZeqThqvDkddCp0ioTfUMH2g0nfeN7LIAbTFnb5I5CRoU6fXldqT\nYBXfFxzAc8wPgluX9HbMLtADcxqNks3uF8qszWsLscyF93UhbgUpg3pbCWHH+hFe\n4sbt9lxXzOs/ZPGN7io8zEoy4fNw6WEXDnhKwYOZvCVnofOckfkOW5UnFPieiNrK\nnHv46y8UKdEOxWSrYJMk\n=GE9x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T09:43:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/b85d1fac847c9b2872667e8246b91dc7f8cba749","node_id":"C_kwDOSir9AdoAKGI4NWQxZmFjODQ3YzliMjg3MjY2N2U4MjQ2YjkxZGM3ZjhjYmE3NDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/a98857acff9cb744c45b1d6ee91e2fb424d3419b","sha":"a98857acff9cb744c45b1d6ee91e2fb424d3419b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/a98857acff9cb744c45b1d6ee91e2fb424d3419b"}],"sha":"b85d1fac847c9b2872667e8246b91dc7f8cba749","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/b85d1fac847c9b2872667e8246b91dc7f8cba749"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51116673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arbirali","id":51116673,"login":"arbirali","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTE2Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/a98857acff9cb744c45b1d6ee91e2fb424d3419b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T08:56:25Z","email":"rahat.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Rahat Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T08:56:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Sidebar responsiveness (#22)\n\n* feat: Sidebar responsiveness\n\n* fix(admin-console): make the mobile nav readable in dark mode\n\nThe context bar''s trigger is painted with `--pgn-color-white`, which the\ndark theme resolves to the body background, and its labels use numbered\n`gray-*` steps the theme leaves at their light values - so the bar sat\ninvisible on the dark page with dark ink on it. Restate the surface, the\nsecondary ink and the pending-count badge under\n`[data-paragon-theme-variant=\"dark\"]`, and move the page label onto\n`text-base`, which the theme does override.\n\nThe nav-link styles shared by the sheet and the desktop rail get the same\ntreatment, so the navigation is legible wherever it renders.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018uXgShu5TagEcfNBGFevJh\n\n* fix(admin-console): keep the sticky nav bar opaque under the dark theme\n\n`--pgn-color-theme-bg-gray` is defined only in the light theme, so under\ndark the `var()` has nothing to resolve to and the whole declaration is\ndropped - leaving the context bar transparent and the page content\nscrolling straight through it. Both the console shell and the sticky bar\nnow fall back to `--pgn-color-body-bg`, which is the surface the page was\nalready showing, so the two stay on the same colour in either theme.\n\n\n* fix: UI fixes\n\n* test(admin-console): cover the responsive navigation\n\nAdds coverage for the pieces the responsive pass introduced and for the\ntwo seams where it met the newer base:\n\n- `useNavSheetVisibility`: the keep-mounted close window, the reduced\n  motion shortcut, a reopen cancelling a pending close, closing when the\n  viewport crosses the breakpoint, and listener/timer cleanup.\n- `AdminNavLinks`: a parametrised check that every id in `NAV_SECTIONS`\n  resolves to a label and every section to a title, so a nav item added\n  without a message fails here rather than throwing at render time in\n  both the rail and the sheet. Plus grouping, badges, the sheet-only\n  active indicator and the navigate callback.\n- `useAdminNavigation`: role and capability filtering against the real\n  nav config, badge rollup, and active-route resolution.\n- `AdminNavContextBar`: the section/page trail and its fallback, the\n  rolled-up count in the badge and the accessible name, and opening and\n  dismissing the sheet.\n- `AdminConsolePage`: both navigations stay mounted, so the breakpoint\n  swap remains a CSS concern and a resize cannot remount the nav.\n- Sessions Instructor Reports: the CSV button keeps both its small size\n  and its Program/Instructor gating.\n\nStylesheets are mapped through `identity-obj-proxy` under Jest, so the\ndark-theme and sticky-background rules are not covered here.\n\n* fix(responsive): Fix responsive issues (#24)","tree":{"sha":"17fedc8c27f0f13e59154c368d10d1fff460981e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/trees/17fedc8c27f0f13e59154c368d10d1fff460981e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/commits/a98857acff9cb744c45b1d6ee91e2fb424d3419b","verification":{"payload":"tree 17fedc8c27f0f13e59154c368d10d1fff460981e\nparent 22301cf1ac4fe0bf641980774619f2a8f0d93c03\nauthor Rahat Ali <rahat.ali@arbisoft.com> 1788771385 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788771385 +0500\n\nfeat: Sidebar responsiveness (#22)\n\n* feat: Sidebar responsiveness\n\n* fix(admin-console): make the mobile nav readable in dark mode\n\nThe context bar''s trigger is painted with `--pgn-color-white`, which the\ndark theme resolves to the body background, and its labels use numbered\n`gray-*` steps the theme leaves at their light values - so the bar sat\ninvisible on the dark page with dark ink on it. Restate the surface, the\nsecondary ink and the pending-count badge under\n`[data-paragon-theme-variant=\"dark\"]`, and move the page label onto\n`text-base`, which the theme does override.\n\nThe nav-link styles shared by the sheet and the desktop rail get the same\ntreatment, so the navigation is legible wherever it renders.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018uXgShu5TagEcfNBGFevJh\n\n* fix(admin-console): keep the sticky nav bar opaque under the dark theme\n\n`--pgn-color-theme-bg-gray` is defined only in the light theme, so under\ndark the `var()` has nothing to resolve to and the whole declaration is\ndropped - leaving the context bar transparent and the page content\nscrolling straight through it. Both the console shell and the sticky bar\nnow fall back to `--pgn-color-body-bg`, which is the surface the page was\nalready showing, so the two stay on the same colour in either theme.\n\n\n* fix: UI fixes\n\n* test(admin-console): cover the responsive navigation\n\nAdds coverage for the pieces the responsive pass introduced and for the\ntwo seams where it met the newer base:\n\n- `useNavSheetVisibility`: the keep-mounted close window, the reduced\n  motion shortcut, a reopen cancelling a pending close, closing when the\n  viewport crosses the breakpoint, and listener/timer cleanup.\n- `AdminNavLinks`: a parametrised check that every id in `NAV_SECTIONS`\n  resolves to a label and every section to a title, so a nav item added\n  without a message fails here rather than throwing at render time in\n  both the rail and the sheet. Plus grouping, badges, the sheet-only\n  active indicator and the navigate callback.\n- `useAdminNavigation`: role and capability filtering against the real\n  nav config, badge rollup, and active-route resolution.\n- `AdminNavContextBar`: the section/page trail and its fallback, the\n  rolled-up count in the badge and the accessible name, and opening and\n  dismissing the sheet.\n- `AdminConsolePage`: both navigations stay mounted, so the breakpoint\n  swap remains a CSS concern and a resize cannot remount the nav.\n- Sessions Instructor Reports: the CSV button keeps both its small size\n  and its Program/Instructor gating.\n\nStylesheets are mapped through `identity-obj-proxy` under Jest, so the\ndark-theme and sticky-background rules are not covered here.\n\n* fix(responsive): Fix responsive issues (#24)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnnw5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJtgQABxlGsL2Gp5/QWZLsEZC93A4\noA5gIFo7GHQMQ5OYgj9Vvsy5Kdj4GjIdwhEawCpvO0aS5a+vlBCzjcvEGfX+SHmF\nlPVc5tweTgPEfKlbqyzNQ+JpL9y0L5w0dDGds4ub/fra38IzzuLiKEVA6Cob+rrk\n3+rp+ldlJxnzNLty3IMCpUxC3k+lPVT+QNiKu6VfzQJ3vj1XaBkwpqv6ZWFh6Ndw\nR1jMcc04fDE+3QbxbhYBlXxGuFavB5mI9CBF8PxKpVOrbEZGA3x+c/UUiP01zoPc\nMOF4mSvYWyjqijiBJjCZYn5e7ge4aYbXIolJ2RIjIORY3O+UHBFKHhP9WFHYZ47t\nADv2hVUvh8cMzpXny0Bo5rOs6/ZUcrsSq7BIxYwfNsFOm4RsLhg+2mVMyF52Lq8O\n17vIFNM4WtkAHF9G2FPeJL+OBPdY/6JYW4d/kPxR/snRfQlt9k6khllO3Rbj/wK8\nfc5dIOSlXFmHVO5IboMrGSxQjLk+QPlY80BXT+U8Zl6moKKN72TO3q3SQ9xDsO22\n4cri0ZiGiABLQH6qU2dQCBx52E/rYcK3CFHcxSY6hvMHDCNdrA8G/8Dq1DaGeGpr\n2DqzCwuHpRZZHMcyid0XgVeYhbZmwiOyU5cwzonUaFjlmQ5pd6UsNLBT0Dhn5svb\neZRrNDdFtuhuM/J3pUR/\n=pFBc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T08:56:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/a98857acff9cb744c45b1d6ee91e2fb424d3419b","node_id":"C_kwDOSir9AdoAKGE5ODg1N2FjZmY5Y2I3NDRjNDViMWQ2ZWU5MWUyZmI0MjRkMzQxOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/22301cf1ac4fe0bf641980774619f2a8f0d93c03","sha":"22301cf1ac4fe0bf641980774619f2a8f0d93c03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/22301cf1ac4fe0bf641980774619f2a8f0d93c03"}],"sha":"a98857acff9cb744c45b1d6ee91e2fb424d3419b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/a98857acff9cb744c45b1d6ee91e2fb424d3419b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51116673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arbirali","id":51116673,"login":"arbirali","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTE2Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/22301cf1ac4fe0bf641980774619f2a8f0d93c03/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T06:11:36Z","email":"rahat.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Rahat Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T06:11:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(reports): send the applied date range to the details sheets (#21)\n\n* fix(reports): send the applied date range to the details sheets\n\nBoth report tabs fetched their details sheet with only `program` + the person''s\nid, so after applying a Start/End Date filter the sheet listed the whole\nhistory while the table behind it showed the filtered rows.\n\n- `getInstructorSessionDetails` / `getAttendanceDetails` now take\n  `startDate`/`endDate` and send them as the `from`/`to` params the listings\n  and the CSV exports already use, omitting either when it is empty.\n- `useInstructorSessionDetails` / `useAttendanceDetails` carry the dates in\n  their query keys, so the sheet refetches per range instead of serving a\n  cached unfiltered payload.\n- The pages hand `appliedFilters.startDate/endDate` down through\n  `ReportDataTable` to the sheets, so a draft filter the user has not applied\n  is never sent, and Clear all filters drops the params again.\n\nNeeds the matching backend change in tutor-contrib-fbr\n(`rahat/report-detail-date-filters`); until that lands the extra params are\nsimply ignored.\n\nTests: 6 new files / 20 cases across both tabs — request params for no dates,\nboth bounds, start-only and end-only; the mapped detail payload; the\nclick-through from a row to the detail request; and applied-vs-draft plus\nclearing. Full suite: 12 suites, 102 tests passing.\n\n* fix: Admin dashboard UI fixes","tree":{"sha":"492e8ee55561e35ebca62cdf8ce7ad5f85f97da6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/trees/492e8ee55561e35ebca62cdf8ce7ad5f85f97da6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/commits/22301cf1ac4fe0bf641980774619f2a8f0d93c03","verification":{"payload":"tree 492e8ee55561e35ebca62cdf8ce7ad5f85f97da6\nparent 6a8da8f5f8592a5c23b10a0d46cec22cd4c5589d\nauthor Rahat Ali <rahat.ali@arbisoft.com> 1788329496 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788329496 +0500\n\nfix(reports): send the applied date range to the details sheets (#21)\n\n* fix(reports): send the applied date range to the details sheets\n\nBoth report tabs fetched their details sheet with only `program` + the person''s\nid, so after applying a Start/End Date filter the sheet listed the whole\nhistory while the table behind it showed the filtered rows.\n\n- `getInstructorSessionDetails` / `getAttendanceDetails` now take\n  `startDate`/`endDate` and send them as the `from`/`to` params the listings\n  and the CSV exports already use, omitting either when it is empty.\n- `useInstructorSessionDetails` / `useAttendanceDetails` carry the dates in\n  their query keys, so the sheet refetches per range instead of serving a\n  cached unfiltered payload.\n- The pages hand `appliedFilters.startDate/endDate` down through\n  `ReportDataTable` to the sheets, so a draft filter the user has not applied\n  is never sent, and Clear all filters drops the params again.\n\nNeeds the matching backend change in tutor-contrib-fbr\n(`rahat/report-detail-date-filters`); until that lands the extra params are\nsimply ignored.\n\nTests: 6 new files / 20 cases across both tabs — request params for no dates,\nboth bounds, start-only and end-only; the mapped detail payload; the\nclick-through from a row to the detail request; and applied-vs-draft plus\nclearing. Full suite: 12 suites, 102 tests passing.\n\n* fix: Admin dashboard UI fixes","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql74YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOM0QAHw/xhVVSkTlTua6ZIgEgW1c\nyYEjc6XkGkonAGJm/9SPhccCWIuslvHdAEQjTYdDmKyuVTBD0Lc0Gt9Vsf3x/mPz\n+p4smUtwUi5wLrN4F5DDk2CharXDRuEANz/6OUhaHq+6abOm23YqtREanQRdnbDG\nHgrdW4zfQCShtq078NVfzG38hvX9HL5hPLs7Bhjt3UZyaVSo2fz07jhsUztqDmRO\nj/PTfllRN1ng0DuIEFQWBT7CbLrJ/uRavtj2fUucU092JEdvZlmBhx9HjzkmjtxS\nU3ns4xjFvLCJeMMBAGWig5p6LnV89siXffo4843TgSK3rfWElM3709iLc9zsKf2d\n7ucenDfKXRMvQAF9FDlyEr41QvlloACLAuO1VKfRKvlrdUJS5QORUN/uA/J+aK9d\nWD2o2RIsg49azUQkCrrIzEQj3nVAxwE1A8VBx2FtVE3NINdo8d9IrnOT/SpSpKHn\n0XdhAvwcf3CRRgRJuMidkdkiYHJdbmPUJcndSHBINPk2sbTHOCsYcQ3KYQ2n6QoX\n73mYqFiasMCL+aX7MoZiC/xfW5HiiebYsg4fLjZh1Ay9R8bezcatNTWxAT8fKtv8\nI1nRQppU19+nRuJnoz8PKf6NgFyqp5lS4BDBgzHcIWoCU86OdZkLL87sXhDBk7Ty\n5KI3Wy9i0jG1bjzdR7ne\n=XBEL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T06:11:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/22301cf1ac4fe0bf641980774619f2a8f0d93c03","node_id":"C_kwDOSir9AdoAKDIyMzAxY2YxYWM0ZmUwYmY2NDE5ODA3NzQ2MTlmMmE4ZjBkOTNjMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/6a8da8f5f8592a5c23b10a0d46cec22cd4c5589d","sha":"6a8da8f5f8592a5c23b10a0d46cec22cd4c5589d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/6a8da8f5f8592a5c23b10a0d46cec22cd4c5589d"}],"sha":"22301cf1ac4fe0bf641980774619f2a8f0d93c03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/22301cf1ac4fe0bf641980774619f2a8f0d93c03"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51116673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arbirali","id":51116673,"login":"arbirali","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTE2Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/6a8da8f5f8592a5c23b10a0d46cec22cd4c5589d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T13:22:35Z","email":"rahat.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Rahat Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T13:22:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Program Report trainee roster, progress sheet, and report fixes (#17)\n\n* feat: Program Report trainee roster, progress sheet, and report fixes\n\n- Add expandable Program Report rows showing the program''s trainee\n  roster (name, email, batch), backed by GET /program/overview/.\n- Add a right-side Trainee Progress Sheet showing one trainee''s\n  per-course grade and completion progress, backed by\n  GET /program/trainee-progress/, styled to match CourseScoresSheet''s\n  colored course cards and rounded-pill progress bars.\n- Fix Program and Sessions report date filters to send from/to instead\n  of start_date/end_date, matching what the backend actually reads\n  (previously a silent no-op).\n- Give each Reports sidebar item (Program/Sessions/Attendance) a\n  distinct icon instead of sharing the same chart-line icon.\n\n* feat(reports): drop 6-month date range cap and gate CSV export on Program/Instructor (#18)\n\n* feat(reports): drop 6-month date range cap and gate CSV export on Program/Instructor\n\n* fix(reports): size the Program and Instructor filters explicitly\n\nBoth selects sized themselves to their longest option, so long programme\ntitles and instructor names stretched those filters well past City and\nDate Range. Give Program 350px and Instructor 220px, ellipsize longer\nlabels, and add the row the column gap it was missing. City and the date\nrange keep sizing to their own content.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GRuzbLTDovJZFxhoGnAzxz\n\n* fix: filter row spaces\n\n* feat(reports): download Program Report CSVs from the backend (#20)\n\nReplaces the client-side PDF export with backend-streamed CSVs on the\nexisting report endpoints (?export=csv): the filtered Program table, one\ntrainee''s course progress, and a per-program summary sheet.\n\nAdds Description, Start Date and End Date columns; removes Finalized and\nAvg. Score. Drops @react-pdf/renderer and the pdf/ renderers it backed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4332eec32dbdd0b21e71ade9776b0e705c3ab520","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/trees/4332eec32dbdd0b21e71ade9776b0e705c3ab520"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/commits/6a8da8f5f8592a5c23b10a0d46cec22cd4c5589d","verification":{"payload":"tree 4332eec32dbdd0b21e71ade9776b0e705c3ab520\nparent a24a5e5267711aa98d82cb4d94fd5d93e886db4f\nauthor Rahat Ali <rahat.ali@arbisoft.com> 1788268955 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788268955 +0500\n\nfeat: Program Report trainee roster, progress sheet, and report fixes (#17)\n\n* feat: Program Report trainee roster, progress sheet, and report fixes\n\n- Add expandable Program Report rows showing the program''s trainee\n  roster (name, email, batch), backed by GET /program/overview/.\n- Add a right-side Trainee Progress Sheet showing one trainee''s\n  per-course grade and completion progress, backed by\n  GET /program/trainee-progress/, styled to match CourseScoresSheet''s\n  colored course cards and rounded-pill progress bars.\n- Fix Program and Sessions report date filters to send from/to instead\n  of start_date/end_date, matching what the backend actually reads\n  (previously a silent no-op).\n- Give each Reports sidebar item (Program/Sessions/Attendance) a\n  distinct icon instead of sharing the same chart-line icon.\n\n* feat(reports): drop 6-month date range cap and gate CSV export on Program/Instructor (#18)\n\n* feat(reports): drop 6-month date range cap and gate CSV export on Program/Instructor\n\n* fix(reports): size the Program and Instructor filters explicitly\n\nBoth selects sized themselves to their longest option, so long programme\ntitles and instructor names stretched those filters well past City and\nDate Range. Give Program 350px and Instructor 220px, ellipsize longer\nlabels, and add the row the column gap it was missing. City and the date\nrange keep sizing to their own content.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GRuzbLTDovJZFxhoGnAzxz\n\n* fix: filter row spaces\n\n* feat(reports): download Program Report CSVs from the backend (#20)\n\nReplaces the client-side PDF export with backend-streamed CSVs on the\nexisting report endpoints (?export=csv): the filtered Program table, one\ntrainee''s course progress, and a per-program summary sheet.\n\nAdds Description, Start Date and End Date columns; removes Finalized and\nAvg. Score. Drops @react-pdf/renderer and the pdf/ renderers it backed.\n\n----