blic"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/e3cf59a9b8ddcc294f26f33faf59c699f14ad202/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T06:24:31Z","email":"rahat.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Rahat Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T06:24:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(dashboard): wire the Attendance card to its endpoint (#15)\n\nAttendance overview now reads GET /fbr/api/reports/dashboard/attendance/,\nwhich was the last section still backed by fixtures. mockData.js and\nselectors.js had no consumers left afterwards and are deleted, so every\nfigure on the dashboard now comes from the API.\n\nFour numbers the fixtures invented are gone, because the endpoint does not\nhave them: the \"+2.4 pts vs last period\" delta, \"11 below 75% threshold\",\n\"today''s sessions marked 5/6\" and \"trainees tracked\". The footer stat row\nthey occupied goes with them.\n\nWhat replaces them is real. `pending` joins present/absent/leave as a fourth\nstate, in neutral grey: the backend counts it in the denominator, so hiding\nit would inflate the rate — on seeded data that is ~48% against ~72%. A\nprogramme with attendance_rate null reads \"Not started\" rather than 0%,\nsince no sessions yet is not the same as nobody attending, and those sort\nlast. The programme list is a ranked sample the API caps at ten, so it now\nsays \"Showing the 10 lowest of 23 programs\" instead of implying it is the\nwhole portfolio.\n\nNeeds attention loses a level. The course was a heading row above its\nsessions; it is now an eyebrow on each session row — COURSE · DIRECT\nTAXATION, or NO COURSE ATTACHED for a programme-wide ceremony — so a row\nsays what it belongs to without a grouping row repeating it. isGroup, the\nlevel-3 indent and the heading styling all go with it.\n\n\"Unmarked\" becomes \"Pending\" throughout the copy. Status.PENDING is what\nthe platform stores and what the Attendance report already renders, so the\ndashboard was the one screen using its own word.\n\nThe Users role cards deep-link to their own tab: the card carries ?role=,\nand UsersPage derives the active tab from the URL rather than mirroring it\ninto state. A role that is not a visible tab resolves to All on its own,\nincluding when the super-admin access probe settles after first render, and\nthe tab now survives a reload or a shared link.\n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"86d885c256f68df117e13e8d264366cce83cc292","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/trees/86d885c256f68df117e13e8d264366cce83cc292"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/commits/e3cf59a9b8ddcc294f26f33faf59c699f14ad202","verification":{"payload":"tree 86d885c256f68df117e13e8d264366cce83cc292\nparent 4d7232eedaecf5d84b789c3f23638c5cf5e82a42\nauthor Rahat Ali <rahat.ali@arbisoft.com> 1787552671 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787552671 +0500\n\nfeat(dashboard): wire the Attendance card to its endpoint (#15)\n\nAttendance overview now reads GET /fbr/api/reports/dashboard/attendance/,\nwhich was the last section still backed by fixtures. mockData.js and\nselectors.js had no consumers left afterwards and are deleted, so every\nfigure on the dashboard now comes from the API.\n\nFour numbers the fixtures invented are gone, because the endpoint does not\nhave them: the \"+2.4 pts vs last period\" delta, \"11 below 75% threshold\",\n\"today''s sessions marked 5/6\" and \"trainees tracked\". The footer stat row\nthey occupied goes with them.\n\nWhat replaces them is real. `pending` joins present/absent/leave as a fourth\nstate, in neutral grey: the backend counts it in the denominator, so hiding\nit would inflate the rate — on seeded data that is ~48% against ~72%. A\nprogramme with attendance_rate null reads \"Not started\" rather than 0%,\nsince no sessions yet is not the same as nobody attending, and those sort\nlast. The programme list is a ranked sample the API caps at ten, so it now\nsays \"Showing the 10 lowest of 23 programs\" instead of implying it is the\nwhole portfolio.\n\nNeeds attention loses a level. The course was a heading row above its\nsessions; it is now an eyebrow on each session row — COURSE · DIRECT\nTAXATION, or NO COURSE ATTACHED for a programme-wide ceremony — so a row\nsays what it belongs to without a grouping row repeating it. isGroup, the\nlevel-3 indent and the heading styling all go with it.\n\n\"Unmarked\" becomes \"Pending\" throughout the copy. Status.PENDING is what\nthe platform stores and what the Attendance report already renders, so the\ndashboard was the one screen using its own word.\n\nThe Users role cards deep-link to their own tab: the card carries ?role=,\nand UsersPage derives the active tab from the URL rather than mirroring it\ninto state. A role that is not a visible tab resolves to All on its own,\nincluding when the super-admin access probe settles after first render, and\nthe tab now survives a reload or a shared link.\n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqi+OfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ5oQAJgnTK/AjSrD6hC1yMAAeULg\n/pf9ADNySWAHDtdkEqWSuF59hQuGp6y3ZDTUlXmrb/uuA16OtmMnL3pSBvH9LgV0\nez3fJ4KIGHAMI/B5YXZAVPSifTpMbvQ2EeJOwvlWCcj62FemNhhqGGkzdAf9Oms+\n232GvvppfDwASrAkwX2r8GDbzqQ3fWSX1/OOWoFmx5GZwdBTy1pq8Ra/zb1ldg/r\nG4dpn8Zyq9Yqu1b4Z9RBSvTdsIEZ/eqHsvc9Nq+JLzIQnFnllhVGXGmvHrNr803X\n0+XiYsqrVVHbqD4jlndzBztnzzMn0dxfUFnspnjrB+NJxkhObTScx86x2WerdG9/\ngKQvU20jITCKwiAdb334zAjpB2GaRpBUDJmZSajXdnJKQEOkPPXUNSb6nsAC2F2g\ng5y3yUiRUYl3Qmdx4luYpuBMEgp8C4fq5uAu9a+SHQcL5k1dYr24sr2v85LZ/+2W\n0jdaZmlBuuEmXylJKpbT1/h6lUBNDn4OFmtNmtX45qvmGLXDh8UWH6ATnDYFtgZ0\ne/53QouIs3n1Poi+2Y0T00HBeZdAxe8dogSoIinXFsSSoaehjJqg9tdS3nTN1foS\nReJBPG7PFBThkuDwQ1fSje3TMJHQMNOYIDUTAlr1pfuZMklxNj7ctyfUitU4rnPt\nJTAiugFI6AOLPZrD183E\n=eOIN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":