ons","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/3d4c4020f5b2e1f935f4f47ee83884f63ceff3dd","node_id":"C_kwDOSir9AdoAKDNkNGM0MDIwZjViMmUxZjkzNWY0ZjQ3ZWU4Mzg4NGY2M2NlZmYzZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commit/13d7e04d275608288e6c056a218b7d5ed1c944a9","sha":"13d7e04d275608288e6c056a218b7d5ed1c944a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/13d7e04d275608288e6c056a218b7d5ed1c944a9"}],"sha":"3d4c4020f5b2e1f935f4f47ee83884f63ceff3dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/3d4c4020f5b2e1f935f4f47ee83884f63ceff3dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51116673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arbirali","id":51116673,"login":"arbirali","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTE2Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/commits/13d7e04d275608288e6c056a218b7d5ed1c944a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T13:38:18Z","email":"rahat.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Rahat Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T13:38:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add dashboard data layer, tokens and shared UI primitives (#10)\n\n* feat: add dashboard data layer, tokens and shared UI primitives\n\nGroundwork for the FBR Admin dashboard. Nothing is rendered yet -- this\nlayer only adds the pieces the section widgets build on:\n\n- data/: api client, react-query hooks, selectors and mock fixtures\n- constants.js: colour tokens plus attendance/rating band helpers\n- messages.js: i18n strings for the dashboard\n- styles.scss: dashboard stylesheet, including a dark-variant block keyed\n  off Paragon''s `data-paragon-theme-variant` attribute\n- SectionHeading / SectionState / MeterBar / SegmentedBar / StarRating /\n  WeeklySessionsChart: presentational primitives shared by every section\n\n* feat: add dashboard section widgets (#11)\n\n* feat: add dashboard section widgets\n\nBuilds the six dashboard sections on top of the primitives and data layer\nfrom the previous PR. Still not wired into any route, so this is dead code\nuntil the next PR in the stack:\n\n- UsersOverview: user counts and role split\n- SessionsOverview: session volume plus the weekly chart\n- AttendanceOverview: attendance bands and rates\n- FeedbackOverview: rating distribution and averages\n- ProgramPerformance: per-program completion figures\n- NeedsAttention: items flagged for admin follow-up\n\nRole cards hand their surface and hue to the stylesheet as custom\nproperties so the dark variant can restyle them; task actions use\nParagon''s primary Button.\n\n* feat: add Dashboard page and wire it into admin console nav (#12)\n\n* feat: add Dashboard page and wire it into admin console nav\n\nAssembles the sections into DashboardPage and makes the dashboard reachable:\n\n- DashboardPage: composes the six sections, handles loading/permission\n  states via useReportsAccess and falls back to mock data\n- routes.jsx: /dashboard route\n- Sidebar.jsx, constants.js, messages.js: Dashboard nav item under\n  Administration, using the fa-tachometer-alt icon\n\n* feat: enhanced weekly chart","tree":{"sha":"623c77d9baf67aa2243713f4108682d26a5d3eba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/trees/623c77d9baf67aa2243713f4108682d26a5d3eba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-fbr-admin/git/commits/13d7e04d275608288e6c056a218b7d5ed1c944a9","verification":{"payload":"tree 623c77d9baf67aa2243713f4108682d26a5d3eba\nparent a37695385c48a15fd1d786a0b755f53d6bfffacf\nauthor Rahat Ali <rahat.ali@arbisoft.com> 1787060298 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787060298 +0500\n\nfeat: add dashboard data layer, tokens and shared UI primitives (#10)\n\n* feat: add dashboard data layer, tokens and shared UI primitives\n\nGroundwork for the FBR Admin dashboard. Nothing is rendered yet -- this\nlayer only adds the pieces the section widgets build on:\n\n- data/: api client, react-query hooks, selectors and mock fixtures\n- constants.js: colour tokens plus attendance/rating band helpers\n- messages.js: i18n strings for the dashboard\n- styles.scss: dashboard stylesheet, including a dark-variant block keyed\n  off Paragon''s `data-paragon-theme-variant` attribute\n- SectionHeading / SectionState / MeterBar / SegmentedBar / StarRating /\n  WeeklySessionsChart: presentational primitives shared by every section\n\n* feat: add dashboard section widgets (#11)\n\n* feat: add dashboard section widgets\n\nBuilds the six dashboard sections on top of the primitives and data layer\nfrom the previous PR. Still not wired into any route, so this is dead code\nuntil the next PR in the stack:\n\n- UsersOverview: user counts and role split\n- SessionsOverview: session volume plus the weekly chart\n- AttendanceOverview: attendance bands and rates\n- FeedbackOverview: rating distribution and averages\n- ProgramPerformance: per-program completion figures\n- NeedsAttention: items flagged for admin follow-up\n\nRole cards hand their surface and hue to the stylesheet as custom\nproperties so the dark variant can restyle them; task actions use\nParagon''s primary Button.\n\n* feat: add Dashboard page and wire it into admin console nav (#12)\n\n* feat: add Dashboard page and wire it into admin console nav\n\nAssembles the sections into DashboardPage and makes the dashboard reachable:\n\n- DashboardPage: composes the six sections, handles loading/permission\n  states via useReportsAccess and falls back to mock data\n- routes.jsx: /dashboard route\n- Sidebar.jsx, constants.js, messages.js: Dashboard nav item under\n  Administration, using the fa-tachometer-alt icon\n\n* feat: enhanced weekly chart","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhGBKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAl2cQAJDrqO+ibbXfD8St1F1vKsgZ\n0w0Yb0ttOoVWXA0yusac1iwypiygZb7XR+orYwnVkkTqXKbUHyBAN/0Xv41NnBnV\nKpGyXmtCXDORVrjy7Bu3EjGUtBpP2HjogTBCkf1N87CHKrnV5jJqrJJxRvd5HbrD\n06Pwzli27wiYjAElq1CPkGu2PKnwnJBDuOrW+ixOqK+wT+ccWBisBpIRn7XbNpai\nfF8YIub3CW05ZVRNgqks8vvufTqMFqK4B+joCNKwfq30AGAJxoEVEkZf6eKxNUgC\nSnMrwEZ3t7hkmI0tXnGH2E/73NBY9C+unGX07DPf7Tks0ORtSEgVnERv4CCzQtg7\na4RtrU4ceynttrq3UzEnGRsQEYYzc5LWPRwsz54Vd2H+FZExsrdqNWtmXSvHoFHu\nlvEbiFi7jtyoQ3JQy6Re5VJldEVfbLA/UlahzlG1r83sHY8XTer9M3Rt/4mhG7De\nz1LQKW739KcGIynuxHTgGUmw4zlAvI9Ieewb9hlqdMBEd5ThKrdEJOcze/WVfkhb\ne1bmw24fjeM2OfOf5hH/xwin3va0SKKjPJEdGgAioXOLX1Qbd+gzZ1oLunYQLNko\nKOWaVbvFj27g5eKurHA29HGPBRHv12Z7zonGQhL47E4BVp3p8L8iY1Yi8bZ69pah\nUasgY3Nsq9ck1p8tlqqb\n=aMZE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T13:38:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_i