fc73dc03e35c1dc886bc6468013eb2275","sha":"90a5615fc73dc03e35c1dc886bc6468013eb2275","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Omnishore-Smart-Agents/Omniplatform/commits/90a5615fc73dc03e35c1dc886bc6468013eb2275"}],"sha":"eb1d41b840bce5708b21fb73fa135a7bcc50a64c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Omnishore-Smart-Agents/Omniplatform/commits/eb1d41b840bce5708b21fb73fa135a7bcc50a64c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25951435?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaviTharuma/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaviTharuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaviTharuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaviTharuma/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RaviTharuma","id":25951435,"login":"RaviTharuma","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTUxNDM1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaviTharuma/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaviTharuma/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaviTharuma/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaviTharuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaviTharuma/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RaviTharuma","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Omnishore-Smart-Agents/Omniplatform/commits/90a5615fc73dc03e35c1dc886bc6468013eb2275/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-14T17:09:04Z","email":"25951435+RaviTharuma@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ravi Tharuma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-14T17:09:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add native OpenCode runtime and session support (#586)\n\n* Discover native OpenCode sessions from local SQLite state\n\nRead OpenCode''s local SQLite store directly so Mission Control can surface\nreal sessions without requiring a gateway bridge. The scanner is schema-tolerant\nfor the observed OpenCode 1.4.3 layout and prefers explicit OPENCODE_DB_PATH\nover store discovery when present.\n\nConstraint: OpenCode state formats vary across local installs and can span multiple DB files\nRejected: Stub a synthetic in-memory session source | would not prove native compatibility\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate\nDirective: Keep session discovery schema-tolerant; do not hardcode a single DB layout without real fixtures\nTested: src/lib/__tests__/opencode-sessions.test.ts\nNot-tested: UI-level rendering against very large real OpenCode histories\n\n* Expose OpenCode through runtime detection and session APIs\n\nWire the new OpenCode scanner into Mission Control''s runtime detection and\nsession APIs so the dashboard can discover local OpenCode installs and merge\nOpenCode sessions alongside Claude, Codex, and Hermes.\n\nConstraint: Runtime/session support had to stay additive and avoid breaking existing local and gateway flows\nRejected: Ship OpenCode only through the external bridge agent | would leave native runtime support incomplete\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate\nDirective: Keep OpenCode session support additive; do not regress existing Claude/Codex/Hermes merge behavior\nTested: src/lib/__tests__/agent-runtimes-opencode.test.ts; pnpm typecheck\nNot-tested: Cross-machine OpenCode installs with custom binary paths outside the current candidate list\n\n* Surface OpenCode in runtime setup and session branding\n\nMake OpenCode visible as a first-class runtime in the settings and onboarding\nsurfaces, and give local OpenCode sessions distinct branding in the session UI\nso operators can recognize them without falling back to gateway semantics.\n\nConstraint: UI changes had to fit existing runtime cards and onboarding flows without introducing new design primitives\nRejected: Reuse Codex branding for OpenCode | would hide the new runtime distinction and confuse operators\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow\nDirective: Keep OpenCode visually distinct from Codex and gateway sessions in any future session lists or runtime cards\nTested: pnpm typecheck\nNot-tested: Visual review in every dashboard panel that may later render runtime badges\n\n* Preserve OpenCode session behavior across workspace flows\n\nPropagate OpenCode as a real session kind through conversation lists, workspace\nstate, and terminal-related UI so the app stops collapsing it into gateway or\nunsupported PTY behavior in downstream flows.\n\nConstraint: OpenCode had to remain transcript/continue-only because the PTY backend still supports only Claude and Codex\nRejected: Expose OpenCode as PTY-capable | would advertise a terminal path that the backend rejects\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate\nDirective: If PTY support is added later, update both the attach route and the workspace gating together\nTested: pnpm typecheck; tests/session-controls.spec.ts\nNot-tested: Multi-pane workspace ergonomics for future OpenCode PTY support (currently disabled)\n\n* Add native OpenCode transcript and continue route support\n\nTeach the session transcript and continue endpoints to understand OpenCode\nsessions, read real OpenCode message history, and invoke the configured\nOpenCode CLI while surfacing provider/model failures honestly.\n\nConstraint: Real OpenCode continue behavior is environment-dependent because saved sessions can reference unavailable providers/models\nRejected: Pretend continue always succeeds in tests | would hide the real failure mode and make the API dishonest\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate\nDirective: Keep transcript parsing schema-tolerant and keep continue semantics honest when the local OpenCode environment cannot satisfy a saved session\nTested: src/app/api/sessions/__tests__/transcript-opencode.test.ts; src/app/api/sessions/__tests__/continue-route-opencode.test.ts\nNot-tested: Every possible OpenCode message payload variant beyond the observed real local schema\n\n* Make OpenCode session verification hermetic in E2E\n\nAdd a deterministic OpenCode binary and a real-schema SQLite fixture to the\nE2E harness so session listing, transcript reads, and continue-session HTTP\nflows can be verified from a clean checkout without ambient local state.\n\nConstraint: The verification path had to work even when .next and test-results were absent at the start of the run\nRejected: Depend on the developer''s ambient OpenCode install/state in Playwright | not contribution-ready and not reproducible\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate\nDirective: Keep the E2E harness fixture aligned with the observed real OpenCode schema whenever upstream OpenCode changes its local state layout\nTested: tests/session-controls.spec.ts from a clean state with no .next and no test-results\nNot-tested: Multi-user or multi-workspace E2E permutations beyond the single-session fixture path\n\n* Make build and lint verification reproducible in the fork\n\nPin Next''s workspace root to this repo and ignore generated E2E artifacts in\nlint so the verification sequence remains stable in /Users/ravi/Code/forks\nwithout relying on parent-directory lockfiles or pre-created output folders.\n\nConstraint: Contribution work must remain fully isolated under /Users/ravi/Code/forks\nRejected: Manually create test-results or rely on ambient lockfile layout | brittle and not reproducible\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow\nDirective: Keep verification tooling self-contained in the fork workspace; do not reintroduce assumptions about parent-directory state\nTested: pnpm build; pnpm lint from a clean state\nNot-tested: Alternate package-manager layouts beyond the current pnpm-based workspace\n\n* Document OpenCode session API semantics clearly\n\nUpdate the OpenAPI contract so the expanded runtime/session surface describes\nOpenCode accurately, including transcript and continue behavior plus honest\n500-path error semantics for continue when the local runtime cannot satisfy a\nsaved session.\n\nConstraint: Contract parity must stay green while describing behavior truthfully\nRejected: Leave continue/transcript behavior implicit | would make the docs disagree with tested runtime behavior\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow\nDirective: Keep the OpenAPI spec aligned with route behavior whenever OpenCode session semantics evolve\nTested: pnpm api:parity\nNot-tested: External client generation against the updated schema\n\n* Document OpenCode capabilities in the API index\n\nUpdate the route catalog copy so the public API index reflects the actual\nsession capabilities after native OpenCode support, including transcript and\ncontinue coverage without implying unsupported PTY behavior.\n\nConstraint: The API index must stay truthful without broadening scope beyond the implemented OpenCode paths\nRejected: Leave the catalog at Claude/Codex wording | would under-document the shipped OpenCode surface\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow\nDirective: Keep the API index descriptions aligned with the OpenAPI contract and actual route behavior\nTested: pnpm api:parity\nNot-tested: Downstream docs consumers beyond the built-in API index view\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ravi Tharuma <RaviTharuma@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"117380a3d189b09f5a1e0a647ddf1f639ad7c3a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Omnishore-Smart-Agents/Omniplatform/git/trees/117380a3d189b09f5a1e0a647ddf1f639ad7c3a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Omnishore-Smart-Agents/Omniplatform/git/commits/90a5615fc73dc03e35c1dc886bc6468013eb2275","verification":{"payload":"tree 117380a3d189b09f5a1e0a647ddf1f639ad7c3a1\nparent bd972bc953d1bf2c6d9f7febc941a2d3b3b63ba0\nauthor Ravi Tharuma <25951435+RaviTharuma@users.noreply.github.com> 1776186544 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776186544 +0700\n\nfeat: add native OpenCode runtime and session support (#586)\n\n* Discover native OpenCode sessions from local SQLite state\n\nRead OpenCode''s local SQLite store directly so Mission Control can surface\nreal sessions without requiring a gateway bridge. The scanner is schema-tolerant\nfor the observed OpenCode 1.4.3 layout and prefers explicit OPENCODE_DB_PATH\nover store discovery when present.\n\nConstraint: OpenCode state formats vary across local installs and can span multiple DB files\nRejected: Stub a synthetic in-memory session source | would not prove native compatibility\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate\nDirective: Keep session discovery schema-tolerant; do not hardcode a single DB layout without real fixtures\nTested: src/lib/__tests__/opencode-sessions.test.ts\nNot-tested: UI-level rendering against very large real OpenCode histories\n\n* Expose OpenCode through runtime detection and session APIs\n\nWire the new OpenCode scanner into Mission Control''s runtime detection and\nsession APIs so the dashboard can discover local OpenCode installs and merge\nOpenCode sessions alongside Claude, Codex, and Hermes.\n\nConstraint: Runtime/session support had to stay additive and avoid breaking existing local and gateway flows\nRejected: Ship OpenCode only through the external bridge agent | would leave native runtime support incomplete\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate\nDirective: Keep OpenCode session support additive; do not regress existing Claude/Codex/Hermes merge behavior\nTested: src/lib/__tests__/agent-runtimes-opencode.test.ts; pnpm typecheck\nNot-tested: Cross-machine OpenCode installs with custom binary paths outside the current candidate list\n\n* Surface OpenCode in runtime setup and session branding\n\nMake OpenCode visible as a first-class runtime in the settings and onboarding\nsurfaces, and give local OpenCode sessions distinct branding in the session UI\nso operators can recognize them without falling back to gateway semantics.\n\nConstraint: UI changes had to fit existing runtime cards and onboarding flows without introducing new design primitives\nRejected: Reuse Codex branding for OpenCode | would hide the new runtime distinction and confuse operators\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow\nDirective: Keep OpenCode visually distinct from Codex and gateway sessions in any future session lists or runtime cards\nTested: pnpm typecheck\nNot-tested: Visual review in every dashboard panel that may later render runtime badges\n\n* Preserve OpenCode session behavior across workspace flows\n\nPropagate OpenCode as a real session kind through conversation lists, workspace\nstate, and terminal-related UI so the app stops collapsing it into gateway or\nunsupported PTY behavior in downstream flows.\n\nConstraint: OpenCode had to remain transcript/continue-only because the PTY backend still supports only Claude and Codex\nRejected: Expose OpenCode as PTY-capable | would advertise a terminal path that the backend rejects\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate\nDirective: If PTY support is added later, update both the attach route and the workspace gating together\nTested: pnpm typecheck; tests/session-controls.spec.ts\nNot-tested: Multi-pane workspace ergonomics for future OpenCode PTY support (currently disabled)\n\n* Add native OpenCode transcript and continue route support\n\nTeach the session transcript and continue endpoints to understand OpenCode\nsessions, read real OpenCode message history, and invoke the configured\nOpenCode CLI while surfacing provider/model failures honestly.\n\nConstraint: Real OpenCode continue behavior is environment-dependent because saved sessions can reference unavailable providers/models\nRejected: Pretend continue always succeeds in tests | would hide the real failure mode and make the API dishonest\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate\nDirective: Keep transcript parsing schema-tolerant and keep continue semantics honest when the local OpenCode environment cannot satisfy a saved session\nTested: src/app/api/sessions/__tests__/transcript-opencode.test.ts; src/app/api/sessions/__tests__/continue-route-opencode.test.ts\nNot-tested: Every possible OpenCode message payload variant beyond the observed real local schema\n\n* Make OpenCode session verification hermetic in E2E\n\nAdd a deterministic OpenCode binary and a real-schema SQLite fixture to the\nE2E harness so session listing, transcript reads, and continue-session HTTP\nflows can be verified from a clean checkout without ambient local state.\n\nConstraint: The verification path had to work even when .next and test-results were absent at the start of the run\nRejected: Depend on the developer''s ambient OpenCode install/state in Playwright | not contribution-ready and not reproducible\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate\nDirective: Keep the E2E harness fixture aligned with the observed real OpenCode schema whenever upstream OpenCode changes its local state layout\nTested: tests/session-controls.spec.ts from a clean state with no .next and no test-results\nNot-tested: Multi-user or multi-workspace E2E permutations beyond the single-session fixture path\n\n* Make build and lint verification reproducible in the fork\n\nPin Next''s workspace root to this repo and ignore generated E2E artifacts in\nlint so the verification sequence remains stable in /Users/ravi/Code/forks\nwithout relying on parent-directory lockfiles or pre-created output folders.\n\nConstraint: Contribution work must remain fully isolated under /Users/ravi/Code/forks\nRejected: Manually create test-results or rely on ambient lockfile layout | brittle and not reproducible\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow\nDirective: Keep verification tooling self-contained in the fork workspace; do not reintroduce assumptions about parent-directory state\nTested: pnpm build; pnpm lint from a clean state\nNot-tested: Alternate package-manager layouts beyond the current pnpm-based workspace\n\n* Document OpenCode session API semantics clearly\n\nUpdate the OpenAPI contract so the expanded runtime/session surface describes\nOpenCode accurately, including transcript and continue behavior plus honest\n500-path error semantics for continue when the local runtime cannot satisfy a\nsaved session.\n\nConstraint: Contract parity must stay green while describing behavior truthfully\nRejected: Leave continue/transcript behavior implicit | would make the docs disagree with tested runtime behavior\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow\nDirective: Keep the OpenAPI spec aligned with route behavior whenever OpenCode session semantics evolve\nTested: pnpm api:parity\nNot-tested: External client generation against the updated schema\n\n* Document OpenCode capabilities in the API index\n\nUpdate the route catalog copy so the public API index reflects the actual\nsession capabilities after native OpenCode support, including transcript and\ncontinue coverage without implying unsupported PTY behavior.\n\nConstraint: The API index must stay truthful without broadening scope beyond the implemented OpenCode paths\nRejected: Leave the catalog at Claude/Codex wording | would under-document the shipped OpenCode surface\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow\nDirective: Keep the API index descriptions aligned with the OpenAPI contract and actual route behavior\nTested: pnpm api:parity\nNot-tested: Downstream docs consumers beyond the built-in API index view\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ravi Tharuma <RaviTharuma@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp3nSwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMhsQAAz7qls7qLe3wSWKCTp+kUcy\nHTtekD1H7rWK/0QNpcUIlubfVzcXxbrVZltImmDlPTj5x1HgQ5FxMiavyEpYwD66\najKUQejSMYAkqcHemIgbwriRVAMYVWAEnKyTLJMDDN8MdooQB6Nxrcc1pzIcvt0E\nLuR+5t6o0cc1UFmMvJE3Q2p4Vo1YAookbzMhaZYedfS5C4se6bmf7y5Nj88S1Hlh\noIBrYF1N0BPck4ClwnAuCVvL8kM4WSBdg75oKlKiJi2MIDhQwoMtEfd2yyskWwj/\n7eYBvRb4xU5/X353tq4cuWNgplBkTmSG2ojLjtbgydZvyDEABiaWlSKVKa82pFC1\nViedAjS3GLC692YuOtDy+O3v1Q/3h9GSKaBC4DKjyFlaROplB381tzF3gxgK0SbW\nQhumrEqSaP0WgQsLdKX0KoUEP/Ix+u98kHbAKNqHlHdw49aH0pp3tDzobhmquzEu\nWv6aZeZVQzM2yRJ88vWCg7YS2G8cS5kgfW05ULGTYsIcZUVPmTBwz+w