{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grasdouble/sebastien-lemouillour.fr/commit/030c65973c6aedf4d2e2cc95cdfe74972beafcdf","node_id":"C_kwDOSjUSptoAKDAzMGM2NTk3M2M2YWVkZjRkMmUyY2M5NWNkZmU3NDk3MmJlYWZjZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grasdouble/sebastien-lemouillour.fr/commit/5c7f70016a404fa871021dcf24ce146165d2c61a","sha":"5c7f70016a404fa871021dcf24ce146165d2c61a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grasdouble/sebastien-lemouillour.fr/commits/5c7f70016a404fa871021dcf24ce146165d2c61a"}],"sha":"030c65973c6aedf4d2e2cc95cdfe74972beafcdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grasdouble/sebastien-lemouillour.fr/commits/030c65973c6aedf4d2e2cc95cdfe74972beafcdf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1218742?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noofreuuuh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noofreuuuh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noofreuuuh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noofreuuuh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/noofreuuuh","id":1218742,"login":"noofreuuuh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTg3NDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noofreuuuh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noofreuuuh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noofreuuuh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noofreuuuh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noofreuuuh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/noofreuuuh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grasdouble/sebastien-lemouillour.fr/commits/5c7f70016a404fa871021dcf24ce146165d2c61a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T20:41:57Z","email":"dev.n2ofr@gmail.com","name":"Noofreuuuh"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T20:41:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add ai chat (#65)\n\n* feat: add ai-playground et ai-chatbot\n\n* refactor: migrate ai-chatbot to Lufa Design System with full component adoption and semantic tokens\n\n* refactor: complete migration to Lufa Design System in AI Playground\n\n- Fully adopted Lufa Design System components across PlaygroundInterface, PromptEditor, ParametersPanel, OutputDisplay, and more.\n- Replaced custom styles with semantic tokens for colors, spacing, and borders.\n- Introduced new LoadingIndicator component with gradient fill and reduced motion support.\n- Updated CapabilitiesInfo, ModelSelector, and PerformanceMetrics components to utilize DS components and styles.\n- Minimized custom CSS to only cover areas not handled by the Design System.\n- Added translation keys for loading model messages in English and French.\n- Ensured all tests pass and linting is clean.\n\n* feat: Refactor AI Playground components and add shared capabilities\n\n- Updated OutputDisplay styles for improved text handling.\n- Refactored PlaygroundInterface to enhance layout and integrate new shared components: CapabilitiesInfo, LoadingIndicator, and ModelSelector.\n- Removed unused translations from en.json and fr.json, and added shared translations for capabilities and loading states.\n- Introduced new shared components: CapabilitiesInfo, LoadingIndicator, and ModelSelector with corresponding styles and tests.\n- Updated model registry with new models and adjusted parameters for better performance.\n- Simplified provider factory to support only WebLLM, removing Transformers.js integration.\n- Added type definitions for shared components and ensured proper i18n support.\n\n* refactor: remove ai-playground parcel and related components\n\n- Deleted ai-playground parcel files including i18n, parcel.tsx, and configuration files.\n- Removed references to ai-playground in the header-bar navigation and localization files.\n- Updated shared package by removing unused components and dependencies related to ai-playground.\n- Adjusted import maps in slm-container to exclude ai-playground.\n\n* feat: add ConversationHistory component for managing chat history\n\n- Implemented ConversationHistory component to display, select, and delete conversations.\n- Added styles for conversation history UI.\n- Created index file for easy exports from conversation components.\n\nfeat: add CapabilitiesInfo and CapabilitiesWarning components\n\n- Introduced CapabilitiesInfo component to display browser capabilities.\n- Added CapabilitiesWarning component to alert users about missing capabilities.\n- Created corresponding styles and tests for both components.\n\nfeat: add LoadingIndicator and ModelSelector components\n\n- Developed LoadingIndicator component to show loading progress and status.\n- Implemented ModelSelector component for selecting models with detailed options.\n- Added styles and index files for both components.\n\nfix: refactor useConversationHistory hook for better type safety\n\n- Improved parsing logic for conversations stored in localStorage.\n- Enhanced error handling and validation for conversation data.\n\nchore: update i18n structure and remove unused language files\n\n- Removed old i18n files for LLM and updated main i18n configuration.\n- Added new loadError message to existing language files.\n\ntest: add unit tests for CapabilitiesWarning component\n\n- Created tests to verify rendering of warnings based on capabilities.\n- Ensured proper functionality of the CapabilitiesWarning component.\n\nfix: update vitest configuration for test setup\n\n- Adjusted setup file path in vitest configuration for correct test execution.\n\n* feat: implement chat area components including MessageInput, MessageList, and MessageContent\n\n- Added MessageInput component for user input with send functionality.\n- Introduced MessageList component to display conversation history with user and assistant messages.\n- Created MessageContent component to render messages with markdown support.\n- Implemented styles for chat area components.\n- Added tests for MessageInput and MessageList components.\n- Developed CapabilitiesCheck and CapabilitiesInfo components for model setup.\n- Created LoadingIndicator and ModelSelector components for loading states and model selection.\n- Implemented ConversationSidebar for managing conversation history.\n- Updated index files for new component exports.\n\n* refactor: reorganize AI chatbot components by UI responsibility, enhance translation keys, and improve loading indicators\n\n* feat: add gd-changeset-auditor skill for auditing changeset quality\n\n- Introduced a new memory agent, gd-changeset-auditor, that audits changeset quality on git branches.\n- Implemented capabilities to analyze changesets, validate quality, recommend consolidation, and generate corrected changesets.\n- Created detailed documentation in README.md outlining the agent''s purpose, activation, capabilities, and usage examples.\n- Added SKILL.md to define the agent''s description, mission, and core values.\n- Developed a script (analyze-changesets.py) for mechanical analysis of changesets, including coverage checking and violation detection.\n- Established memory architecture with structured files for persona, creed, bond, memory, and capabilities.\n- Included references for first breath activation, memory guidance, and real-world audit examples to aid in agent learning and operation.\n\n* Potential fix for pull request finding ''Unused import''\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <223894421+github-code-quality[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: enhance ESLint and TypeScript configuration, add highlight.js and markdown support, and improve vendor management\n\n* feat: add slm-changeset-auditor agent for auditing changeset quality\n\n- Introduced a new memory agent that audits changeset quality on git branches.\n- Implemented capabilities to analyze changesets, validate quality, recommend consolidation, and generate corrected changesets.\n- Created README.md detailing agent purpose, activation, capabilities, and usage examples.\n- Added SKILL.md for agent description and activation commands.\n- Developed analyze-changesets.py script for mechanical analysis of changesets.\n- Established memory architecture with session logs and structured files for learning repository patterns.\n- Included references for first breath activation, memory guidance, and real-world audit examples.\n- Defined core values, personality traits, and operational guidelines in CREED.md and BOND.md.\n- Set up templates for memory management and organic growth of knowledge.\n\n* fix: add changeset for learn\n\n* feat: enhance slm-changeset-auditor with detailed audit session examples, improved error handling, and comprehensive test suite\n\n* Remove outdated templates and scripts for changeset auditing\n\n- Deleted memory guidance documentation to streamline knowledge management.\n- Removed BOND, CAPABILITIES, CREED, INDEX, MEMORY, and PERSONA templates to eliminate redundancy.\n- Erased the analyze-changesets.py script and its associated test suite to simplify the auditing process.\n\n* fix: update AI chatbot parcel version from minor to major\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <223894421+github-code-quality[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"65282866130c95d87cb82b38fae7aeb4147ac198","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grasdouble/sebastien-lemouillour.fr/git/trees/65282866130c95d87cb82b38fae7aeb4147ac198"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grasdouble/sebastien-lemouillour.fr/git/commits/5c7f70016a404fa871021dcf24ce146165d2c61a","verification":{"payload":"tree 65282866130c95d87cb82b38fae7aeb4147ac198\nparent e895eb01c29e23a3b10bae54c551e5d025b9c0b7\nauthor Noofreuuuh <dev.n2ofr@gmail.com> 1780778517 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780778517 +0200\n\nfeat: add ai chat (#65)\n\n* feat: add ai-playground et ai-chatbot\n\n* refactor: migrate ai-chatbot to Lufa Design System with full component adoption and semantic tokens\n\n* refactor: complete migration to Lufa Design System in AI Playground\n\n- Fully adopted Lufa Design System components across PlaygroundInterface, PromptEditor, ParametersPanel, OutputDisplay, and more.\n- Replaced custom styles with semantic tokens for colors, spacing, and borders.\n- Introduced new LoadingIndicator component with gradient fill and reduced motion support.\n- Updated CapabilitiesInfo, ModelSelector, and PerformanceMetrics components to utilize DS components and styles.\n- Minimized custom CSS to only cover areas not handled by the Design System.\n- Added translation keys for loading model messages in English and French.\n- Ensured all tests pass and linting is clean.\n\n* feat: Refactor AI Playground components and add shared capabilities\n\n- Updated OutputDisplay styles for improved text handling.\n- Refactored PlaygroundInterface to enhance layout and integrate new shared components: CapabilitiesInfo, LoadingIndicator, and ModelSelector.\n- Removed unused translations from en.json and fr.json, and added shared translations for capabilities and loading states.\n- Introduced new shared components: CapabilitiesInfo, LoadingIndicator, and ModelSelector with corresponding styles and tests.\n- Updated model registry with new models and adjusted parameters for better performance.\n- Simplified provider factory to support only WebLLM, removing Transformers.js integration.\n- Added type definitions for shared components and ensured proper i18n support.\n\n* refactor: remove ai-playground parcel and related components\n\n- Deleted ai-playground parcel files including i18n, parcel.tsx, and configuration files.\n- Removed references to ai-playground in the header-bar navigation and localization files.\n- Updated shared package by removing unused components and dependencies related to ai-playground.\n- Adjusted import maps in slm-container to exclude ai-playground.\n\n* feat: add ConversationHistory component for managing chat history\n\n- Implemented ConversationHistory component to display, select, and delete conversations.\n- Added styles for conversation history UI.\n- Created index file for easy exports from conversation components.\n\nfeat: add CapabilitiesInfo and CapabilitiesWarning components\n\n- Introduced CapabilitiesInfo component to display browser capabilities.\n- Added CapabilitiesWarning component to alert users about missing capabilities.\n- Created corresponding styles and tests for both components.\n\nfeat: add LoadingIndicator and ModelSelector components\n\n- Developed LoadingIndicator component to show loading progress and status.\n- Implemented ModelSelector component for selecting models with detailed options.\n- Added styles and index files for both components.\n\nfix: refactor useConversationHistory hook for better type safety\n\n- Improved parsing logic for conversations stored in localStorage.\n- Enhanced error handling and validation for conversation data.\n\nchore: update i18n structure and remove unused language files\n\n- Removed old i18n files for LLM and updated main i18n configuration.\n- Added new loadError message to existing language files.\n\ntest: add unit tests for CapabilitiesWarning component\n\n- Created tests to verify rendering of warnings based on capabilities.\n- Ensured proper functionality of the CapabilitiesWarning component.\n\nfix: update vitest configuration for test setup\n\n- Adjusted setup file path in vitest configuration for correct test execution.\n\n* feat: implement chat area components including MessageInput, MessageList, and MessageContent\n\n- Added MessageInput component for user input with send functionality.\n- Introduced MessageList component to display conversation history with user and assistant messages.\n- Created MessageContent component to render messages with markdown support.\n- Implemented styles for chat area components.\n- Added tests for MessageInput and MessageList components.\n- Developed CapabilitiesCheck and CapabilitiesInfo components for model setup.\n- Created LoadingIndicator and ModelSelector components for loading states and model selection.\n- Implemented ConversationSidebar for managing conversation history.\n- Updated index files for new component exports.\n\n* refactor: reorganize AI chatbot components by UI responsibility, enhance translation keys, and improve loading indicators\n\n* feat: add gd-changeset-auditor skill for auditing changeset quality\n\n- Introduced a new memory agent, gd-changeset-auditor, that audits changeset quality on git branches.\n- Implemented capabilities to analyze changesets, validate quality, recommend consolidation, and generate corrected changesets.\n- Created detailed documentation in README.md outlining the agent''s purpose, activation, capabilities, and usage examples.\n- Added SKILL.md to define the agent''s description, mission, and core values.\n- Developed a script (analyze-changesets.py) for mechanical analysis of changesets, including coverage checking and violation detection.\n- Established memory architecture with structured files for persona, creed, bond, memory, and capabilities.\n- Included references for first breath activation, memory guidance, and real-world audit examples to aid in agent learning and operation.\n\n* Potential fix for pull request finding ''Unused import''\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <223894421+github-code-quality[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: enhance ESLint and TypeScript configuration, add highlight.js and markdown support, and improve vendor management\n\n* feat: add slm-changeset-auditor agent for auditing changeset quality\n\n- Introduced a new memory agent that audits changeset quality on git branches.\n- Implemented capabilities to analyze changesets, validate quality, recommend consolidation, and generate corrected changesets.\n- Created README.md detailing agent purpose, activation, capabilities, and usage examples.\n- Added SKILL.md for agent description and activation commands.\n- Developed analyze-changesets.py script for mechanical analysis of changesets.\n- Established memory architecture with session logs and structured files for learning repository patterns.\n- Included references for first breath activation, memory guidance, and real-world audit examples.\n- Defined core values, personality traits, and operational guidelines in CREED.md and BOND.md.\n- Set up templates for memory management and organic growth of knowledge.\n\n* fix: add changeset for learn\n\n* feat: enhance slm-changeset-auditor with detailed audit session examples, improved error handling, and comprehensive test suite\n\n* Remove outdated templates and scripts for changeset auditing\n\n- Deleted memory guidance documentation to streamline knowledge management.\n- Removed BOND, CAPABILITIES, CREED, INDEX, MEMORY, and PERSONA templates to eliminate redundancy.\n- Erased the analyze-changesets.py script and its associated test suite to simplify the auditing process.\n\n* fix: update AI chatbot parcel version from minor to major\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <223894421+github-code-quality[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJIYVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0K4QADa7ngSdiTxCIA9bfFZfItEV\ntkZxi6FsarqoZ8H4JrplaxShKL13c+XvNvD0LoN8dFORCg5wbrUi7Ab407BAQE2b\nUN4K6E+9EDxFYi6iJ0pMdHWbNtNa5RMvpogdSBdkjXGUmKKhOh5unfBJnSVv1Y7A\nbFJvVgy/kqrWedNhWDPOhmeWn26K2xCbnUEiJkGYTIuDLF2j1ldIo+tO8HDiMx92\nFwG5Tg+C99bb+THO4+QMyrc3sZbYVYqSjVM4eEoVMbsdhvgmFGsOEQL6Z3y789Sw\nusGBvIMQLNpyVUSiHFy0SHOzt0AoiX0ygda7UMPWkmURfgwEqf8eVaYgNGx3fv3A\nXjRw3g2QRHFj2qVv+HXjbPgp/gFvGzReAMN481aytBnegaieIszQGQNXJ4U65c5v\nmGUfTq47vFdzXmUIZqW7fe2Y/SAHZlbMwM5SBHI+HbHxVPruyBlDUvg/RgE5LV+V\neMGp