s in both languages.\n- Expanded on hybrid search strategies with a trade-off table and visual flowchart for clarity.\n- Clarified the implications of overlap in chunking with a practical percentage table for both English and French versions.\n- Introduced a reranking approach table to outline latency, cost, and quality considerations.\n- Provided a comparative analysis of vector databases, emphasizing operational friction and filtering capabilities.\n- Updated vector search sections to include flowcharts and emphasize the importance of metadata in retrieval quality.\n\n* fix: update bilingual guide content for gpu-and-vram section","tree":{"sha":"a0c6bde45671e94711bcfe4615a0c1667803e725","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grasdouble/sebastien-lemouillour.fr/git/trees/a0c6bde45671e94711bcfe4615a0c1667803e725"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grasdouble/sebastien-lemouillour.fr/git/commits/1a93f69b59ab1f2ea48baefce29c17f6be657b88","verification":{"payload":"tree a0c6bde45671e94711bcfe4615a0c1667803e725\nparent a51507ab51091c8371374204ef7c356c43d2d188\nauthor Noofreuuuh <dev.n2ofr@gmail.com> 1780257357 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780257357 +0200\n\nfix: add table and schema in guides (#53)\n\n* Refactor code structure for improved readability and maintainability\n\n* Enhance RAG Vector Search Documentation\n\n- Added mermaid diagrams to illustrate document indexing and graph RAG processes in both English and French.\n- Included a detailed scorecard for evaluating RAG systems, highlighting key metrics and their targets in both languages.\n- Expanded on hybrid search strategies with a trade-off table and visual flowchart for clarity.\n- Clarified the implications of overlap in chunking with a practical percentage table for both English and French versions.\n- Introduced a reranking approach table to outline latency, cost, and quality considerations.\n- Provided a comparative analysis of vector databases, emphasizing operational friction and filter