gents (#49)\n\n* Add French and English guides for GitHub Copilot and AI Agents\n\n- Introduced new markdown files for configuring AGENTS.md, creating Skills, and using Custom Agents in both English and French.\n- Added introductory guides for GitHub Copilot, detailing its various modes and effective usage.\n- Implemented Model Context Protocol (MCP) documentation to enhance agent capabilities.\n- Updated localization files to include new content for the Copilot section.\n- Organized content structure to improve accessibility and understanding of AI agent workflows.\n\n* feat: add publishedAt and updatedAt fields to tutorials and guides\n\n- Updated tutorial frontmatter to include publishedAt and updatedAt dates.\n- Enhanced the parsing logic to validate date formats for publishedAt and updatedAt.\n- Implemented filtering of tutorials based on publication status in the useLearn hook.\n- Added localization for published and updated dates in English and French.\n- Updated dependencies for lufa_design_system and related packages.\n\n* Update content for LLM and AI agents documentation\n\n- Revised French and English documentation for \"Copilot with AI Agents\" including MCP and Skills sections, enhancing clarity and examples.\n- Updated publication and update dates for various LLM-related articles to December 31, 2026.\n- Improved structure and examples in \"RAG Fundamentals,\" \"LLM Production,\" and \"Prompt Engineering\" sections to better guide users.\n\n* feat: implement useShowUnpublished hook and update catalog filtering logic\n\n* feat: add scripts for catalog order mapping, consistency checking, inventory snapshot, and structural validation\n\n- Implemented `catalog-order-map.py` to read and validate the ordering of guides in a catalog, detecting duplicates and checking for contiguous order.\n- Created `consistency-check.py` to cross-reference category keys, catalog orders, content folders, and i18n files, reporting any discrepancies.\n- Developed `inventory-snapshot.py` to output a comprehensive list of guides with their metadata including category, catalog, order, difficulty, and dates.\n- Added `structural-validation.py` for deterministic checks on guides, including frontmatter parity, date validity, duplicate URLs, and banned phrases.\n- Introduced unit tests for all new scripts to ensure functionality and correctness, utilizing fixture-based temporary directories for testing.\n- Updated existing tests to enhance coverage and ensure consistency across the learn data structure.\n\n* feat: enhance structural validation and update catalog workflows with new link checks and guide modes\n\n* feat: update voice and content quality rules across guides and scripts\n\n* feat: update publication dates and enhance content clarity in AI fundamentals and prompt engineering sections\n\n* feat: add decision log and update publication dates for tooling essentials guides\n\n* refactor: update pnpm workspaces and vite tooling documentation for clarity and conciseness\n\n- Revised explanations and examples in pnpm workspaces documentation to enhance readability and reduce redundancy.\n- Improved the structure and flow of the vite tooling documentation, emphasizing key concepts and best practices for beginners.\n- Adjusted code snippets for accuracy and consistency across both English and French versions.\n\n* fix: add more catalog\n\n* Update LLM documentation in French and English: revise content for clarity, accuracy, and consistency; adjust publication dates; enhance explanations of LLM functionality and AI concepts.\n\n* Remove outdated course items and descriptions from French localization file for AI and LLM topics in the learn package.\n\n* Update publication dates\n\n* fix changeset\n\n* fix review\n\n* fix review\n\n* chore: add missing parcels to lufa_design-system update\n\n* Refactor tags in LLM-related content for consistency and clarity\n\n- Updated tags in various English and French markdown files related to LLMs to use \"llm\" and more relevant keywords.\n- Removed outdated or less relevant tags such as \"IA\" and \"contexte\" to improve searchability and relevance.\n- Ensured all files maintain a consistent tagging structure for better organization and discoverability.\n\n* fix: update pluralization keys for guide counts in localization files\n\n* chore: update publication dates for LLM content and enhance LangSwitcher component\n\n- Updated publication dates for multiple LLM-related markdown files to December 31, 2026.\n- Added a new LangSwitcher component for language selection with corresponding tests.\n- Updated package.json to include new dependencies for the LangSwitcher component.\n- Adjusted TypeScript configuration to include .tsx files.","tree":{"sha":"9a6ecdae0f4e05fcfb5f68e584bcea60a25341e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grasdouble/sebastien-lemouillour.fr/git/trees/9a6ecdae0f4e05fcfb5f68e584bcea60a25341e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grasdouble/sebastien-lemouillour.fr/git/commits/f19544dd50bb8b17503d726c4bc85f61ccd4892d","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a6ecdae0f4e05fcfb5f68e584bcea60a25341e4\nparent 405908593a18d79b3d14c28c50d5abd164e5df44\nauthor Noofreuuuh <dev.n2ofr@gmail.com> 1780230178 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780230178 +0200\n\nfeat: add bilingual guides and enhance documentation for AI agents (#49)\n\n* Add French and English guides for GitHub Copilot and AI Agents\n\n- Introduced new markdown files for configuring AGENTS.md, creating Skills, and using Custom Agents in both English and French.\n- Added introductory guides for GitHub Copilot, detailing its various modes and effective usage.\n- Implemented Model Context Protocol (MCP) documentation to enhance agent capabilities.\n- Updated localization files to include new content for the Copilot section.\n- Organized content structure to improve accessibility and understanding of AI agent workflows.\n\n* feat: add publishedAt and updatedAt fields to tutorials and guides\n\n