ommits/e9752409ca66518172b46f132000dbf116fec7c1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T12:10:27Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T12:10:54Z","email":"jascha@tarnover.com","name":"Jascha"},"message":"clip-logger clipboard-stealer, Woodpecker +2, sequoia-engineering npm (June 7 2026)\n\nclip-logger PyPI clipboard-stealing crypto campaign (June 7 2026):\n- clip-logger 1.0.0–1.1.2 (8 versions; OSV MAL-2026-5293)\n- bittensor-burn-watch 1.2.0–1.3.4 (16 versions; OSV MAL-2026-5292)\nBoth periodically scan the clipboard for cryptocurrency secret-phrase\npatterns and exfiltrate matches to a hardcoded endpoint.\nDetected by kam193 / bad-packages.kam193.eu.\n\nWoodpecker PyPI campaign two additional packages (June 7 2026):\n- cmd2func 0.2.2, 0.2.3 (OSV MAL-2026-5290)\n- magique-ai 0.4.5 (OSV MAL-2026-5294)\nSame obfuscated Bun-runtime JS infostealer as the twelve packages\ndisclosed June 6; relates to the Mini Shai Hulud worm campaign.\nSources: OSV MAL-2026-5290/5294; bad-packages.kam193.eu/pypi/campaign/2026-06-compr-woodpecker\n\nsequoia-engineering npm malware (June 7 2026):\n- sequoia-engineering 2.2.2 (OSV MAL-2026-5291)\nCommunicates with a domain associated with malicious activity;\ndetected by OpenSSF Package Analysis.\n\nAutomatically updated every 4 hours 2026-06-07T12:10:27Z","tree":{"sha":"d800c74174030f023b75b8a55f79a003f3d87ce0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jaschadub/compromised-packages-check/git/trees/d800c74174030f023b75b8a55f79a003f3d87ce0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jaschadub/compromised-packages-check/git/commits/e9752409ca66518172b46f132000dbf116fec7c1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/768841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaschadub/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaschadub/fo