claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jaschadub/compromised-packages-check/commits/8c362c3a109e888f4f37ba9554f0e5bc51456593/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T04:18:44Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T04:19:06Z","email":"jascha@tarnover.com","name":"Jascha"},"message":"Add lightning PyPI 2.6.2/2.6.3 — same April 30 2026 campaign as pytorch-lightning\n\nThe `lightning` package (the unified Lightning AI distribution, distinct from\n`pytorch-lightning`) was compromised in the same 2026-04-compr-lightning\nmaintainer-credential attack that injected a Bun-runtime JavaScript infostealer\ninto both packages. Versions 2.6.2 and 2.6.3 were removed from PyPI; 2.6.1 is\nthe last clean release. `pytorch-lightning` was already tracked; this commit\ncloses the gap for its sibling package.\n\nPrimary sources:\n- https://osv.dev/vulnerability/MAL-2026-3201 (kam193/ossf)\n- https://github.com/Lightning-AI/pytorch-lightning/security/advisories/GHSA-w37p-236h-pfx3\n- https://socket.dev/blog/lightning-pypi-package-compromised\n- https://www.aikido.dev/blog/pytorch-lightning-pypi-compromise-mini-shai-hulud\n\nAutomatically updated every 4 hours 2026-06-07T04:18:35Z","tree":{"sha":"e603b06f3ac25f84a4fa98d251c2516b1a589c01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jaschadub/compromised-packages-check/git/trees/e603b06f3ac25f84a4fa98d251c2516b1a589c01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jaschadub/compromised-packages-check/git/commits/8c362c3a109e888f4f37ba9554f0e5bc51456593","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},