.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/commits/ebd31ecdcaa785440f0f3ff7e78e3186557a31f4","verification":{"payload":"tree ae760e90fd24ccb9bba374dfe38995ac944c6527\nparent 754ce9bfd26ebf2d5b3c8b62e59261520761bc2b\nparent ff167f016dffd44a355f000105e20f7d6d710b45\nauthor Klas Nyman <klas.nyman@telia.com> 1791129428 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791129428 +0200\n\nMerge pull request #2 from nymankla/feat/android-client\n\nAdd a .NET MAUI Android client and extract the shared API client","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwndUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2rIQAKHe0nAckv1RX2N6L6JPGG0v\nKaKQ2ZbMn9fVZlK/AQiWGndz7njCghYqpQGKtg/gq9eAjT9M/hUNXYQwnuTdALPG\nl5A/bP2dXo5rQcLRTLl3ieYfMUWqNNpMS7QbqyVxJ6EtlVSfvNt8iA2LptfbmSMK\noXecSvxG/6G39xxPT0w/KC3lD8ehNmyNOpUC20n2UQk6tej5yHsaMowKqZl741yg\nydMSivQmXm3lI4Wu2i9VPfp8/WYvxPsTPWplVUKmNlmsent3n/8aNWq0LKXiicx8\ncQejNI7k8iNH4V7qfOilbJWVK25fJbu5qJVQu6s1wwQgUsPOp1VJpoB+9ftViHZX\n6No2zoXRprHEIRbkak2Kvpl921Ec8wegQETcF3ynjcW0/Vq8skeEGChIADbiz7xz\n4Tg9oz4hwMh5YHLiG/h/igyPkEbDD3ohL+v9ndBJF/oEPbEN22TYjBSkecsBTyvv\nWo2BsNrX8hfXR1mEt/YeG3lGQHDO9/D6iarebNG7j08lknJiHt1jcMGvccEnoWUs\nq/LwqaRAPIFtwu6Gk9qJRsvhTjXnTCjAPPhmhRIg3kTwYEDBm0J52yrgoRB9B0E5\npiMFvZQYvYcJWs+Br1r40938k+RsmJAbqljo6sLzXCX8kYA0pX5MhPElZfI/CDrn\nadiunFk4G+R4a3H9Mt01\n=f7Er\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T15:57:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/ebd31ecdcaa785440f0f3ff7e78e3186557a31f4","node_id":"C_kwDOSjy22NoAKGViZDMxZWNkY2FhNzg1NDQwZjBmM2ZmN2U3OGUzMTg2NTU3YTMxZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/754ce9bfd26ebf2d5b3c8b62e59261520761bc2b","sha":"754ce9bfd26ebf2d5b3c8b62e59261520761bc2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/754ce9bfd26ebf2d5b3c8b62e59261520761bc2b"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/ff167f016dffd44a355f000105e20f7d6d710b45","sha":"ff167f016dffd44a355f000105e20f7d6d710b45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/ff167f016dffd44a355f000105e20f7d6d710b45"}],"sha":"ebd31ecdcaa785440f0f3ff7e78e3186557a31f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/ebd31ecdcaa785440f0f3ff7e78e3186557a31f4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/ff167f016dffd44a355f000105e20f7d6d710b45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:23:24Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:23:24Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"message":"Update the remaining outdated packages\n\nEverything NuGet reported as outdated, except two cases explained below.\n\nRuntime packages move 10.0.11 -> 10.0.12, which also lines them up with the EF\nCore version the Aspire 13.6.0 upgrade forced in the previous commit:\nMicrosoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi, Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Design,\nSystem.IO.Packaging, and the Microsoft.Extensions.* packages used by the mobile\nprojects.\n\naspire.ServiceDefaults moves Http.Resilience and ServiceDiscovery to 10.10.0 and\nthe OpenTelemetry packages to 1.19.x. Scalar.AspNetCore goes 2.17.2 -> 2.17.13.\nTest tooling moves to Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk 18.10.1, xunit.v3 4.0.1 and\ncoverlet.collector 10.1.0.\n\nTwo left alone deliberately:\n\n- Microsoft.Maui.Controls is reported as 10.0.20 -> 10.0.110, but the reference\n  is Version=\"$(MauiVersion)\" and that property resolves to 10.0.20 from the\n  installed maui-android workload. Pinning the package forward would leave it\n  mismatched against the workload''s packs. Moving MAUI means running\n  dotnet workload update, which changes the SDK installation rather than this\n  repository, so it is not done here.\n- The two Aspire Keycloak packages report \"Not found at the sources\" only\n  because they are prerelease and the check looks for a newer stable. They are\n  already on 13.6.0-preview, matching the rest of the Aspire packages.\n\nVerified: solution builds with only the pre-existing ASPIRE010 and CS8604\nwarnings, the mobile head builds clean in both Debug and Release — Release being\nthe trimmed, AOT-compiled one — and the suites are unchanged at 40 client\ncontract tests, 110 view model tests, and UnitTests with its one pre-existing\nInMemory failure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ae760e90fd24ccb9bba374dfe38995ac944c6527","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/trees/ae760e90fd24ccb9bba374dfe38995ac944c6527"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/commits/ff167f016dffd44a355f000105e20f7d6d710b45","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/ff167f016dffd44a355f000105e20f7d6d710b45","node_id":"C_kwDOSjy22NoAKGZmMTY3ZjAxNmRmZmQ0NGEzNTVmMDAwMTA1ZTIwZjdkNmQ3MTBiNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/1bba2be35a768564253aad4a459d8aa82dda855a","sha":"1bba2be35a768564253aad4a459d8aa82dda855a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/1bba2be35a768564253aad4a459d8aa82dda855a"}],"sha":"ff167f016dffd44a355f000105e20f7d6d710b45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/ff167f016dffd44a355f000105e20f7d6d710b45"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/1bba2be35a768564253aad4a459d8aa82dda855a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:16:27Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:16:27Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"message":"Update Aspire to 13.6.0 and realign the EF Core pins\n\nThe Aspire package bumps were already in the working tree — the AppHost SDK and\nthe hosting, Keycloak, Redis, PostgreSQL and Redis output-caching packages all\nmoved from 13.5.3 to 13.6.0. They did not build.\n\nAspire.Npgsql.EntityFrameworkCore.PostgreSQL 13.6.0 pulls\nMicrosoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational 10.0.12 transitively, while Tests and\nUnitTests pinned it to 10.0.11, so both failed restore with NU1605 package\ndowngrade errors. Those pins move to 10.0.12.\n\nTests had also been left on Aspire.Hosting.Testing 13.5.3 while the AppHost SDK\nit loads moved to 13.6.0; that is now aligned too.\n\nThe comments on those pins claimed they existed to force 10.0.9 because Aspire\npulled 10.0.8 — both numbers were already wrong before this change. They now say\nwhat the pin is actually for: matching whatever the health-checks package brings\nin transitively, which has to be revisited whenever the Aspire packages move.\n\nBuilds clean and the test suites are unchanged: 40 client contract tests, 110\nview model tests, and UnitTests with its one pre-existing failure\n(CreateAsync_ReturnsValidationError_ForDuplicateMemberYear, which cannot pass\nagainst EF Core InMemory because that provider does not enforce unique indexes).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef0046795d4d7cfdb55ade038b847bb91d492d86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/trees/ef0046795d4d7cfdb55ade038b847bb91d492d86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/commits/1bba2be35a768564253aad4a459d8aa82dda855a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/1bba2be35a768564253aad4a459d8aa82dda855a","node_id":"C_kwDOSjy22NoAKDFiYmEyYmUzNWE3Njg1NjQyNTNhYWQ0YTQ1OWQ4YWE4MmRkYTg1NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/77419e51a2a0bbc261cd301e5de960e894df7967","sha":"77419e51a2a0bbc261cd301e5de960e894df7967","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/77419e51a2a0bbc261cd301e5de960e894df7967"}],"sha":"1bba2be35a768564253aad4a459d8aa82dda855a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/1bba2be35a768564253aad4a459d8aa82dda855a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/77419e51a2a0bbc261cd301e5de960e894df7967/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T14:38:33Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T14:38:33Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"message":"Harden the Android client for Release builds\n\nRelease builds trim and AOT-compile, and the failures that causes appear only\nthere and only at runtime. This closes that gap and verifies it on a device.\n\nArcheryJsonContext supplies source-generated serialization metadata for every\nwire type, and ArcheryApiClient now passes a JsonTypeInfo on every call instead\nof using the reflection-based System.Net.Http.Json overloads. With that done the\ntrim analyzer is switched back on in Archery.Client — it was parked in the\nextraction commit precisely until this work — and the project builds clean with\nIsTrimmable and IsAotCompatible set. A future call that reaches for a\nreflection-based overload is now a desktop build warning rather than a silent\nRelease-only failure.\n\nThe generated options reproduce JsonSerializerDefaults.Web, which is what\nSystem.Net.Http.Json applied implicitly before. The 40 contract tests pass\nunchanged, which is what proves the wire format did not move: camelCase names,\ninteger enums, ISO dates and no computed display properties. That is exactly\nwhat those tests were written for.\n\nThe cleartext exemption can no longer ship. The base manifest no longer declares\nnetworkSecurityConfig; a Debug-only manifest overlay adds it, and the config it\npoints at is dropped from every other configuration. Verified by inspecting both\nmerged manifests: present in Debug, absent in Release.\n\nThat left no way to exercise a trimmed build against the local HTTP stack, so\nArcheryReleaseSmokeTest=true re-adds it for that purpose, documented as a test\nharness that must never be set for a package that leaves the machine.\n\nVerified with exactly that: a Release APK, trimmed and AOT-compiled, installed\non the emulator. Keycloak sign-in, the dashboard with its nested stats, enums,\ndates and decimals, and the member list all load correctly, with no crash and no\ntrimming or AOT failure in logcat.\n\nAlso replaces the obsolete Page.DisplayAlert calls with DisplayAlertAsync, and\nmodels the guest club filter with a real \"All clubs\" sentinel instead of a null\nelement — null rendered as a blank picker row and put the collection at odds\nwith what compiled XAML bindings expect.\n\nStill not ready to ship, and noted in MauiProgram: there is only one settings\nfile, so a Release build still points at the development stack. Production needs\nits own appsettings with real HTTPS endpoints, plus signing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6608c6a7bd07e82a328200c5235ecbf9e710efe9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/trees/6608c6a7bd07e82a328200c5235ecbf9e710efe9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/commits/77419e51a2a0bbc261cd301e5de960e894df7967","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/77419e51a2a0bbc261cd301e5de960e894df7967","node_id":"C_kwDOSjy22NoAKDc3NDE5ZTUxYTJhMGJiYzI2MWNkMzAxZTVkZTk2MGU4OTRkZjc5Njc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/17315bac39e704ac90d78077b836a994eaf441b5","sha":"17315bac39e704ac90d78077b836a994eaf441b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/17315bac39e704ac90d78077b836a994eaf441b5"}],"sha":"77419e51a2a0bbc261cd301e5de960e894df7967","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/77419e51a2a0bbc261cd301e5de960e894df7967"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/17315bac39e704ac90d78077b836a994eaf441b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:24:39Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:24:39Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"message":"Add the dashboard and make it the landing screen\n\nOne read-only call on launch, then stat tiles, a meter, the next competition,\ntop scorers and recent competitions. Sign-in and session restore now land here\ninstead of on the member list. 12 new view model tests, 110 in the suite.\n\nVerified on the emulator against the running stack: the numbers match the web\ndashboard exactly — 117 active members, 57 800 kr collected, 98% collection\nrate, 13 competitions.\n\nDeliberately not charts. A handful of headline numbers is a row of stat tiles\nrather than a grouped bar chart, and the collection rate is a single ratio\nagainst a limit, so it is a meter on a same-hue track rather than a two-slice\npie. The lists are short tables. Values wear ink colours and the accent is\ncarried by the marks, so no number depends on its colour to be read.\n\nCollectionRate is clamped to 0..1 before it reaches the meter, so a server-side\npercentage outside that range cannot make the bar overflow its track.\n\nTiles double as navigation into their sections, and the screen ends with a\nshortcut to recording training attendance, which is the most common thing\nanyone opens this app to do.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8a0844e6d689f602f2fb7ceb3e2e20fbed413746","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/trees/8a0844e6d689f602f2fb7ceb3e2e20fbed413746"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/commits/17315bac39e704ac90d78077b836a994eaf441b5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/17315bac39e704ac90d78077b836a994eaf441b5","node_id":"C_kwDOSjy22NoAKDE3MzE1YmFjMzllNzA0YWM5MGQ3ODA3N2I4MzZhOTk0ZWFmNDQxYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/3b5892b2d432e0c6ca15ae760259051fa98b8a0e","sha":"3b5892b2d432e0c6ca15ae760259051fa98b8a0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/3b5892b2d432e0c6ca15ae760259051fa98b8a0e"}],"sha":"17315bac39e704ac90d78077b836a994eaf441b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/17315bac39e704ac90d78077b836a994eaf441b5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/3b5892b2d432e0c6ca15ae760259051fa98b8a0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:17:17Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:17:17Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"message":"Add external participants to the Android client\n\nGuests list with search, a club filter and add/edit/delete, reachable from the\nflyout. 13 new view model tests, 98 in the suite. Verified on the emulator:\nthe list renders with club affiliations and the edit form loads an existing\nguest.\n\nThe club filter is derived from the data rather than fixed, because there is no\nclub entity to enumerate. Reloading keeps the chosen club if it still exists and\nfalls back to \"all\" if it does not — deleting the last guest of a club would\notherwise leave the picker pointing at something gone, showing an empty list\nwith no obvious way back.\n\nThere is no GET by id for external participants, so the edit form picks its\nsubject out of the list.\n\nThis completes the fee scope decided at planning: member fees are viewed and\nmarked paid from member detail, while the year-wide fee matrix and the bulk\ncreation run stay on the web as desk work.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"df5d7b548952c0341c0b002b96210742d0c0eb7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/trees/df5d7b548952c0341c0b002b96210742d0c0eb7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/commits/3b5892b2d432e0c6ca15ae760259051fa98b8a0e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/3b5892b2d432e0c6ca15ae760259051fa98b8a0e","node_id":"C_kwDOSjy22NoAKDNiNTg5MmIyZDQzMmUwYzZjYTE1YWU3NjAyNTkwNTFmYTk4YjhhMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/7a918acdf06091b9dd9ab443b01731eb23de7ed1","sha":"7a918acdf06091b9dd9ab443b01731eb23de7ed1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/7a918acdf06091b9dd9ab443b01731eb23de7ed1"}],"sha":"3b5892b2d432e0c6ca15ae760259051fa98b8a0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/3b5892b2d432e0c6ca15ae760259051fa98b8a0e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/7a918acdf06091b9dd9ab443b01731eb23de7ed1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:02:27Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:02:27Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"message":"Add competitions, participants and results to the Android client\n\nCompetitions list and edit, a detail screen with Participants and Results tabs,\nparticipant registration and result entry. 35 new view model tests, 85 in the\nsuite.\n\nVerified on the emulator: opened a competition, switched tabs, scored a\nregistered archer from the participants list, saw the result appear in order,\nand deleted it again.\n\nThe rule that shaped both forms: a participant and a result each belong to\nexactly one of a member or an external participant, enforced by the\nCK_*_SingleParticipant check constraints. Rather than holding two nullable ids\nand nulling one before posting, the forms offer a single member-or-guest\nchoice, so an invalid combination cannot be expressed at all; switching the\nchoice clears the previous pick. Registration also hides archers who are\nalready entered, which removes the commonest rejected save.\n\nResults sort by score descending, then X count. Placement cannot be the primary\nsort because it is only set once somebody assigns it. \"Score\" on a registration\nopens the result form pre-filled with that archer''s bow class, age class and\ngender, so the scorer confirms what was entered at sign-on instead of retyping\nit. Editing an existing result locks the archer: reassigning a recorded score is\na different operation and could collide with that archer''s own result.\n\nScore fields are bound as strings and parsed against the current and invariant\ncultures. The app runs under sv-SE, and an Entry bound straight to an int\nsilently discards anything the current culture cannot parse.\n\nFixes a crash, and a latent one. Shell applies [QueryProperty] by calling\nConvert.ChangeType, and Guid does not implement IConvertible — so passing a Guid\nto a Guid? query property throws \"Object must implement IConvertible\" and takes\nthe process down. That killed the app on opening the result form from a\nregistration, and MemberEditPage had the same defect waiting: it had only ever\nbeen opened from Add, which passes no parameters, never from Edit on a detail\npage. Every page that takes parameters now implements IQueryAttributable and\nreads the dictionary directly, which removes the conversion step entirely.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9345487fe41062b9ddc9d2c7acd379de8d1289e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/trees/9345487fe41062b9ddc9d2c7acd379de8d1289e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/commits/7a918acdf06091b9dd9ab443b01731eb23de7ed1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/7a918acdf06091b9dd9ab443b01731eb23de7ed1","node_id":"C_kwDOSjy22NoAKDdhOTE4YWNkZjA2MDkxYjlkZDlhYjQ0M2IwMTczMWViMjNkZTdlZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/dd3e27f6015212a3927622d520c84c25c449a390","sha":"dd3e27f6015212a3927622d520c84c25c449a390","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/dd3e27f6015212a3927622d520c84c25c449a390"}],"sha":"7a918acdf06091b9dd9ab443b01731eb23de7ed1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/7a918acdf06091b9dd9ab443b01731eb23de7ed1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/dd3e27f6015212a3927622d520c84c25c449a390/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T22:38:15Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T22:38:15Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"message":"Add training attendance and history to the Android client\n\nThe at-the-range roll call, which is the reason this app exists: pick a date,\ntick who turned up, add a note, save. Plus a history screen for looking a past\nsession up. 19 new view model tests, 50 in the suite.\n\nVerified on the emulator against the running stack: ticked two members and a\nguest, saved, and confirmed the session on the history screen and in the\ndatabase.\n\nSelection lives on stable AttendeeRow objects rather than on the filtered\ncollection. That is what makes the important case work: tick someone, search\nfor someone else, and save — the hidden-but-ticked people are still sent. Save\nis a full replace of the attendee list for the date, not a delta, so it has to\nsubmit every ticked row rather than only the visible ones. Both are covered by\ntests, and the behaviour was re-checked by hand on the device because getting\nit wrong silently drops attendees rather than failing.\n\nThe attendance screen keeps the date, the running total and Save fixed while\nonly the two lists scroll, and the whole row is the hit target rather than just\nthe checkbox — it is tapped repeatedly and quickly while standing at the range.\n\nThe no-session response shape is handled explicitly: the endpoint answers with\nsessionId null and no attendees for a date nothing has been recorded against,\nrather than 404.\n\nFixes a bug the tests caught in TrainingHistoryViewModel: the newest date is\nselected automatically after loading the date list, but doing that through the\nOnSelectedDateChanged handler routed into RunAsync, which refuses to re-enter\nwhile IsBusy — and IsBusy was already true because the load was still running.\nThe auto-selected date therefore showed no attendees at all. The detail is now\nawaited directly, with a flag so the handler stands down.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d2e0f8c8b619b81c2e23fc93456cab4515281cb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/trees/d2e0f8c8b619b81c2e23fc93456cab4515281cb4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/commits/dd3e27f6015212a3927622d520c84c25c449a390","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/dd3e27f6015212a3927622d520c84c25c449a390","node_id":"C_kwDOSjy22NoAKGRkM2UyN2Y2MDE1MjEyYTM5Mjc2MjJkNTIwYzg0YzI1YzQ0OWEzOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/a26446c7e678818160e531f31fb70268f0a274a8","sha":"a26446c7e678818160e531f31fb70268f0a274a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/a26446c7e678818160e531f31fb70268f0a274a8"}],"sha":"dd3e27f6015212a3927622d520c84c25c449a390","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/dd3e27f6015212a3927622d520c84c25c449a390"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/a26446c7e678818160e531f31fb70268f0a274a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T22:27:18Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T22:27:18Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"message":"Add member CRUD to the Android client\n\nMembers list, detail and edit, with 31 view model tests. Verified on the\nemulator: created a member from the phone (153 -> 154), opened its detail,\nswipe-deleted it with confirmation, and checked the server was back to 153.\n\nThe list gains search, an active-only toggle, bow-class and sort pickers, a\ncount summary, pull to refresh, tap to open and swipe to delete. Sorting is an\nenum bound to a picker rather than the web app''s SortState/SortableHeader pair,\nwhich depends on clickable column headers a phone does not have.\n\nMember detail shows the profile and that member''s fees with a one-tap \"mark\npaid\", matching the web app''s action. The button is hidden on a fee that is\nalready paid: the view model refuses to act on one, and offering an action that\nsilently does nothing is worse than not offering it.\n\nValidation on the edit form is deliberately thin — required names, no future\nbirth date, no join date before birth. The API validates little beyond the\npersonnummer, so these only avoid an obviously doomed round trip; the\npersonnummer checksum is left to the server rather than reimplementing\nPersonnummerParser here, where it would drift. Anything the server rejects is\nshown from its own response.\n\nErrorBanner replaces the error markup that was being repeated per page, so\n\"cannot reach the server\" looks and behaves the same everywhere.\n\nAppShell now subscribes to IAuthService.SessionEnded. That event already fired\nwhen a refresh failed, but nothing listened, so an expired refresh token left\nthe user on a screen that could only ever report the expiry with no route back\nto signing in.\n\nAll 31 view model tests run without an emulator, which is the point of keeping\nview models in Archery.Mobile.Core.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"26d7d58672c7998a6c8bb15ae69d462c0bfbe5b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/trees/26d7d58672c7998a6c8bb15ae69d462c0bfbe5b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/commits/a26446c7e678818160e531f31fb70268f0a274a8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/a26446c7e678818160e531f31fb70268f0a274a8","node_id":"C_kwDOSjy22NoAKGEyNjQ0NmM3ZTY3ODgxODE2MGU1MzFmMzFmYjcwMjY4ZjBhMjc0YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/809efc9c4d5948ddbd970267714e1b22ce1ce94f","sha":"809efc9c4d5948ddbd970267714e1b22ce1ce94f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/809efc9c4d5948ddbd970267714e1b22ce1ce94f"}],"sha":"a26446c7e678818160e531f31fb70268f0a274a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/a26446c7e678818160e531f31fb70268f0a274a8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/809efc9c4d5948ddbd970267714e1b22ce1ce94f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T20:42:48Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T20:42:48Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"message":"Add the MAUI Android client with a working Keycloak sign-in\n\nFirst running mobile code: sign in through Keycloak and list members from the\nAPI. Verified on an emulator end to end — Chrome Custom Tab, custom-scheme\nredirect, token exchange, member list over 10.0.2.2, and session restore across\nan app restart with no second sign-in.\n\nTwo projects rather than one. Archery.Mobile.Core is a plain net10.0 library\nholding every view model, reaching the platform only through the interfaces in\nAbstractions/. That is what makes view models unit testable: dotnet test cannot\nrun a net10.0-android assembly, and a net10.0 test project cannot reference one.\nIt is also the iOS story — adding a head becomes one target framework plus\nPlatforms/iOS, with no view model touched.\n\nArchery.Mobile is the Android head: OidcClient driving MAUI''s WebAuthenticator,\nSecureStorage for tokens, Shell navigation, and the login and members pages.\nArcheryAuthService implements both IAuthService and the shared\nIArcheryTokenProvider, so the extracted ArcheryApiClient gets its bearer token\nwithout knowing anything about mobile. Refresh is proactive with a five-minute\nskew rather than a retry-on-401 handler, which would mean resending a request\nwhose content has already been consumed.\n\nArchery.Mobile is deliberately excluded from the solution build configurations\n(no Build.0 entries). A net10.0-android project makes dotnet build fail with\nNETSDK1147 wherever the MAUI workload is absent, including most CI agents, and\nTests references the AppHost so the requirement would spread into dotnet test.\nBuild the app explicitly with -f net10.0-android. It is not added to the AppHost\nfor the same reason.\n\nThree things that cost real time, now documented in CLAUDE.md:\n\n- Discovery refuses a plain-HTTP authority. DiscoveryPolicy.AllowHttpOnLoopback\n  exempts localhost, but the emulator reaches the host as 10.0.2.2, which is not\n  loopback from the device''s point of view, so the relaxation must be explicit\n  and is scoped to http authorities only.\n- A user imported without \"realmRoles\" gets no realm roles at all, and\n  offline_access then fails the token exchange with \"Offline tokens not allowed\n  for the user or client\" — it is a realm role as well as a client scope. The\n  web app never hit this because it does not request that scope.\n- MAUI defines its own IBrowser, which collides with OidcClient''s.\n\nDebug builds now show the underlying reason in the sign-in error. Diagnosing an\nOIDC failure from a generic message means guessing, and on a device the logger\noutput is not readily visible.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fc210bd72ac31f3fc846a2fbe0c54bb25b1a662f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/trees/fc210bd72ac31f3fc846a2fbe0c54bb25b1a662f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/commits/809efc9c4d5948ddbd970267714e1b22ce1ce94f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/809efc9c4d5948ddbd970267714e1b22ce1ce94f","node_id":"C_kwDOSjy22NoAKDgwOWVmYzljNGQ1OTQ4ZGRiZDk3MDI2NzcxNGUxYjIyY2UxY2U5NGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/eee6eca5b63252f16b7a54f70418a72fd8d04dbf","sha":"eee6eca5b63252f16b7a54f70418a72fd8d04dbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/eee6eca5b63252f16b7a54f70418a72fd8d04dbf"}],"sha":"809efc9c4d5948ddbd970267714e1b22ce1ce94f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/809efc9c4d5948ddbd970267714e1b22ce1ce94f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/eee6eca5b63252f16b7a54f70418a72fd8d04dbf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:42:51Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:42:51Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"message":"Make the API and Keycloak reachable from an Android emulator\n\nPrepares the infrastructure a .NET MAUI client needs, with no mobile code yet.\nVerified end to end by simulating the app''s OIDC flow: authorization code +\nPKCE against the new public client with Host: 10.0.2.2:8081, token exchange,\nthen a call to the API with the resulting token, which returned 200.\n\nAppHost:\n\n- apiservice gets WithExternalHttpEndpoints(). A device cannot use Aspire\n  service discovery, so unlike the Blazor frontend it needs a real address.\n- Keycloak gets a second, development-only HTTP endpoint on port 8081.\n  Aspire publishes only Keycloak''s HTTPS endpoint (host 8080 -> container\n  8443) behind a self-signed certificate, and Android will not trust it; there\n  was no HTTP endpoint to fall back to, so the emulator could not have signed\n  in at all.\n\nKeycloak realm:\n\n- Adds the archerymobile client: public, PKCE S256 required, direct access\n  grants off, custom-scheme redirect URIs, and its own copy of the\n  archery-api-audience mapper. Without that mapper the API rejects its tokens,\n  because the realm has no client scope carrying the audience. The existing\n  archeryweb client cannot be reused: an APK cannot keep its secret.\n- defaultClientScopes is listed explicitly. Supplying optionalClientScopes\n  alone leaves a client with no default scopes, and authorization then fails\n  with invalid_scope for \"openid profile email\".\n\nAPI:\n\n- Keycloak:AdditionalValidIssuers, development only. Keycloak stamps \"iss\"\n  from the Host header of the token request, so a token obtained via 10.0.2.2\n  carries a different issuer than the discovery document the API reads, and\n  validation fails with IDX10205 — which surfaces as a bare 401 with an empty\n  body. These are added to, not substituted for, the metadata issuer; the web\n  app was re-tested and still signs in and loads data.\n- UseHttpsRedirection is now skipped in development, so plain HTTP from the\n  emulator is not bounced to a certificate it cannot validate. The frontend\n  reaches the API over HTTPS through service discovery either way.\n\nCLAUDE.md records the two traps: that realm JSON edits do not reach an\nexisting environment because the keycloakdata volume is persistent and import\nonly runs against an empty store, and that the API never returns 409 —\nConflictException is declared but never thrown, and conflicts come back as 400.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"db83a42257e0cf5095094f07b56c97150c1f0800","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/trees/db83a42257e0cf5095094f07b56c97150c1f0800"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/commits/eee6eca5b63252f16b7a54f70418a72fd8d04dbf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/eee6eca5b63252f16b7a54f70418a72fd8d04dbf","node_id":"C_kwDOSjy22NoAKGVlZTZlY2E1YjYzMjUyZjE2YjdhNTRmNzA0MThhNzJmZDhkMDRkYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/a48bfaafd75db2da0bc48452706f3c06e25e7b0c","sha":"a48bfaafd75db2da0bc48452706f3c06e25e7b0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/a48bfaafd75db2da0bc48452706f3c06e25e7b0c"}],"sha":"eee6eca5b63252f16b7a54f70418a72fd8d04dbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/eee6eca5b63252f16b7a54f70418a72fd8d04dbf"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/a48bfaafd75db2da0bc48452706f3c06e25e7b0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:30:15Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:30:15Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"message":"Stop tracking ASP.NET Core data-protection keys\n\naspire.Web persists its data-protection keys to .dp-keys so auth cookies stay\nreadable across restarts. That directory was not ignored, so a key generated\nby running the app locally was committed in 6bd0f9b and has been tracked ever\nsince, and every clone has been sharing it.\n\nThose keys sign and encrypt the auth cookies, so they are per-machine secrets\nand do not belong in the repo. Ignore the directory and untrack the key. The\nfiles stay on disk, so local sessions are unaffected; other machines will\ngenerate their own on first run and existing cookies there become unreadable,\nwhich just means signing in again.\n\nNot purged from history: it is a development-only key, and the realm config\nalready carries a committed client secret. Rotating both is worth doing before\nanything is deployed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d8c0e7226e00ba7d6a0544dcd60fe79880b768bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/trees/d8c0e7226e00ba7d6a0544dcd60fe79880b768bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/commits/a48bfaafd75db2da0bc48452706f3c06e25e7b0c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/a48bfaafd75db2da0bc48452706f3c06e25e7b0c","node_id":"C_kwDOSjy22NoAKGE0OGJmYWFmZDc1ZGIyZGEwYmM0ODQ1MjcwNmYzYzA2ZTI1ZTdiMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/494779986a5ad9b369f370bbd3e58483dfdc1d6b","sha":"494779986a5ad9b369f370bbd3e58483dfdc1d6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/494779986a5ad9b369f370bbd3e58483dfdc1d6b"}],"sha":"a48bfaafd75db2da0bc48452706f3c06e25e7b0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/a48bfaafd75db2da0bc48452706f3c06e25e7b0c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/494779986a5ad9b369f370bbd3e58483dfdc1d6b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:24:25Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:24:25Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"message":"Extract Archery.Client so the API client can be shared with a mobile head\n\nMoves ArcheryApiClient and the wire models out of aspire.Web into a new\nnet10.0 library with no ASP.NET dependency, in preparation for a .NET MAUI\nAndroid client. The client''s only coupling to the web host was its\nconstructor and AddBearerToken; both are replaced by an IArcheryTokenProvider\nabstraction, which aspire.Web implements in WebArcheryTokenProvider keeping\nthe SSR-prerender fallback verbatim.\n\nAlso added to the shared library:\n\n- ArcheryApiErrors, one normaliser for the four error envelopes the API\n  emits. The ReadValidationErrorsAsync helper copy-pasted into three pages\n  deserialises ProblemDetails'' \"errors\" into a List<string>, but\n  ProblemDetails returns a dictionary keyed by field, so it threw and showed\n  \"Failed to parse server validation response\" instead of the real error.\n  The shared version reads the body once and probes it with JsonDocument.\n  The three copies are left in place; collapsing them is a separate change.\n- ArcheryApiException, deriving from HttpRequestException so the existing\n  catch sites still work now that EnsureSuccessStatusCode is gone.\n- IArcheryApiClient, so view models can later be tested without an\n  HttpMessageHandler.\n- [JsonIgnore] on the five computed display properties, which were being\n  serialised into request bodies.\n\naspire.Web needs only a project reference, a <Using> item, one line in\n_Imports.razor and one DI registration; no page or component changed. The\ndead BearerTokenHandler, registered nowhere, is deleted.\n\nArchery.Client.Tests covers routes and verbs, culture-independent DateOnly\nquery formatting, bearer attachment, the integer-enum wire format, and every\nerror envelope including the no-session training-attendance response.\n\nVerified against the running stack: Keycloak sign-in, Members, Dashboard,\nCompetitions, competition detail, Training Attendance, Fees, and a\ncreate-then-delete member round trip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8fbb83d3fe4aeb363524e545dc2f6ff89fb544f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/trees/8fbb83d3fe4aeb363524e545dc2f6ff89fb544f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/commits/494779986a5ad9b369f370bbd3e58483dfdc1d6b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/494779986a5ad9b369f370bbd3e58483dfdc1d6b","node_id":"C_kwDOSjy22NoAKDQ5NDc3OTk4NmE1YWQ5YjM2OWYzNzBiYmQzZTU4NDgzZGZkYzFkNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/754ce9bfd26ebf2d5b3c8b62e59261520761bc2b","sha":"754ce9bfd26ebf2d5b3c8b62e59261520761bc2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/754ce9bfd26ebf2d5b3c8b62e59261520761bc2b"}],"sha":"494779986a5ad9b369f370bbd3e58483dfdc1d6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/494779986a5ad9b369f370bbd3e58483dfdc1d6b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/754ce9bfd26ebf2d5b3c8b62e59261520761bc2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T08:57:39Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T08:57:39Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"message":"Add Keycloak database setup and update Docker configuration for production","tree":{"sha":"7a502ff9335d42e570593b9a853717d4bc4130ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/trees/7a502ff9335d42e570593b9a853717d4bc4130ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/commits/754ce9bfd26ebf2d5b3c8b62e59261520761bc2b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/754ce9bfd26ebf2d5b3c8b62e59261520761bc2b","node_id":"C_kwDOSjy22NoAKDc1NGNlOWJmZDI2ZWJmMmQ1YjNjOGI2MmU1OTI2MTUyMDc2MWJjMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/59c6b2acdde1e18ccfe92e96fbf4c5d03a64a281","sha":"59c6b2acdde1e18ccfe92e96fbf4c5d03a64a281","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/59c6b2acdde1e18ccfe92e96fbf4c5d03a64a281"}],"sha":"754ce9bfd26ebf2d5b3c8b62e59261520761bc2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/754ce9bfd26ebf2d5b3c8b62e59261520761bc2b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/commits/59c6b2acdde1e18ccfe92e96fbf4c5d03a64a281/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T08:31:02Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T08:31:02Z","email":"nymankla@gmail.com","name":"Klas Nyman"},"message":"Update package references to version 13.5.3 for Aspire libraries and OpenTelemetry","tree":{"sha":"0d62d8448caa4faba6a781a8f574b58eb18e8867","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/trees/0d62d8448caa4faba6a781a8f574b58eb18e8867"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nymankla/archery/git/commits/59c6b2acdde1e18ccfe92e96fbf4c5d03a64a281","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/59c6b2acdde1e18ccfe92e96fbf4c5d03a64a281","node_id":"C_kwDOSjy22NoAKDU5YzZiMmFjZGRlMWUxOGNjZmU5MmU5NmZiZjRjNWQwM2E2NGEyODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nymankla/archery/commit/d555566