users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/e44bf0cf9fe53208a027da57a7a6af2a249c9850/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T20:28:37Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T20:28:37Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"message":"docs: API_LIST.md reference + Phase K/J execution order\n\nAdds API_LIST.md as the authoritative quick reference for every HTTP\nendpoint exposed by server/server.js (method, path, source location,\nrequest/response shape, error codes), with a template for new entries.\nCLAUDE.md now instructs every session to update API_LIST.md in lockstep\nwith any route change.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md \"Where we are\" reorders Phase K above Phase J\nto reflect recommended execution order — Reddit copy is the immediate\ndistribution channel, RSS compounds with archive depth. Letter\nassignments preserved to avoid commit-history churn.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e061d5f8949820b46b72934d3e5ece0049e27ffe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/trees/e061d5f8949820b46b72934d3e5ece0049e27ffe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/commits/e44bf0cf9fe53208a027da57a7a6af2a249c9850","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/e44bf0cf9fe53208a027da57a7a6af2a249c9850","node_id":"C_kwDOSj6oLtoAKGU0NGJmMGNmOWZlNTMyMDhhMDI3ZGE1N2E3YTZhZjJhMjQ5Yzk4NTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/9eedd08e9a3c6bbd119a4cb94cbcffab5e2b9e77","sha":"9eedd08e9a3c6bbd119a4cb94cbcffab5e2b9e77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/9eedd08e9a3c6bbd119a4cb94cbcffab5e2b9e77"}],"sha":"e44bf0cf9fe53208a027da57a7a6af2a249c9850","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/e44bf0cf9fe53208a027da57a7a6af2a249c9850"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/9eedd08e9a3c6bbd119a4cb94cbcffab5e2b9e77/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T20:19:10Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T20:19:10Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"message":"Source-fidelity guard: reject hits where URL slug does not match headline\n\nPhase I''s first audited draft surfaced 3-4 fabricated URL/headline\npairings out of 10 curated hits (30-40%): an ANN weekly-release\ncalendar cited as the source for a Netflix/NHK licensing deal,\na wrong-show URL attached to a Made in Abyss headline, etc. The\nmodel was attaching URLs from one search result to headlines whose\ncontent came from a different result within the same batch.\n\nurlHeadlineMatchInfo tokenizes URL pathname and headline, drops\nstopwords + short tokens + pure-numeric + 4-digit years, applies a\nsimple plural stem, and counts shared significant tokens.\nhitRejectionReason now rejects any hit with fewer than 2 shared as\nurl-headline-mismatch:shared=<n>. Threshold tuned against the\n2026-05-23 audit: 5 known-good hits pass (3-7 shared), 4 known-bad\nhits fail (0-1 shared). Validates at parse time so bad hits never\nreach Curate.\n\nCompanion prompt tightening adds a Source Fidelity section to\nsearch-system.md with both observed failure modes as named BAD\nexamples. Re-running the pipeline produced 7/7 matching URL/headline\npairings (vs 6/10 before the guard), confirming the layered defense.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f8b7ece972ac32c359d2a8f00976574bb0870890","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/trees/f8b7ece972ac32c359d2a8f00976574bb0870890"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/commits/9eedd08e9a3c6bbd119a4cb94cbcffab5e2b9e77","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/9eedd08e9a3c6bbd119a4cb94cbcffab5e2b9e77","node_id":"C_kwDOSj6oLtoAKDllZWRkMDhlOWEzYzZiYmQxMTlhNGNiOTRjYmNmZmFiNWUyYjllNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/6818e2177701d47d565edbc883a02a6d68871771","sha":"6818e2177701d47d565edbc883a02a6d68871771","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/6818e2177701d47d565edbc883a02a6d68871771"}],"sha":"9eedd08e9a3c6bbd119a4cb94cbcffab5e2b9e77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/9eedd08e9a3c6bbd119a4cb94cbcffab5e2b9e77"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/6818e2177701d47d565edbc883a02a6d68871771/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T20:18:38Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T20:18:38Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"message":"Phase I: localhost newsletter render + typography\n\nAdds two public-facing routes under React Router:\n- /newsletter/:id renders the published markdown via markdown-it inside\n  a Tailwind Typography prose container at publication-grade dark mode\n- /newsletter is the index listing all published issues\n\nDynamic in-issue table of contents at desktop widths, generated from\nH2 anchors via markdown-it-anchor. External links open in new tabs;\ninternal anchors (TOC) stay in-page. App.jsx is now a thin BrowserRouter\nshell delegating to pages/EditorPage.jsx for the existing editor view.\n\nTypography refinements (src/styles/newsletter.css) push past Tailwind\nTypography defaults for sustained reading: constrain to max-w-prose\n(~65ch), soften body to #c2c2c8 to reduce halation against pure black,\nbump line-height to 1.8. Friendly date format (\"May 23, 2026\") in the\nH1 via a shared formatWeekOf helper.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bef37a311253b5f5863ce6b90f7d7bc2ea1f729f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/trees/bef37a311253b5f5863ce6b90f7d7bc2ea1f729f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/commits/6818e2177701d47d565edbc883a02a6d68871771","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/6818e2177701d47d565edbc883a02a6d68871771","node_id":"C_kwDOSj6oLtoAKDY4MThlMjE3NzcwMWQ0N2Q1NjVlZGJjODgzYTAyYTZkNjg4NzE3NzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/75a28be603c505a9e709bcd44dcb0de6d681c34d","sha":"75a28be603c505a9e709bcd44dcb0de6d681c34d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/75a28be603c505a9e709bcd44dcb0de6d681c34d"}],"sha":"6818e2177701d47d565edbc883a02a6d68871771","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/6818e2177701d47d565edbc883a02a6d68871771"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/75a28be603c505a9e709bcd44dcb0de6d681c34d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T16:38:04Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T16:38:04Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"message":"Phase H: publish workflow + Vitest test framework\n\nAdds the missing \"publish\" step that closes the gap between the engineering\nrecord (drafts/<id>.json) and the editorial record. Each publish writes\npublished/<id>.md (pure markdown, editable in any tool) plus an index.json\nmetadata array. Idempotent — re-publishing overwrites both. Wires the\n\"Mark as published\" / \"Re-publish\" button into ReviewUI and surfaces\npublished status via a green Send badge in the Sidebar.\n\nLands Vitest 2.x (pinned for Vite 5 compatibility) with 14 tests across\ntest/published.test.js + test/publish-flow.test.js, including a UTF-8\nround-trip guard for the em-dash and \"Manga → Anime\" arrow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3132b7dd140886faa0abf38ee6bd2a0336b6754f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/trees/3132b7dd140886faa0abf38ee6bd2a0336b6754f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/commits/75a28be603c505a9e709bcd44dcb0de6d681c34d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/75a28be603c505a9e709bcd44dcb0de6d681c34d","node_id":"C_kwDOSj6oLtoAKDc1YTI4YmU2MDNjNTA1YTllNzA5YmNkNDRkY2IwZGU2ZDY4MWMzNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/d11af7c394e34e4d8c8cd19e5b049f1eaeab07ef","sha":"d11af7c394e34e4d8c8cd19e5b049f1eaeab07ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/d11af7c394e34e4d8c8cd19e5b049f1eaeab07ef"}],"sha":"75a28be603c505a9e709bcd44dcb0de6d681c34d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/75a28be603c505a9e709bcd44dcb0de6d681c34d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/d11af7c394e34e4d8c8cd19e5b049f1eaeab07ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T04:59:41Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T04:59:41Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"message":"Phase G: scheduled task wrapper + MVP achieved\n\nThree PowerShell scripts enabling unattended weekly pipeline runs via\nWindows Task Scheduler, plus Gmail-on-failure notifications. The\npipeline''s local-development MVP is now complete - all seven phases\nof the active plan are closed.\n\nScheduled task scripts:\n  - scripts/run-scheduled.ps1: the wrapper Windows Task Scheduler\n    invokes. Resolves project root from its own location, redirects\n    stdout + stderr to logs/scheduled-<timestamp>.log via cmd /c\n    append-redirection (sidesteps PowerShell 5.1''s NativeCommandError\n    wrapping of native-cmd stderr), invokes node server/pipeline/index.js\n    directly (not pnpm - avoids PATH issues in scheduled-task context),\n    fires a failure-notification email on non-zero exit via\n    Send-MailMessage against Gmail SMTP (smtp.gmail.com:587, TLS,\n    authenticated with GMAIL_USER + GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD env vars).\n    Email skipped silently if either env var is missing.\n  - scripts/install-task.ps1: registers a scheduled task via\n    Register-ScheduledTask. Args: -DayOfWeek, -Time (HH:mm), optional\n    -Name. Settings: WakeToRun + StartWhenAvailable +\n    AllowStartIfOnBatteries + DontStopIfGoingOnBatteries +\n    ExecutionTimeLimit 30min. Uses -RunLevel Highest so WakeToRun is\n    honored.\n  - scripts/uninstall-task.ps1: idempotent removal of a registered\n    task by name.\n\nHardened install-task.ps1 against the elevation footgun:\n  - $ErrorActionPreference = ''Stop'' so any cmdlet failure halts the\n    script (the initial cut printed a green \"success\" banner even\n    when Register-ScheduledTask returned Access Denied because the\n    error was non-terminating).\n  - Up-front WindowsBuiltInRole::Administrator check with a clear\n    \"must be run elevated\" message + cd instructions to re-run from\n    an Administrator PowerShell window. Catches the elevation issue\n    before any Scheduler calls so the user gets a helpful message\n    instead of a deep cmdlet stack trace.\n  - try/catch around Register-ScheduledTask with a specific hint if\n    the error message contains \"Access is denied\".\n\nAll three scripts pass [System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::\nParseFile syntax verification.\n\nImplementation gotcha worth remembering (captured in\nIMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md): em-dash characters (U+2014) in regular\ndouble-quoted PowerShell strings break parsing on PS 5.1 because the\nfile is read as Windows-1252 by default; the UTF-8 byte sequence for\nem-dash includes a quote-like character that prematurely terminates\nthe string. Here-strings (@\"...\"@) and comments tolerate em-dashes;\nregular \"...\" strings do not. Stuck to ASCII hyphens throughout the\n.ps1 files.\n\nDocs:\n  - PROGRESS.md: Scheduled task wrapper added to \"What''s built and\n    working\" with full detail on all three scripts. New \"Scheduled\n    runs (optional)\" section with prominent admin-PowerShell-required\n    callout, full project path (incl. note about the \"newesletter\"\n    folder-name typo so future-me doesn''t lose 10 minutes again),\n    Gmail App Password setup steps, install commands for Jeremy''s\n    three confidence-building test runs (Saturday 0800, Saturday\n    1700, Sunday 0800), manual-fire / verify / uninstall commands.\n    \"Next phase\" section replaced with MVP-achieved note.\n  - IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md: Phase G marked closed. \"Where we are\"\n    updated with the MVP-achieved announcement covering all seven\n    phases.\n  - FUTURE_ENHANCEMENTS.md: published-archive entry (the editorial-\n    content-aware-queries idea) and Railway cloud-deployment migration\n    entry, both tagged post-MVP.\n  - .gitignore: logs/ added alongside usage/ and drafts/.\n\nField-tested by Jeremy: all three test tasks installed cleanly from\nelevated PowerShell. State ''Ready'' on all three. Saturday 17:00 fire\nwill be the first natural validation; manual fire via\nStart-ScheduledTask is available if earlier confirmation is wanted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac4c6ce2e53d7785f164954e0ba58a66601d9ba5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/trees/ac4c6ce2e53d7785f164954e0ba58a66601d9ba5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/commits/d11af7c394e34e4d8c8cd19e5b049f1eaeab07ef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/d11af7c394e34e4d8c8cd19e5b049f1eaeab07ef","node_id":"C_kwDOSj6oLtoAKGQxMWFmN2MzOTRlMzRlNGQ4YzhjZDE5ZTViMDQ5ZjFlYWVhYjA3ZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/f262da8e6692dd21caccd31e3e23aa9cb9038700","sha":"f262da8e6692dd21caccd31e3e23aa9cb9038700","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/f262da8e6692dd21caccd31e3e23aa9cb9038700"}],"sha":"d11af7c394e34e4d8c8cd19e5b049f1eaeab07ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/d11af7c394e34e4d8c8cd19e5b049f1eaeab07ef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/f262da8e6692dd21caccd31e3e23aa9cb9038700/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T03:11:58Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T03:11:58Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"message":"Phase F: Review UI polish — sidebar, validator visibility, history\n\nThe editor''s UI is now a real review tool: history sidebar (drafts +\nrecent runs with success/failure indicators), past-draft viewing in\nread-only mode, per-section copy/edit/regenerate affordances with\nvalidator-warning badges, cost + duration + warnings in the draft\nfooter. Failure visibility comes from the historical Recent runs\nsidebar (pulling from usage.jsonl) rather than live SSE — equivalent\nUX for a single-user local app at a fraction of the engineering.\n\nServer side:\n  - server/server.js: new GET /api/runs endpoint exposing recent\n    usage.jsonl entries (success and failure) with per-stage call\n    counts + cost. Clamped to 100 max, defaults to 25.\n  - server/pipeline/index.js: buildClientView (now exported) enriched\n    with validation + usage summary fields. regenerateSection returns\n    the full client view rather than just the updated section — keeps\n    UI data in sync after every regenerate without a second fetch.\n  - server/pipeline/drafts.js: listDrafts metadata now includes\n    warningCount (curate + write validator counts summed) so the\n    sidebar can render warning badges without loading each full draft.\n\nClient side:\n  - src/components/Sidebar.jsx (new): collapsible left sidebar listing\n    all drafts (newest first, with cost / hit count / duration /\n    warning count) and the last 15 runs from usage.jsonl. Success vs\n    failure derived from stage call counts per runType: pipeline needs\n    all three stages, regenerate needs write, replay needs curate +\n    write. Click a draft to load it; active draft highlighted.\n  - src/App.jsx: rebuilt around three additional state slots\n    (sidebarOpen, drafts/runs, viewingPast). New handler selectDraft\n    fetches the full draft body and shapes it into the client view.\n    The latest draft (head of drafts list) is the only one that\n    allows regeneration; anything else is read-only.\n  - src/components/PipelineStatus.jsx: simplified from the misleading\n    four-stage indicator (the client never received intermediate\n    stage events anyway) to a single \"Running pipeline...\" state with\n    elapsed-time tick.\n  - src/components/Section.jsx: per-section copy-to-clipboard button,\n    validator-warning badge (count + hover tooltip listing warning\n    kinds), regenerate button disabled when viewingPast is true.\n  - src/components/ReviewUI.jsx: cost/duration/warning-count footer\n    line under the week header; dedicated callout block above the\n    section list for cross-section warnings (URL appearing in two\n    output sections, source-dominance).\n\nWhat did NOT land (deliberately):\n  - Full SSE for real-time stage transitions. Original lean was a\n    full implementation; pushback prevailed on simpler \"Running...\"\n    indicator with elapsed time. Failure visibility provided by the\n    historical Recent runs sidebar instead.\n  - Regenerate-against-past-draft (forking). Locks in read-only past\n    drafts (Option A from design discussion). Forking captured as a\n    candidate enhancement if the workflow ever needs editable history.\n\nVisual verification by the editor confirmed: sidebar collapses\nsmoothly, success/failure icons render correctly (red X for prior\nfailed pipeline runs from Phase A diagnostic sessions, green check\nfor successes), warning badges visible, full markdown copy produces\nReddit-compatible output (KonoSuba fourth season, Quintessential\nQuintuplets sequel, Kyoto Animation''s Sparks of Tomorrow, etc).\n\nThe pipeline is now functionally MVP. Only Phase G (Task Scheduler\nwrapper for unattended weekly runs) remains before the project hits\nthe original 10-step goal.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4ae07dbd1ae509f50eac7915a60d29cd1d1cc4c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/trees/4ae07dbd1ae509f50eac7915a60d29cd1d1cc4c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/commits/f262da8e6692dd21caccd31e3e23aa9cb9038700","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/f262da8e6692dd21caccd31e3e23aa9cb9038700","node_id":"C_kwDOSj6oLtoAKGYyNjJkYThlNjY5MmRkMjFjYWNjZDMxZTNlMjNhYTljYjkwMzg3MDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/2ca5fc012fdd527abc9b7bc45a9435d805ba4c3b","sha":"2ca5fc012fdd527abc9b7bc45a9435d805ba4c3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/2ca5fc012fdd527abc9b7bc45a9435d805ba4c3b"}],"sha":"f262da8e6692dd21caccd31e3e23aa9cb9038700","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/f262da8e6692dd21caccd31e3e23aa9cb9038700"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/2ca5fc012fdd527abc9b7bc45a9435d805ba4c3b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T02:37:56Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T02:37:56Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"message":"Phase D + E: draft persistence + cheap section regeneration\n\nPipeline 8 smoke test: full run produced drafts/2026-05-23-020310.json\nat $1.01 / 358s. Followed by a regenerate test on the industry section\nthat ran in 12.8s for $0.0162 — only that section changed in the saved\ndraft, all other sections preserved. Phase D + E bundled because they\nshare the same persistence layer.\n\nDraft persistence (Phase E):\n  - server/pipeline/drafts.js (new) — saveDraft, loadDraft,\n    loadLatestDraft, listDrafts. One JSON file per run at\n    drafts/<weekOf>-<HHMMSS>.json containing rawHits, curated,\n    written, and the per-run usage record. Schema is versioned\n    (version: 1) for future migrations. loadLatestDraft picks by\n    createdAt field (not file mtime) so the directory can be moved\n    or touched without breaking ordering.\n  - runPipeline finalizes its usage record and saves the draft inside\n    the try block so the saved record includes the finalized cost.\n    Drafts only saved on success — failures leave only the usage.jsonl\n    entry.\n  - drafts/ directory already gitignored (set up preemptively in a\n    previous session).\n\nSection regeneration (Phase D):\n  - server/pipeline/write.js — writeSection(sectionId, curated,\n    runUsage) exported as a peer of write(). Internal refactor:\n    write() now uses writeSection as its per-section loop body.\n    Zero behavior change for the full-write path.\n  - server/pipeline/index.js — regenerateSection now loads the latest\n    draft, fires one Write call against that section''s already-\n    curated hits, then re-saves the draft in place (preserves id,\n    original usage field stays intact). The regenerate''s own usage\n    line is appended to usage.jsonl as a separate entry with\n    runType: ''regenerate''. Costs ~$0.02 and runs in ~10-15s vs. the\n    prior $1+ / 6-min behavior of re-running the whole pipeline.\n  - The existing React UI (Section.jsx regenerate button + App.jsx\n    handler) was already wired to POST /api/regenerate-section, so\n    no client-side changes were needed.\n\nReplay-from-draft CLI flag (Phase E side-benefit):\n  - pnpm generate --from-draft=latest (or --from-draft=<id>) loads a\n    saved draft''s rawHits and re-runs only Curate + Write. Skips the\n    $1 Search stage. Enables $0.13 prompt iteration cycles on\n    Curate / Write. New draft saved as its own file; original\n    untouched.\n  - Fixed the CLI guard in pipeline/index.js to handle being imported\n    by node -e (process.argv[1] can be undefined in that case).\n\nDrafts REST endpoints:\n  - GET /api/drafts — metadata list (id, createdAt, weekOf,\n    totalCost, durationMs, sectionCounts) sorted desc by createdAt.\n    Does not load the full bodies, keeps the response small.\n  - GET /api/drafts/:id — full draft body.\n  - 404 returned for missing drafts (vs 500 for other errors).\n\nBonus observations from Pipeline 8 (validates Phase C polish in\nproduction):\n  - URL denylist filtered 7 real placeholder URLs cleanly\n    (all encyclopedia/anime/upcoming/tv). No false positives.\n  - Curate validator caught a real `stale` hit (publishedDate\n    2026-05-02, >7 days ago). The deterministic validator layer is\n    paying for itself.\n\nDocs:\n  - PROGRESS.md: three new \"What''s built and working\" entries\n    (Draft persistence, Section regeneration, Replay-from-draft +\n    REST endpoints). Trajectory table gained Pipeline 8 and Regen 1\n    rows. Spend total $7.76 -> $8.79 across 12 attempts.\n    DEBUG_DUMP_HITS / DEBUG_DUMP_CURATED cleanup item now notes\n    they''re redundant with drafts on disk; kept for inline log\n    inspection until clearly unused.\n  - IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md: Phase D and Phase E both marked closed\n    in a combined section. Phase F (Review UI polish) is now the\n    next active phase.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ffe1add7825a251298cb60a90939dd160b1e9e90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/trees/ffe1add7825a251298cb60a90939dd160b1e9e90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/commits/2ca5fc012fdd527abc9b7bc45a9435d805ba4c3b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/2ca5fc012fdd527abc9b7bc45a9435d805ba4c3b","node_id":"C_kwDOSj6oLtoAKDJjYTVmYzAxMmZkZDUyN2FiYzliN2JjNDVhOTQzNWQ4MDViYTRjM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/736a790c46daf30dd8d98cdadec8df046e25ecdc","sha":"736a790c46daf30dd8d98cdadec8df046e25ecdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/736a790c46daf30dd8d98cdadec8df046e25ecdc"}],"sha":"2ca5fc012fdd527abc9b7bc45a9435d805ba4c3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/2ca5fc012fdd527abc9b7bc45a9435d805ba4c3b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/736a790c46daf30dd8d98cdadec8df046e25ecdc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T01:30:51Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T01:30:51Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"message":"Phase C: real Write, URL denylist, source-priority overhaul\n\nPipeline 7 smoke test: 4/4 search + 1 curate + 6/6 write calls\nsucceeded; total run cost $0.99 (forecast $1.20-1.30); Write itself\n$0.05 (forecast $0.20-0.30) thanks to system-prompt caching across\nthe 6 sequential calls; zero Write-validator warnings; publication-\nquality markdown across all sections with correct voice and inline\nsource links. The pipeline now produces real content end-to-end.\n\nReal Write stage:\n  - server/pipeline/write.js replaced with 6 sequential Claude calls\n    per run (5 content sections in newsletter order, then intro last).\n    Single-section-isolated input: each content call sees only its\n    section''s curated hits; the intro call gets a compact summary of\n    headlines across all sections so it can identify themes.\n    No tools, NO_THINKING, effort: low, max_tokens: 1500. Sequential\n    for the same Tier 1 rate-limit reasons as Search.\n  - prompts/write-system.md encodes voice rules from CLAUDE.md\n    (informative trade-publication register, no hype, no exclamations,\n    no emoji, no clickbait phrasing) with GOOD/BAD examples,\n    per-section format requirements (3-5 sentence stories with ###\n    headers for full-entry sections; bullet list for Quick Hits;\n    plain prose with no header for intro), and source-attribution\n    rules ([Source: <name>](<url>) inline).\n  - Empty-section short-circuit: when curated input for a section\n    has 0 hits, Write skips the LLM call and returns an empty string.\n    Saves cost on thin-news weeks.\n  - Per-section status recorded in runUsage.stages.write.sections\n    mirroring the Search pattern (status, item count).\n\nStage-level deterministic validator (third use of the pattern):\n  - validateWritten() runs after the 6 Write calls. Emits warnings\n    for intro-length, story-count (per section), no-source-link\n    (each story must include an inline Markdown link), quick-hits-\n    count, hype-phrase (regex denylist of HUGE/MASSIVE/FINALLY/EPIC/\n    SHOCKING + clickbait phrases like \"fans are losing it\" /\n    \"you won''t believe\" / \"here''s why\"), and exclamation point usage.\n  - recordWriteValidation() helper in usage.js writes warnings + count\n    into runUsage.stages.write.validation. Same pattern as\n    recordCurateValidation from Phase B.\n  - Pattern now applied at all three LLM stages (Search has\n    per-section status; Curate and Write each have validation +\n    per-section status).\n\nPrompt + code iteration applied post-smoke-test (no verification\nre-run - trust the changes and surface effects in the next pipeline\nrun via the new logging):\n  - URL denylist added to validateHit (search.js) and isValidHit\n    (curate.js). Six surgical patterns reject placeholder URLs that\n    pass the basic shape regex but point at category indexes,\n    year-only / year-month archives, encyclopedia entries, or tag\n    pages (e.g. /encyclopedia/anime/upcoming/tv, /news/, /news/2026,\n    /news/2026/04, /category/..., /tag/...). Patterns are anchored\n    (mostly with $) to minimize false positives. Pipeline 7 surfaced\n    7 of 13 curated hits with such URLs - the basic-shape regex\n    passed them because they DID have a path. Per-rejection logging\n    with the matching pattern name + URL preview surfaces every\n    filtered URL so false positives are immediately visible.\n  - Source-priority overhaul in search-system.md. Restructured into\n    Tier 0 (first-party studio / platform / publisher sources -\n    Sunrise, Bones, Production I.G, MAPPA, Wit Studio, CloverWorks,\n    Kyoto Animation, Trigger, Studio Pierrot, Toei Animation, plus\n    Crunchyroll/Netflix/etc. and Shueisha/Kodansha/etc.) and Tier 1\n    (news outlets, with MAL News promoted from #5 to #3 alongside\n    Anime Corner). New \"Source diversity\" subsection requires at\n    least 3 distinct sources per call and bans >70% from any single\n    outlet. Pipeline 7 had 100% ANN; the prompt-level intervention\n    should drop dominance to ~60-70% without adding API calls.\n\nDocs:\n  - FUTURE_ENHANCEMENTS.md: dedicated studio press-release search\n    query added with trigger condition (>2 consecutive runs of\n    source-dominance warnings after the Phase C prompt overhaul).\n  - PROGRESS.md: Write moved from \"stubbed\" to \"built and working\"\n    with full detail. URL denylist added as its own entry.\n    Trajectory table gained Pipeline 7 row. Spend total\n    $6.77 -> $7.76 across 10 attempts. \"What''s stubbed\" effectively\n    empty - pipeline produces real content end-to-end.\n  - IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md: Phase C marked closed with full \"what\n    landed\" + \"did not land\" sections. Phase D (section regeneration\n    wiring) is now the next active phase.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d8ef5c6b4b550bfb69c8c43d781d77c48480f3e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/trees/d8ef5c6b4b550bfb69c8c43d781d77c48480f3e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/commits/736a790c46daf30dd8d98cdadec8df046e25ecdc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/736a790c46daf30dd8d98cdadec8df046e25ecdc","node_id":"C_kwDOSj6oLtoAKDczNmE3OTBjNDZkYWYzMGRkOGQ5OGNkYWRlYzhkZjA0NmUyNWVjZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/86e0a48e5e0dec32dc33835f658b3a611e9f05f1","sha":"86e0a48e5e0dec32dc33835f658b3a611e9f05f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/86e0a48e5e0dec32dc33835f658b3a611e9f05f1"}],"sha":"736a790c46daf30dd8d98cdadec8df046e25ecdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/736a790c46daf30dd8d98cdadec8df046e25ecdc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/86e0a48e5e0dec32dc33835f658b3a611e9f05f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-22T15:30:54Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-22T15:30:54Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"message":"Phase B: real Curate, post-curate validator, prompt iteration\n\nPipeline 6 smoke test: 26 raw search hits -> 19 curated hits across 5\noutput sections; Curate cost $0.078 (predicted band $0.05-0.10); zero\nschema warnings; total per-run cost $1.10 (predicted $1.05-1.10).\n\nReal Curate stage:\n  - server/pipeline/curate.js replaced with a single Claude call\n    (no tools, NO_THINKING, effort: low). Reads raw hits keyed by input\n    section, returns the 5 output sections (new-upcoming, industry,\n    manga-anime, community, quick-hits). Multi-text-block JSON parser\n    mirrors the Search-stage scan from Phase A.\n  - Editorial rubric lives in prompts/curate-system.md so edits don''t\n    require code changes. Encodes dedup heuristic (topic + source\n    preference, ANN > Crunchyroll > others), 7-day recency cutoff,\n    newsworthiness filter, section routing rules, Quick Hits criteria,\n    and sizing guidance (12-20 total hits per run).\n\nStage-level deterministic validator:\n  - validateCurated() runs after the LLM call. Emits warnings for\n    url-no-path, no-date, stale (>7d), cross-section (same URL in two\n    output sections), sizing (count out of rubric range), and\n    source-dominance (>80% one source).\n  - recordCurateValidation() helper in usage.js writes warnings +\n    count into runUsage.stages.curate.validation so accumulating data\n    tells us how often each issue actually occurs. No filtering -\n    warnings are observability, not gating.\n  - Pattern complements the LLM rubric: the rubric reduces failure\n    rate, the validator catches what slips through. Likely reusable\n    for a post-Write validator in Phase C.\n\nPrompt iteration applied post-smoke-test (no verification re-run -\ntrust the changes and validate in Phase C''s smoke test):\n  - validateHit + isValidHit regex tightened from /^https?:\\/\\//i to\n    /^https?:\\/\\/[^/]+\\/[^/]+/i so URLs without a path beyond the\n    domain (e.g. https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/) no longer pass.\n    Pipeline 6 surfaced 5 such placeholder URLs that the looser regex\n    accepted; tightening prevents the cascade where Curate treats\n    distinct stories with the same fake URL as routable-but-deduped.\n  - search-system.md URL field requirement now explicitly bans\n    homepages, section indexes, date archives, and category landing\n    pages. Tells the model to omit the story rather than return a\n    placeholder URL.\n  - curate-system.md manga-anime routing rule tightened: source\n    material must be a *published manga*. Explicit exclusions for\n    light novels, visual novels, original anime, sequels of existing\n    anime, and live-action. Driven by Pipeline 6 misrouting a Gundam\n    Wing sequel into manga-anime - Gundam Wing is original anime, not\n    a manga-to-anime adaptation.\n\nDEBUG_DUMP_CURATED env flag added to pipeline/index.js mirroring the\nexisting DEBUG_DUMP_HITS pattern. Removed when draft persistence\n(Phase E) lands.\n\nDocs:\n  - PROGRESS.md: Curate moved from \"stubbed\" to \"built and working\"\n    with full detail on LLM call shape, parser, and validator.\n    Trajectory table gained Step B manga-anime diagnostic and\n    Pipeline 6 entries. Spend total updated $5.55 -> $6.77.\n  - IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md: Phase B marked closed with \"what landed\"\n    section. Phase C (real Write) is now the next active phase.\n  - FUTURE_ENHANCEMENTS.md: hybrid Curate (deterministic dedup pre-pass\n    + LLM routing on the deduped set) added with trigger condition\n    (Curate cost > $0.10 consistently OR input > 25 hits per run).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"41801a44933697fe9afa28ea2992079bba2895d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/trees/41801a44933697fe9afa28ea2992079bba2895d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/commits/86e0a48e5e0dec32dc33835f658b3a611e9f05f1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/86e0a48e5e0dec32dc33835f658b3a611e9f05f1","node_id":"C_kwDOSj6oLtoAKDg2ZTBhNDhlNWUwZGVjMzJkYzMzODM1ZjY1OGIzYTYxMWU5ZjA1ZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/a6362d61ee7a127e7d464b15cd880f0265e3338a","sha":"a6362d61ee7a127e7d464b15cd880f0265e3338a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/a6362d61ee7a127e7d464b15cd880f0265e3338a"}],"sha":"86e0a48e5e0dec32dc33835f658b3a611e9f05f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/86e0a48e5e0dec32dc33835f658b3a611e9f05f1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/a6362d61ee7a127e7d464b15cd880f0265e3338a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-22T14:29:07Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-22T14:29:07Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"message":"Phase A: stabilize Search, instrument failures, restructure docs\n\nStep 3 is now stable end-to-end: pipeline 5/5 sections, ~$1.00/run, ~6 min\nwall, no rate-limit incidents. Closes the diagnostic chapter opened in the\nprior session.\n\nArchitecture changes (drive cost and reliability):\n  - Swap web_search_20260209 -> web_search_20250305 (legacy). The new tool\n    silently wraps in code_execution_20260120 on Sonnet 4.6; Step B vs Step A\n    showed 37.5s vs 320-625s/call with no observable filtering benefit.\n  - Set thinking: NO_THINKING. The prior session''s hypothesis that thinking\n    drove cost was disproven during Step A.\n  - Serialize the 4 section calls (was Promise.all). Parallel fan-out busts\n    Tier 1''s 30k input-tokens-per-minute limit because cache_read counts\n    toward it. Wall-time penalty (~3x) acceptable.\n  - Add 429 retry with retry-after compliance, MAX_429_RETRIES=3 in\n    trackedCall. Defense in depth alongside serialization.\n\nEditorial-scope decision:\n  - Drop the dedicated manga-anime search query. Pipeline 5 evidence showed\n    adaptation news (Tanuki, Iwamoto-senpai, Black Channel, Medalist film,\n    Netflix lineup) surfaces reliably via general + new-upcoming. Curate\n    will route adaptation hits into the Manga -> Anime output section. Same\n    logic that previously dropped dedicated convention and seiyuu queries.\n\nParser hardening:\n  - parseHits now scans every text block last -> first and accepts the\n    first valid JSON array. The Pipeline 5 manga-anime miss was caused by\n    Claude emitting JSON in an earlier text block than the closing summary\n    text block, not by malformed JSON. Position is non-deterministic.\n  - parseHits returns { hits, status } where status is one of\n    success | empty | parse-failed | no-text.\n\nFailure instrumentation (Layer 1 + 2):\n  - Per-section status recorded into runUsage.stages.search.sections so\n    every usage.jsonl entry carries which sections succeeded/failed.\n  - Sidecar usage/failures.jsonl appended on any parse-failed / no-text\n    response: block-type sequence + first-500-char snippets of every text\n    block. Forensic record that lets us classify failures offline without\n    re-firing the API call.\n  - Layer 3 (real-time salvage call) captured in FUTURE_ENHANCEMENTS.md\n    tagged to Phase B as a companion, with an explicit trigger condition\n    (>1 parse-failed per month in failures.jsonl).\n\nTooling and ops:\n  - createRunUsage(''full'') -> createRunUsage(''pipeline''). Migrated 6\n    existing usage.jsonl entries; backup at usage/usage.jsonl.bak.\n  - test-step-a.js generalized to accept QUERY / SECTION env vars. Dump\n    file now named per-section so successive diagnostics don''t overwrite\n    each other.\n\nDocs restructured to three-doc lifecycle:\n  - PROGRESS.md = what WAS done. Rewritten to close the open-problem\n    chapter from the prior session and reflect Step 3 stabilization.\n  - IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md (new) = what we ARE CURRENTLY doing. Active\n    phased plan, scope/cost/validation per phase, where we are in it.\n  - FUTURE_ENHANCEMENTS.md = what we WILL DO LATER. Added Critic-stage\n    revision-loop and Layer 3 salvage-call entries.\n\nPhase B (real Curate) is the next session''s starting point.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2cf8e9241bd5d2745e1da00c970e77371fd3e9ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/trees/2cf8e9241bd5d2745e1da00c970e77371fd3e9ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/commits/a6362d61ee7a127e7d464b15cd880f0265e3338a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/a6362d61ee7a127e7d464b15cd880f0265e3338a","node_id":"C_kwDOSj6oLtoAKGE2MzYyZDYxZWU3YTEyN2U3ZDQ2NGIxNWNkODgwZjAyNjVlMzMzOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commit/c963b31b643cb767c402516e8ed386ad74dcd722","sha":"c963b31b643cb767c402516e8ed386ad74dcd722","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/c963b31b643cb767c402516e8ed386ad74dcd722"}],"sha":"a6362d61ee7a127e7d464b15cd880f0265e3338a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/a6362d61ee7a127e7d464b15cd880f0265e3338a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"yayhooray","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/commits/c963b31b643cb767c402516e8ed386ad74dcd722/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-21T23:06:07Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-21T23:06:07Z","email":"someone@example.com","name":"Anime Intel"},"message":"Step A diagnostic: capture findings, add evidence + future-enhancements doc\n\nThree single-call diagnostics (server/test-step-a.js) overturn the prior\nhypothesis that adaptive thinking was the search-stage cost driver. New\nconfirmed root causes are now documented in PROGRESS.md:\n\n  1. Cost driver is NOT thinking — three runs with thinking disabled\n     produced 320-625s wall times (vs predicted <90s) and $0.17-0.24/call\n     (vs target $0.05-0.10).\n  2. web_search_20260209 on Sonnet 4.6 is wrapped in code_execution_20260120;\n     the model writes Python in a sandbox that calls await web_search(...)\n     and decrypts encrypted_content. Evidence preserved at\n     docs/evidence/step-a-code-execution-wrapper.json (the run-2 dump that\n     first surfaced the wrapper, 40 content blocks of which only 2 are text).\n  3. Search backend is unreliable — repeated \"Detection timed out after 25s\"\n     errors in the dump; model retries with bash sleeps, amplifying wall time.\n  4. Network middleware kills long-lived streams non-deterministically\n     (run A3 died at 462s with undici ''terminated'', run A1 survived 625s).\n     Likely a TLS interceptor; independently confirmed via npm install\n     UNABLE_TO_VERIFY_LEAF_SIGNATURE on the same machine.\n\nFUTURE_ENHANCEMENTS.md captures cost-control measures deferred until the\nStep 3 architecture stabilizes (dedicated API key with monthly cap, Batch\nAPI for Curate/Write, usage-report CLI, etc.).\n\nFresh-machine setup section in PROGRESS.md now documents the\nNODE_OPTIONS=--use-system-ca workaround for the TLS interceptor so the\nnext setup doesn''t lose half a day to it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"adcbb20688c027a0a0f76d2e9141026b934c3626","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/trees/adcbb20688c027a0a0f76d2e9141026b934c3626"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NavyDevilDoc/anime-newsletter/git/commits/c963b31b643cb767c402516e8ed386ad74dcd722","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75228?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yayhooray/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yayhooray","id":75228,"login":"y