om","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T18:03:40Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"chore(release): 0.2.0\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"78f3b3f48c1ccdd1f6b3ce9551698bad88a04a32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/78f3b3f48c1ccdd1f6b3ce9551698bad88a04a32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/d1b31aa0ab8d925f98cd3b347dbbbdf9bc8ae0b2","verification":{"payload":"tree 78f3b3f48c1ccdd1f6b3ce9551698bad88a04a32\nparent d1026f356ba0feb7d9d8297f7981f7e594932081\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786644220 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786644220 +0200\n\nchore(release): 0.2.0\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmp+BvwACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nrKAf+NON0JMOX9oWSlVDD8/s8o9WdC+kTrhnfwE857fCUwRwFa0jUeTrIC4Tc\n1mMAUVcE6kP6yMtbtxJTWcu5o1mFb4QcBca53RCKDBJQvxnLqUTkkDkH5eaT4s6w\n2vytak42ZgaNivFgrR3NqZVRdLjksnqrgip1r5cD5eLZn9TZxzWuZLsf48mkwbiK\nH+fv1EynUM8hKbB+2z2gmM76FgUEfDUDow/oGHGwOC9trlLajwbeA8nN9otIkPEt\nCSnRpO8VTB/+stykBlFKIsnfCFtjIrIioiuPLTemthWPUV5JjyvDY5CrYe2nANwc\ns/fEQi9wT+THm3ShUC0XH/3zKa9+0g==\n=xcb0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T18:06:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/d1b31aa0ab8d925f98cd3b347dbbbdf9bc8ae0b2","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKGQxYjMxYWEwYWI4ZDkyNWY5OGNkM2IzNDdkYmJiZGY5YmM4YWUwYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/d1026f356ba0feb7d9d8297f7981f7e594932081","sha":"d1026f356ba0feb7d9d8297f7981f7e594932081","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/d1026f356ba0feb7d9d8297f7981f7e594932081"}],"sha":"d1b31aa0ab8d925f98cd3b347dbbbdf9bc8ae0b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/d1b31aa0ab8d925f98cd3b347dbbbdf9bc8ae0b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/d1026f356ba0feb7d9d8297f7981f7e594932081/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T16:33:53Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T16:33:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(ui): put the three React admin apps under test, and fix two bugs it found (#108)\n\nextensions/src/javascript, totp/src/javascript and webauthn/src/javascript had\nno tests at all. That gap had a measurable cost this week: eleven major\ndependency bumps - react 18->19 among them - were merged on the strength of\n\"webpack emitted a bundle\", because nothing exercised these screens. Every CI\ngreen tick on this code was worth much less than it looked.\n\n115 tests across the three modules (extensions 9, totp 53, webauthn 53), using\nvitest + React Testing Library to match the idiom login-ui already uses rather\nthan introducing a second one. `yarn test` is wired into each module''s\nfrontend-maven-plugin executions next to `yarn lint`, so the build runs them -\na suite the build does not execute would recreate the problem it is meant to fix.\n\nCoverage went where regressions have actually happened: the useQuery-without-\nerror defect that let a failed load leave constructor defaults in the form and\nSave write them back (silently clearing enforcedFactors, the IP whitelist and\nthe login URL); the trustForwardedFor default that contradicted the shipped\nSEC-135 setting; the self-service prompt that offered backup codes the server\nrejects; the one-shot backup-codes dialog that must not be dismissable before\nacknowledgement; the two-phase confirm on the destructive user reset; and the\nbase64url conversions every WebAuthn credential id round-trips through.\n\nTwo real bugs surfaced while writing them, neither injected:\n\n- ResetUserSection (BOTH the totp and webauthn copies): reset() called\n  setConfirming(false) synchronously before invoking the mutation, so React 18\n  batched it with Apollo''s loading:true and the confirmation box - which holds\n  the \"Resetting...\" label - unmounted in the same render that was supposed to\n  show the in-flight state. The label was unreachable by construction. Moved\n  into the mutation''s onCompleted. This file had already lost and regained that\n  label once through copy-paste drift; two near-identical copies with no shared\n  abstraction and no tests is how that keeps happening.\n\n- Nothing was wrong with webauthn''s SiteSettings error handling, checked and\n  confirmed - the red/green there was demonstrated by temporarily removing the\n  guard rather than by finding a defect.\n\nEvery test was verified capable of failing: the production code was broken in\nthe specific way each test guards against, the test was watched go red, and the\nfix restored. Details per module in the PR.\n\nTwo small testability changes with no behaviour impact: isLazyQueryResultEmpty\nexported from both AuditReportSection files, and b64uToBuf/bufToB64u exported\nfrom webauthnBrowser.js.\n\nFull reactor green: 352 Java tests, 115 React tests, lint and coverage enforced.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"e290426b56481e068f2da3baa53a443d0ed02905","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/e290426b56481e068f2da3baa53a443d0ed02905"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/d1026f356ba0feb7d9d8297f7981f7e594932081","verification":{"payload":"tree e290426b56481e068f2da3baa53a443d0ed02905\nparent 8a58a020aca7f8f6122deb75fdc7e1bc416e5fe4\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786638833 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786638833 +0200\n\ntest(ui): put the three React admin apps under test, and fix two bugs it found (#108)\n\nextensions/src/javascript, totp/src/javascript and webauthn/src/javascript had\nno tests at all. That gap had a measurable cost this week: eleven major\ndependency bumps - react 18->19 among them - were merged on the strength of\n\"webpack emitted a bundle\", because nothing exercised these screens. Every CI\ngreen tick on this code was worth much less than it looked.\n\n115 tests across the three modules (extensions 9, totp 53, webauthn 53), using\nvitest + React Testing Library to match the idiom login-ui already uses rather\nthan introducing a second one. `yarn test` is wired into each module''s\nfrontend-maven-plugin executions next to `yarn lint`, so the build runs them -\na suite the build does not execute would recreate the problem it is meant to fix.\n\nCoverage went where regressions have actually happened: the useQuery-without-\nerror defect that let a failed load leave constructor defaults in the form and\nSave write them back (silently clearing enforcedFactors, the IP whitelist and\nthe login URL); the trustForwardedFor default that contradicted the shipped\nSEC-135 setting; the self-service prompt that offered backup codes the server\nrejects; the one-shot backup-codes dialog that must not be dismissable before\nacknowledgement; the two-phase confirm on the destructive user reset; and the\nbase64url conversions every WebAuthn credential id round-trips through.\n\nTwo real bugs surfaced while writing them, neither injected:\n\n- ResetUserSection (BOTH the totp and webauthn copies): reset() called\n  setConfirming(false) synchronously before invoking the mutation, so React 18\n  batched it with Apollo''s loading:true and the confirmation box - which holds\n  the \"Resetting...\" label - unmounted in the same render that was supposed to\n  show the in-flight state. The label was unreachable by construction. Moved\n  into the mutation''s onCompleted. This file had already lost and regained that\n  label once through copy-paste drift; two near-identical copies with no shared\n  abstraction and no tests is how that keeps happening.\n\n- Nothing was wrong with webauthn''s SiteSettings error handling, checked and\n  confirmed - the red/green there was demonstrated by temporarily removing the\n  guard rather than by finding a defect.\n\nEvery test was verified capable of failing: the production code was broken in\nthe specific way each test guards against, the test was watched go red, and the\nfix restored. Details per module in the PR.\n\nTwo small testability changes with no behaviour impact: isLazyQueryResultEmpty\nexported from both AuditReportSection files, and b64uToBuf/bufToB64u exported\nfrom webauthnBrowser.js.\n\nFull reactor green: 352 Java tests, 115 React tests, lint and coverage enforced.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqffHxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKe8QACgnZMF0Fty3WiK7lOiZNF6e\nplDiJxD6P33QSDCpHNmkYMNhzUZqrD62k08j1wxAtAQXGqaf28ygfW6ke+k2tosE\n8Lwhtvqv0RMobqO/9x/6U9rfalJzVlfjQ5FZP4FVhK4qHzhxAB1Lyup0VG4f5v7U\nkM5JvsdoG1XiGhtSJMjG0FP3Pla1M6nbUWqgNCo880oufGfyLyxc1GDJNF3HtRox\nD/5r1TjbbHMRy2LsjQCQ15yq12URsC4w4e9iBt1M/fo+hv9n7ukiiYD6OMReA0Bz\nwTwfr0ugTcSN5ZJ6LYUeA//h/9KK6aWSscRDwU95HH+L/FNaCuqhsfQPq+IgTvb+\nUyrzfH0CDnvum+L4hB+LqgKyuQWngByF5VnBkCfqE16771P9pdO1+Gn3BcoHCoST\nyv/h8A1XET5mSpFG/MjAwDK0bvbGh50vnxMMER/Qe6YXUZrZLAcqCA9M9M6usBk8\nAzzG+uypQFulkBwNN8TcJioAmgOT3l/RiXf6zN7iqi5mwlS9rmlWEZeHUSmCFQ2X\n67rwIzhmSiH1WTF4LzrgZGlxUTcn5Lqv6BKOhkog/hQO8fJnREiwdwMMHYzGjBVo\n9AevX0+dDOlJrc6uAo8mGiD+x7LNkzEViNuVX17ceKaDZbETF1SP3k290swUo7Ra\nqw2P6MaQlTzYFboOQef7\n=B3vo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T16:38:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/d1026f356ba0feb7d9d8297f7981f7e594932081","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKGQxMDI2ZjM1NmJhMGZlYjdkOWQ4Mjk3Zjc5ODFmN2U1OTQ5MzIwODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/8a58a020aca7f8f6122deb75fdc7e1bc416e5fe4","sha":"8a58a020aca7f8f6122deb75fdc7e1bc416e5fe4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/8a58a020aca7f8f6122deb75fdc7e1bc416e5fe4"}],"sha":"d1026f356ba0feb7d9d8297f7981f7e594932081","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/d1026f356ba0feb7d9d8297f7981f7e594932081"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/8a58a020aca7f8f6122deb75fdc7e1bc416e5fe4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T15:41:36Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T15:41:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(tests): configure mail the way Jahia 8.2.4 expects, and fail loudly if it does not take (#107)\n\nui.emailFactor and ui.resetRequest have been failing on every run. Neither is a\nproduct bug: the harness configures mail through an API that Jahia 8.2.4.0\nturned into a no-op.\n\nMail delivery moved into a separate mail-service module configured through the\nOSGi PID org.jahia.modules.mail. The old MailService.store(MailSettings) call\nthis harness used still compiles and still returns without throwing - and\npersists nothing:\n\n  WARN [MailServiceImpl] - MailServiceImpl.store(MailSettings) is deprecated and\n       no longer persists anything; configure mail via the OSGi\n       org.jahia.modules.mail configuration instead.\n  WARN [MailServiceImpl] - No mail-service module is installed/configured;\n       message not sent.\n\nsendMessage() then also returns \"successfully\" while delivering nothing, so the\nwhole failure is invisible from the caller''s side. Measured on the stack before\nthis change: settings activated=false, uri=null, store() left activated=false,\nsend reported OK, Mailpit received zero messages. The specs simply timed out\nwaiting 20s for a mail nobody ever sent, which is why this read as Cypress\nflakiness - and why the two specs failed identically on unmodified main when\nA/B''d.\n\n- tests/assets/provisioning.yml installs the mail-service module and writes the\n  PID at stack startup. Both halves are required; the configuration alone does\n  nothing without the module.\n- tests/cypress/fixtures/groovy/setupMail.groovy and\n  tests/assets/setup-smtp-server.groovy now write that PID through\n  ConfigurationAdmin instead of the dead API, parsing SMTP_SERVER_URL from the\n  environment so they cannot drift from docker-compose.yml.\n- setupMail.groovy asserts afterwards that the configuration actually applied\n  and throws if not. A setup step that can fail silently eventually will, and\n  the cost lands on whoever debugs the symptom instead of the cause.\n\nVerified on a licensed Jahia 8.2 stack: mail service reports\n\"ready: host=smtp-server, port=1025\", a probe message reaches Mailpit, and\n\n  ui.emailFactor   3/3\n  ui.resetRequest  1/1\n  full phase 1     25/25 specs, 92/92 tests, All specs passed\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"4c03f4792b9fd2cd284cd6d8b5485c330ff6ab66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/4c03f4792b9fd2cd284cd6d8b5485c330ff6ab66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/8a58a020aca7f8f6122deb75fdc7e1bc416e5fe4","verification":{"payload":"tree 4c03f4792b9fd2cd284cd6d8b5485c330ff6ab66\nparent 578a853caa0e0dfee10f9290613bc67afdb7275f\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786635696 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786635696 +0200\n\nfix(tests): configure mail the way Jahia 8.2.4 expects, and fail loudly if it does not take (#107)\n\nui.emailFactor and ui.resetRequest have been failing on every run. Neither is a\nproduct bug: the harness configures mail through an API that Jahia 8.2.4.0\nturned into a no-op.\n\nMail delivery moved into a separate mail-service module configured through the\nOSGi PID org.jahia.modules.mail. The old MailService.store(MailSettings) call\nthis harness used still compiles and still returns without throwing - and\npersists nothing:\n\n  WARN [MailServiceImpl] - MailServiceImpl.store(MailSettings) is deprecated and\n       no longer persists anything; configure mail via the OSGi\n       org.jahia.modules.mail configuration instead.\n  WARN [MailServiceImpl] - No mail-service module is installed/configured;\n       message not sent.\n\nsendMessage() then also returns \"successfully\" while delivering nothing, so the\nwhole failure is invisible from the caller''s side. Measured on the stack before\nthis change: settings activated=false, uri=null, store() left activated=false,\nsend reported OK, Mailpit received zero messages. The specs simply timed out\nwaiting 20s for a mail nobody ever sent, which is why this read as Cypress\nflakiness - and why the two specs failed identically on unmodified main when\nA/B''d.\n\n- tests/assets/provisioning.yml installs the mail-service module and writes the\n  PID at stack startup. Both halves are required; the configuration alone does\n  nothing without the module.\n- tests/cypress/fixtures/groovy/setupMail.groovy and\n  tests/assets/setup-smtp-server.groovy now write that PID through\n  ConfigurationAdmin instead of the dead API, parsing SMTP_SERVER_URL from the\n  environment so they cannot drift from docker-compose.yml.\n- setupMail.groovy asserts afterwards that the configuration actually applied\n  and throws if not. A setup step that can fail silently eventually will, and\n  the cost lands on whoever debugs the symptom instead of the cause.\n\nVerified on a licensed Jahia 8.2 stack: mail service reports\n\"ready: host=smtp-server, port=1025\", a probe message reaches Mailpit, and\n\n  ui.emailFactor   3/3\n  ui.resetRequest  1/1\n  full phase 1     25/25 specs, 92/92 tests, All specs passed\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfeWwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5PgQAI+NL3BKmAesNaw3oxd0Vm0y\nwOMDacL3YPVPka6JT/9za5fWgSZE+/NKhHMCoF/cmLzpBkckqolTSA0A9/T8zFcv\nzsmjeyv0x/Wfzo2CmrxepvdtD5GpXC1s7W7X91Sl1kg5fCWfTvHzF4KsEPUTsXPd\nFz0jYUvwZnnylXHPuPOtZpd6BU6Nstv/dw8R/jIrLyHtyThJEYb+H661F