"}],"sha":"8a58a020aca7f8f6122deb75fdc7e1bc416e5fe4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/8a58a020aca7f8f6122deb75fdc7e1bc416e5fe4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/578a853caa0e0dfee10f9290613bc67afdb7275f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:56:48Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:56:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: record that the /cms/login gate is scoped to global enforcement (#106)\n\nAn adversarial review found that the gate - valve and filter both - is inert\nwhenever enforcedFactors is empty: MfaLoginGateDecision.isGated() asks\nMfaGlobalPolicy.isEnforcementActive() first, and that is just\n!enforcedFactors.isEmpty(). loginGate.enabled does not change it, because the\nfilter reads that switch only after isGated() has returned true and the valve\nnever reads it at all.\n\nThe consequence an operator needs: on a per-site opt-in deployment\n(enforcedFactors empty, totp.enabled=true on a site) an enrolled user IS\nchallenged through the MFA login UI, but /cms/login still authenticates on the\npassword alone, and the session it grants is global rather than site-scoped.\n\nReviewed and accepted as the gate''s designed scope - it is the counterpart of\nglobal enforcement, and gating a platform-wide endpoint off one site''s opt-in\nfeature would refuse it for everyone. Documenting it so the choice is informed:\nenforce globally if you want /cms/login covered, or refuse the endpoint at the\nreverse proxy and route users to the MFA login UI.\n\nREADME (gate section), the shipped .cfg where an operator sets loginGate.enabled,\nand AGENTS.md so it is not mistaken for an oversight and ''fixed''.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e7409190c176ad5f79ab695f9f87d4b45d11c30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/0e7409190c176ad5f79ab695f9f87d4b45d11c30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/578a853caa0e0dfee10f9290613bc67afdb7275f","verification":{"payload":"tree 0e7409190c176ad5f79ab695f9f87d4b45d11c30\nparent 6f8563a2fd458959165e966c2c815501d0a63e4c\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786633008 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786633008 +0200\n\ndocs: record that the /cms/login gate is scoped to global enforcement (#106)\n\nAn adversarial review found that the gate - valve and filter both - is inert\nwhenever enforcedFactors is empty: MfaLoginGateDecision.isGated() asks\nMfaGlobalPolicy.isEnforcementActive() first, and that is just\n!enforcedFactors.isEmpty(). loginGate.enabled does not change it, because the\nfilter reads that switch only after isGated() has returned true and the valve\nnever reads it at all.\n\nThe consequence an operator needs: on a per-site opt-in deployment\n(enforcedFactors empty, totp.enabled=true on a site) an enrolled user IS\nchallenged through the MFA login UI, but /cms/login still authenticates on the\npassword alone, and the session it grants is global rather than site-scoped.\n\nReviewed and accepted as the gate''s designed scope - it is the counterpart of\nglobal enforcement, and gating a platform-wide endpoint off one site''s opt-in\nfeature would refuse it for everyone. Documenting it so the choice is informed:\nenforce globally if you want /cms/login covered, or refuse the endpoint at the\nreverse proxy and route users to the MFA login UI.\n\nREADME (gate section), the shipped .cfg where an operator sets loginGate.enabled,\nand AGENTS.md so it is not mistaken for an oversight and ''fixed''.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfdswCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoGoQAKxOHyVt7SnoP7m45np2ab1+\nBDgPSeqgzuq1jdk88Sma4qFLDHjcuPD5hy0zu3dctTmUqhS7dsS0Oid0ipnC6Hzh\nxE8ksUF9ezpwGg4WzQ+SWhTOcbUIbrItwG7JpLec8RtzONnCnTUEf8NldONavsKG\nRQVL0Z3T3Wz20DW89fvrDvNue5IvmGISwib7tR3UBmFC4kE/YEAZSZdNIw1dAvUJ\noO/AgPjx44Umk5PaSD+qV+8ChyAYyRW+CJxebvIaAY/fSDQXeFavh2GuEO6xTVo/\n+zAm5jLcKHgtMUSatfr5SHCIOt+FO2II/nizDpclfBdXjkulqSa9+Z5YSZWwizcl\neD+Niajm3ExVlQyz7UcwQiHHBtseIaVCTGS3w+oYcT97wxNyHnp27Nta0dmtd5kj\nf9ENcnzK+nAxV5dnHfM8Y8CbtkEOpxAb+5j8JpM8KzRXr/p23JZKGDdAn+4lHQqn\n6XivTGqwWex6PO5SZKgYvgJODLLkp7ive7qk5nF7zuw7LN0xU7KW8d37YHkhxDQA\n18fa0tKQCLgSUOWqzOE5Puwj8SHCC85vNvjMCbE3y0p4VT2TKi+XVz/3tk802Rb/\nz5EPWfu8bnlkgxgZ4bK5Sv10gzdxCVkd/AqAcdWA3L3pA1q58unZ1I93zHDHKrkv\n4QEGlfzzvtJQqQIQAZE9\n=NAEF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T15:07:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/578a853caa0e0dfee10f9290613bc67afdb7275f","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDU3OGE4NTNjYWEwZTBkZmVlMTBmOTI5MDYxM2JjNjdhZmRiNzI3NWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/6f8563a2fd458959165e966c2c815501d0a63e4c","sha":"6f8563a2fd458959165e966c2c815501d0a63e4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/6f8563a2fd458959165e966c2c815501d0a63e4c"}],"sha":"578a853caa0e0dfee10f9290613bc67afdb7275f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/578a853caa0e0dfee10f9290613bc67afdb7275f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/6f8563a2fd458959165e966c2c815501d0a63e4c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:56:02Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:56:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): restrict GITHUB_TOKEN to contents: read (#105)\n\nCodeQL alert 3 (actions/missing-workflow-permissions, medium): the CI workflow\nnever constrains GITHUB_TOKEN, so it inherits the repository default - commonly\nread/write on every scope. A build job has no business holding write access to\nissues, packages or the contents API; if any build step or a transitive\ndependency of it were compromised, that token is what an attacker would reach\nfor.\n\ncontents: read is all this workflow needs. Checkout reads the repo, and\nactions/upload-artifact uses the artifact service rather than the REST API, so\nit requires no extra scope. The comment on the block says so, and says that\nanything added later which writes back to the repository must widen it\ndeliberately instead of inheriting it.\n\nValidated with yaml.safe_load: one job, five steps, push and pull_request\ntriggers unchanged.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"d08f9044c26882a6796db0b0da49a125ebd2e014","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/d08f9044c26882a6796db0b0da49a125ebd2e014"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/6f8563a2fd458959165e966c2c815501d0a63e4c","verification":{"payload":"tree d08f9044c26882a6796db0b0da49a125ebd2e014\nparent 8fbed195e4532e79de92d69819fc7b84488183d1\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786632962 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786632962 +0200\n\nfix(ci): restrict GITHUB_TOKEN to contents: read (#105)\n\nCodeQL alert 3 (actions/missing-workflow-permissions, medium): the CI workflow\nnever constrains GITHUB_TOKEN, so it inherits the repository default - commonly\nread/write on every scope. A build job has no business holding write access to\nissues, packages or the contents API; if any build step or a transitive\ndependency of it were compromised, that token is what an attacker would reach\nfor.\n\ncontents: read is all this workflow needs. Checkout reads the repo, and\nactions/upload-artifact uses the artifact service rather than the REST API, so\nit requires no extra scope. The comment on the block says so, and says that\nanything added later which writes back to the repository must widen it\ndeliberately instead of inheriting it.\n\nValidated with yaml.safe_load: one job, five steps, push and pull_request\ntriggers unchanged.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfdsCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAs7gQAE3o7lgUwj1eOZ6BCSRT24t8\n0OTAtas1fjwzw7OfATcpV+hpyWCmtasamGoj+ITFgwB4kCswPGWepabzt2Wy8Wjg\nnJRfnwGXKx3SElJFeqbutrTe8W6CBD4uO0CVs8GnSZq4AVOer9HqHS6Zs2b+jGtY\n2bTKYoKxhPKBl77Q7FR/NAHJCAvlO+aOKm1ig0k5oLP2dvEm3yZP0SFzuPnq0Oy3\nPG+49GRKF71DbeEGmYc0U9EZZ1V9RfbHCICLCo49s7Nqk7HxM3E0sGHWOnfGpZyE\nIw/JFJvKCE+i5mRZUeXjepCndcf8FOBpKKoJZoOan8Z8jGjIlDP51GKnT4ELlDSp\ne8afzFKwCY4RDe5uyud3XBc93h/iXDmJKgePial6oAu2tPI7odmFNr4YmVm/Gox9\nwU4Ry1QD/vxCjQEM6p9K6H2g8vi/XTG0YMx1FCXkT/NR1OR+AVsaoG/p3N7C9Lhn\nWjSC2jHyQmASxx/YRG3SZGzBeVo0VFoalazCpi/etccz4Ud5LEIf6kvet+zMfXd/\nLsoHtAhzt2HEkHePYUyiiahqwQuiq3q0jbq9+p/IUkp2+s+4Wl9W3xP15svFgUsu\nR1BLzaxEpyB6Admw02vk4p3m3VS5C+Aj9cbdpFm6Xespawdkvv1aFOgXb4RvyOt8\nyGFlaOXpiUStrqPqyRVn\n=BJeh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T15:06:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.git