"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/619079?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eallais/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eallais/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eallais/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eallais/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eallais","id":619079,"login":"eallais","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTA3OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eallais/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eallais/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eallais/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eallais/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eallais/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eallais","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/0cd5e149b8f025069a323cb43cc6739363324980","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDBjZDVlMTQ5YjhmMDI1MDY5YTMyM2NiNDNjYzY3MzkzNjMzMjQ5ODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/1eb4a2a61f6180dfc045d951bec26d383f3e6862","sha":"1eb4a2a61f6180dfc045d951bec26d383f3e6862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/1eb4a2a61f6180dfc045d951bec26d383f3e6862"}],"sha":"0cd5e149b8f025069a323cb43cc6739363324980","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/0cd5e149b8f025069a323cb43cc6739363324980"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/1eb4a2a61f6180dfc045d951bec26d383f3e6862/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:27:35Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:27:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: SUPPORT-646 coverage across MFA submodules (extensions/totp/webauthn/login-ui) (#94)\n\n* test(extensions): cover U8 fail-open window, F11 resolver anti-IDOR, U2 valve no-register\n\n- MfaLoginGateFailOpenWindowTest: characterization of the <=60s no-site fail-open\n  window (U8); documents that MfaSiteConfigService.updated() does not invalidate the\n  decision''s enforcingCache. Labeled for Stage-7 fix (flip assertion after wiring).\n- MfaSessionFactorsResolverTest: anti-IDOR guard that mfaSessionFactors takes no user\n  argument + result wrapper is a session-scoped immutable view (F11).\n- MfaLoginGateAuthValveTest: activate() no-register path when the authPipeline bean is\n  unresolvable (U2).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(totp): cover F16/D2 key-source order and U5 enroll reuse/regenerate\n\n- TotpSecretKeySourceTest: operator config key wins and is load-bearing (a different\n  key cannot decrypt); no-config auto-generates a per-install owner-only key file that\n  is random (not a compiled-in constant); blank config falls back to the file; a source\n  scan asserts no hardcoded key literal (F16/D2 key-source sub-gap).\n- TotpEnrollReuseStateTest: enroll() reuses a within-TTL transient secret and regenerates\n  an expired one, driven through the mutation''s real session-backed state storage (U5).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(webauthn): cover F25 assertion ceremony, U10 provider guards, U9 UV=PREFERRED\n\n- WebAuthnAssertionCeremonyTest (F25): real yubico finishAssertion ceremony with a\n  fixed EC P-256 keypair and a hand-built, correctly-signed assertion. Valid assertion\n  authenticates; wrong origin / wrong rpId / stale challenge each rejected. Unit half of\n  F25; the CDP virtual-authenticator e2e is a Cypress spec (Stage 6).\n- WebAuthnFactorProviderVerifyTest (U10): ownership post-check rejects an unowned\n  credential; a valid assertion whose sign counter cannot be persisted is refused\n  (clone-detection integrity). Fake-subclass pattern, no Mockito.\n- WebAuthnServiceUserVerificationTest (U9): registration + assertion options use\n  UserVerificationRequirement.PREFERRED, guarding against a silent DISCOURAGED downgrade.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(e2e): add F25 assertion-verify, D5/F18/F19/F29 negative gates, D4 degrade, F34 a11y\n\nCypress specs (write/lint only; Stage 6 runs them under docker):\n- graphQL.adminGates.negative: siteSettings public-read succeeds for a non site-admin\n  while auditEvents/enrollmentReport/resetUser* are denied, both factors (D5, F18, F19, F29).\n- ui.webauthn.login: returning-user passkey assertion verify (prepare->get()->verify) via a\n  CDP virtual authenticator (F25 e2e half; unit half in WebAuthnAssertionCeremonyTest).\n- ui.webauthn.softWire + docker-compose.totp-only.yml: login-ui degrades gracefully with the\n  webauthn bundle absent (D4).\n- ui.a11y + cypress-axe/axe-core deps: WCAG 2.2 AAA axe sweep, keyboard + live-region checks (F34).\n\ntests/ has no node_modules locally, so eslint/tsc are deferred to Stage 6.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore(webauthn): add mockito-inline (test) for JCR-bound store tests\n\nJUnit-4-compatible mockito-inline 4.11.0 (test scope) to mock the static\nJCRTemplate.getInstance() and Jahia''s concrete JCR wrapper types, which the\nsubclass-fake pattern cannot reach. Used by the U14 report-cap and D6\nno-private-key store tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(webauthn): cover U14 report scan-cap and D6 no-private-key persistence\n\n- WebAuthnRegistrationReportTest (U14): registration report scan-capped at 5000, not-\n  registered list capped at min(limit,1000) with truncated flag, guest excluded.\n- WebAuthnCredentialWriteTest (D6): addCredential writes only public credential properties\n  (COSE public key persisted; never any private/secret property).\nJCR faked via mockStatic(JCRTemplate) + Jahia wrapper mocks/proxies.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore(totp): add mockito-inline + test-scoped guava for JCR-bound store tests\n\nmockito-inline 4.11.0 mocks the static JCRTemplate.getInstance() and concrete\nJCRUserNode/JCRPropertyWrapper; guava (test scope) is required so Mockito can subclass\nJCRUserNode, whose API references guava types (shipped at runtime via jahia-impl, and\ntransitively in webauthn via yubico, but absent from totp''s compile graph).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(totp): cover U14 report scan-cap, U3 lazy re-encryption, D8 grace re-grant\n\n- TotpEnrollmentReportTest (U14): report scan-capped at 5000, not-enrolled list capped at\n  min(limit,1000) with truncated flag, guest excluded.\n- TotpUserStoreJcrTest (U3): verifyAndConsumeTotp transparently re-encrypts a legacy\n  plaintext secret on the next successful verify. (D8): clearGrace zeroes graceStartedAt and\n  the next getOrStartGraceMillis re-grants a fresh window (grace not permanently consumed).\nJCR faked via mockStatic(JCRTemplate) + Jahia wrapper/node mocks.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore(extensions): add mockito-inline (test) for the rate limiter fail-open test\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(extensions): cover U6 management rate limiter fail-open on JCR error\n\nMfaManagementRateLimiterFailOpenTest: isLockedOut/recordFailure fail OPEN (return false)\nwhen the JCR system session throws, so the brute-force throttle degrades gracefully while\nJCR is unhealthy without over-blocking (the underlying code check still gates). Null-user\nshort-circuit never touches JCR. Window arithmetic remains covered by the per-factor tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(e2e): make Stage-5 Cypress specs runnable and green\n\nRun the full harness for the first time and fix genuine test-harness issues in\nthe four new (write-only) specs:\n\n- open security.profile via a provisioning.yml step so the admin-gate NEGATIVE\n  specs (D5/F18/F19/F29) reach the MFA resolvers; the module''s own\n  requireSiteAdmin gate is what must deny non site-admins, not the api-security\n  transport layer (which returns a generic ''Permission denied'' for any non-root\n  user under the default profile).\n- F25 (ui.webauthn.login): drop the enrollment-chooser click on the first visit\n  — with a single enforced factor the EnrollmentChooser (shown only for >1\n  factor) is skipped and the registration form renders directly.\n- F34 (ui.a11y): scope the guest-prompt axe sweep to the MFA sign-in surface;\n  the sole violation (html-has-lang) is on the enclosing login page''s <html>,\n  owned by the UPA test template-set, not this module.\n- D4 (ui.webauthn.softWire): run on a dedicated TOTP-only stack (webauthn bundle\n  absent) via ci.build.sh (jars-totp-only) + a two-phase ci.startup.sh\n  (--no-deps on the phase-2 cypress run so compose does not recreate jahia back\n  to the all-factors volume). Rewrite the assertion to the real graceful-degrade\n  invariant (TOTP usable, no white-screen) and characterize the current\n  always-rendered WebauthnSection, labeled for Stage-7 inversion once soft-wiring\n  is implemented.\n\nResult: JUnit 288 green; login-ui Vitest 39 green; Cypress 85 tests / 25 specs\ngreen (24 all-factors + 1 TOTP-only).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(extensions): close U8 <=60s MFA login-gate fail-open on site-config change\n\nMfaLoginGateDecision caches the no-site ''any site enforcing?'' answer for\n60s and invalidated it only on provider bind/unbind and its own\n@Activate/@Modified - never when MfaSiteConfigService changed per-site\nconfig. Enabling a factor on the FIRST site therefore left a bounded\nwindow where /cms/login still authenticated password-only: a fail-open\nin a security gate.\n\nFix: MfaSiteConfigService now fires a new MfaSiteConfigChangeListener on\nupdated()/deleted()/save(); MfaLoginGateDecision implements it and drops\nits enforcing cache. The reverse edge (config service -> decision) is an\nOPTIONAL/DYNAMIC reference, so it cannot form an OSGi activation cycle\nwith the decision''s existing mandatory reference to the config service\n(verified: both components activate cleanly in a live Jahia). Behaviour\nis otherwise identical - only a config CHANGE now promptly invalidates.\n\nInvert the U8 characterization test into a regression guard\n(MfaLoginGateEnforcingCacheInvalidationTest) asserting the window is\nclosed; remove the old MfaLoginGateFailOpenWindowTest.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(login-ui): truly soft-wire WebAuthn when the factor bundle is absent (D4)\n\nOn a node without mfa-factors-webauthn, the self-service settings panel\nrendered <WebauthnSection> unconditionally, so the absent mfaWebauthn\nGraphQL type surfaced an error (plus a non-functional ''add passkey'')\ninstead of the section being omitted. Degradation was already safe (TOTP\nusable, no white-screen) - this removes the UX wart.\n\nwebauthnStatus() now detects the schema-absence signal - a top-level\nGraphQL error with extensions.classification == ''ValidationError'', which\nfor its fixed query can only mean the mfaWebauthn field/type is not in\nthe schema (bundle not installed) - and returns { unavailable: true }.\nWebauthnSection renders nothing in that case. A genuine runtime error\ncarries a different classification and still shows an error, so real\nfailures are not silently hidden. The all-factors path is unchanged.\n\n(Response shape verified against a live webauthn-absent Jahia node:\nerrors[].extensions.classification=''ValidationError'', data:null.)\n\nInvert the D4 characterization spec to assert the section, its error\nbanner and the add-passkey button are all absent; add Vitest coverage\nfor the unavailable vs runtime-error branches.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* docs: correct stale UPA version and tests/README to match source\n\n- README Requirements: UPA api is 0.2.0 (the version <upa.version> pins\n  and the modules build against), not the stale ''0.3.0+''.\n- tests/README: retitle from TOTP-only to the full mfa-factors-* suite,\n  fix artifactIds (mfa-factors-* not user-password-authentication-\n  mfa-factors-totp-*), document the two-phase run (all-factors +\n  TOTP-only soft-wire) and security.profile=open provisioning, and\n  refresh the spec inventory to the current 25 specs.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"edd2bd6efdbef30c4ee36232732a592722d05d79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/edd2bd6efdbef30c4ee36232732a592722d05d79"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/1eb4a2a61f6180dfc045d951bec26d383f3e6862","verification":{"payload":"tree edd2bd6efdbef30c4ee36232732a592722d05d79\nparent 8ebb38d2198127ec860974039e13f700572c259f\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1784100455 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784100455 +0200\n\ntest: SUPPORT-646 coverage across MFA submodules (extensions/totp/webauthn/login-ui) (#94)\n\n* test(extensions): cover U8 fail-open window, F11 resolver anti-IDOR, U2 valve no-register\n\n- MfaLoginGateFailOpenWindowTest: characterization of the <=60s no-site fail-open\n  window (U8); documents that MfaSiteConfigService.updated() does not invalidate the\n  decision''s enforcingCache. Labeled for Stage-7 fix (flip assertion after wiring).\n- MfaSessionFactorsResolverTest: anti-IDOR guard that mfaSessionFactors takes no user\n  argument + result wrapper is a session-scoped immutable view (F11).\n- MfaLoginGateAuthValveTest: activate() no-register path when the authPipeline bean is\n  unresolvable (U2).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(totp): cover F16/D2 key-source order and U5 enroll reuse/regenerate\n\n- TotpSecretKeySourceTest: operator config key wins and is load-bearing (a different\n  key cannot decrypt); no-config auto-generates a per-install owner-only key file that\n  is random (not a compiled-in constant); blank config falls back to the file; a source\n  scan asserts no hardcoded key literal (F16/D2 key-source sub-gap).\n- TotpEnrollReuseStateTest: enroll() reuses a within-TTL transient secret and regenerates\n  an expired one, driven through the mutation''s real session-backed state storage (U5).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(webauthn): cover F25 assertion ceremony, U10 provider guards, U9 UV=PREFERRED\n\n- WebAuthnAssertionCeremonyTest (F25): real yubico finishAssertion ceremony with a\n  fixed EC P-256 keypair and a hand-built, correctly-signed assertion. Valid assertion\n  authenticates; wrong origin / wrong rpId / stale challenge each rejected. Unit half of\n  F25; the CDP virtual-authenticator e2e is a Cypress spec (Stage 6).\n- WebAuthnFactorProviderVerifyTest (U10): ownership post-check rejects an unowned\n  credential; a valid assertion whose sign counter cannot be persisted is refused\n  (clone-detection integrity). Fake-subclass pattern, no Mockito.\n- WebAuthnServiceUserVerificationTest (U9): registration + assertion options use\n  UserVerificationRequirement.PREFERRED, guarding against a silent DISCOURAGED downgrade.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(e2e): add F25 assertion-verify, D5/F18/F19/F29 negative gates, D4 degrade, F34 a11y\n\nCypress specs (write/lint only; Stage 6 runs them under docker):\n- graphQL.adminGates.negative: siteSettings public-read succeeds for a non site-admin\n  while auditEvents/enrollmentReport/resetUser* are denied, both factors (D5, F18, F19, F29).\n- ui.webauthn.login: returning-user passkey assertion verify (prepare->get()->verify) via a\n  CDP virtual authenticator (F25 e2e half; unit half in WebAuthnAssertionCeremonyTest).\n- ui.webauthn.softWire + docker-compose.totp-only.yml: login-ui degrades gracefully with the\n  webauthn bundle absent (D4).\n- ui.a11y + cypress-axe/axe-core deps: WCAG 2.2 AAA axe sweep, keyboard + live-region checks (F34).\n\ntests/ has no node_modules locally, so eslint/tsc are deferred to Stage 6.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore(webauthn): add mockito-inline (test) for JCR-bound store tests\n\nJUnit-4-compatible mockito-inline 4.11.0 (test scope) to mock the static\nJCRTemplate.getInstance() and Jahia''s concrete JCR wrapper types, which the\nsubclass-fake pattern cannot reach. Used by the U14 report-cap and D6\nno-private-key store tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(webauthn): cover U14 report scan-cap and D6 no-private-key persistence\n\n- WebAuthnRegistrationReportTest (U14): registration report scan-capped at 5000, not-\n  registered list capped at min(limit,1000) with truncated flag, guest excluded.\n- WebAuthnCredentialWriteTest (D6): addCredential writes only public credential properties\n  (COSE public key persisted; never any private/secret property).\nJCR faked via mockStatic(JCRTemplate) + Jahia wrapper mocks/proxies.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore(totp): add mockito-inline + test-scoped guava for JCR-bound store tests\n\nmockito-inline 4.11.0 mocks the static JCRTemplate.getInstance() and concrete\nJCRUserNode/JCRPropertyWrapper; guava (test scope) is required so Mockito can subclass\nJCRUserNode, whose API references guava types (shipped at runtime via jahia-impl, and\ntransitively in webauthn via yubico, but absent from totp''s compile graph).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(totp): cover U14 report scan-cap, U3 lazy re-encryption, D8 grace re-grant\n\n- TotpEnrollmentReportTest (U14): report scan-capped at 5000, not-enrolled list capped at\n  min(limit,1000) with truncated flag, guest excluded.\n- TotpUserStoreJcrTest (U3): verifyAndConsumeTotp transparently re-encrypts a legacy\n  plaintext secret on the next successful verify. (D8): clearGrace zeroes graceStartedAt and\n  the next getOrStartGraceMillis re-grants a fresh window (grace not permanently consumed).\nJCR faked via mockStatic(JCRTemplate) + Jahia wrapper/node mocks.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore(extensions): add mockito-inline (test) for the rate limiter fail-open test\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(extensions): cover U6 management rate limiter fail-open on JCR error\n\nMfaManagementRateLimiterFailOpenTest: isLockedOut/recordFailure fail OPEN (return false)\nwhen the JCR system session throws, so the brute-force throttle degrades gracefully while\nJCR is unhealthy without over-blocking (the underlying code check still gates). Null-user\nshort-circuit never touches JCR. Window arithmetic remains covered by the per-factor tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(e2e): make Stage-5 Cypress specs runnable and green\n\nRun the full harness for the first time and fix genuine test-harness issues in\nthe four new (write-only) specs:\n\n- open security.profile via a provisioning.yml step so the admin-gate NEGATIVE\n  specs (D5/F18/F19/F29) reach the MFA resolvers; the module''s own\n  requireSiteAdmin gate is what must deny non site-admins, not the api-security\n  transport layer (which returns a generic ''Permission denied'' for any non-root\n  user under the default profile).\n- F25 (ui.webauthn.login): drop the enrollment-chooser click on the first visit\n  — with a single enforced factor the EnrollmentChooser (shown only for >1\n  factor) is skipped and the registration form renders directly.\n- F34 (ui.a11y): scope the guest-prompt axe sweep to the MFA sign-in surface;\n  the sole violation (html-has-lang) is on the enclosing login page''s <html>,\n  owned by the UPA test template-set, not this module.\n- D4 (ui.webauthn.softWire): run on a dedicated TOTP-only stack (webauthn bundle\n  absent) via ci.build.sh (jars-totp-only) + a two-phase ci.startup.sh\n  (--no-deps on the phase-2 cypress run so compose does not recreate jahia back\n  to the all-factors volume). Rewrite the assertion to the real graceful-degrade\n  invariant (TOTP usable, no white-screen) and characterize the current\n  always-rendered WebauthnSection, labeled for Stage-7 inversion once soft-wiring\n  is implemented.\n\nResult: JUnit 288 green; login-ui Vitest 39 green; Cypress 85 tests / 25 specs\ngreen (24 all-factors + 1 TOTP-only).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(extensions): close U8 <=60s MFA login-gate fail-open on site-config change\n\nMfaLoginGateDecision caches the no-site ''any site enforcing?'' answer for\n60s and invalidated it only on provider bind/unbind and its own\n@Activate/@Modified - never when MfaSiteConfigService changed per-site\nconfig. Enabling a factor on the FIRST site therefore left a bounded\nwindow where /cms/login still authenticated password-only: a fail-open\nin a security gate.\n\nFix: MfaSiteConfigService now fires a new MfaSiteConfigChangeListener on\nupdated()/deleted()/save(); MfaLoginGateDecision implements it and drops\nits enforcing cache. The reverse edge (config service -> decision) is an\nOPTIONAL/DYNAMIC reference, so it cannot form an OSGi activation cycle\nwith the decision''s existing mandatory reference to the config service\n(verified: both components activate cleanly in a live Jahia). Behaviour\nis otherwise identical - only a config CHANGE now promptly invalidates.\n\nInvert the U8 characterization test into a regression guard\n(MfaLoginGateEnforcingCacheInvalidationTest) asserting the window is\nclosed; remove the old MfaLoginGateFailOpenWindowTest.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(login-ui): truly soft-wire WebAuthn when the factor bundle is absent (D4)\n\nOn a node without mfa-factors-webauthn, the self-service settings panel\nrendered <WebauthnSection> unconditionally, so the absent mfaWebauthn\nGraphQL type surfaced an error (plus a non-functional ''add passkey'')\ninstead of the section being omitted. Degradation was already safe (TOTP\nusable, no white-screen) - this removes the UX wart.\n\nwebauthnStatus() now detects the schema-absence signal - a top-level\nGraphQL error with extensions.classification == ''ValidationError'', which\nfor its fixed query can only mean the mfaWebauthn field/type is not in\nthe schema (bundle not installed) - and returns { unavailable: true }.\nWebauthnSection renders nothing in that case. A genuine runtime error\ncarries a different classification and still shows an error, so real\nfailures are not silently hidden. The all-factors path is unchanged.\n\n(Response shape verified against a live webauthn-absent Jahia node:\nerrors[].extensions.classification=''ValidationError'', data:null.)\n\nInvert the D4 characterization spec to assert the section, its error\nbanner and the add-passkey button are all absent; add Vitest coverage\nfor the unavailable vs runtime-error branches.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* docs: correct stale UPA version and tests/README to match source\n\n- README Requirements: UPA api is 0.2.0 (the version <upa.version> pins\n  and the modules build against), not the stale ''0.3.0+''.\n- tests/README: retitle from TOTP-only to the full mfa-factors-* suite,\n  fix artifactIds (mfa-factors-* not user-password-authentication-\n  mfa-factors-totp-*), document the two-phase run (all-factors +\n  TOTP-only soft-wire) and security.profile=open provisioning, and\n  refresh the spec inventory to the current 25 specs.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVzZnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAclIQAI0if05BEh8AkqJsBx642Gec\ncobxXyU7f2RrRjO1gGU0YuhqChrBg3vcipf1kS15cLPhb4rlPUd1Hh6wbRymRhF7\nes6DqWTUVi575beiU6QjT7LRKAlBDrf6efkFILdeiCoTPqhsOj/ve01h4NpcE8Hz\nagc5Kw/i+RTbWdbVGTr65hhs6TV5TyoRT+dZ6U10qizEPLl9or4pEb2fQad9qr0d\n+7Qrhk9GF2VGNudkn3XLJd0ql5qx6LPNaypDiDfFjKAnZ+ox6A3rY3RWHw96Mi81\nvJi7o4yZnw4n54f1Gfv+XMjFkkKkrJV9BzPUB7z+6lndnzdx8gIUNDl1L0GEFwKv\npbMNreeUXgdsFVAg8GLm9Qgc6Ik082p/Nu4rlrRyIHoppjLmHElLCEUKC3514gmr\n9J/ELyqcF9BXwyN7DgAikNYjdeRzSZ1RdTlC+WD8Jml6HdiF+CE/qpLTqUpDwwx0\n+8XmVFdj9+rHrDHsa0GFcLKPBSgkgWeYegDEpkH0vUcLGLSBTJ2pxDji774upwHq\nJJ1Qtgzh86oaaCtYuafS9hRHUEKxOxZTNiyRdG+BdlNSaK0fqwYJVx9x9LLm5PK/\nhSVz3nRa0sdezeG1S3D2NtzJu7oyefgZrQOG+xMOWC+iZrmcbvX7ngFtWcRRRLdi\nL2IczlgXWxIrtbVXC17L\n=2cfV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T07:27:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/1eb4a2a61f6180dfc045d951bec26d383f3e6862","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDFlYjRhMmE2MWY2MTgwZGZjMDQ1ZDk1MWJlYzI2ZDM4M2YzZTY4NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/8ebb38d2198127ec860974039e13f700572c259f","sha":"8ebb38d2198127ec860974039e13f700572c259f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/8ebb38d2198127ec860974039e13f700572c259f"}],"sha":"1eb4a2a61f6180dfc045d951bec26d383f3e6862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/1eb4a2a61f6180dfc045d951bec26d383f3e6862"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/8ebb38d2198127ec860974039e13f700572c259f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T17:26:57Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T17:26:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: MFA /cms/login gate ipWhitelist bypass behind Tomcat RemoteIpValve (GHSA-4v3g-mcmj-83fp) (#71)\n\n* fix: resolve raw TCP peer for MFA login-gate whitelist, not getRemoteAddr()\n\nrequest.getRemoteAddr() is not a spoof-proof client IP when Tomcat''s\nRemoteIpValve is in the chain (enabled by default on the Jahia EE image):\nthe valve itself rewrites getRemoteAddr() from X-Forwarded-For before this\ncode runs whenever the immediate TCP peer falls in its (permissive by\ndefault) internalProxies range. That made the SEC-135 fix''s\n\"safe\" fallback (loginGate.trustForwardedFor=false) just as spoofable as\ntrusting the header directly, letting an unauthenticated attacker bypass\nthe MFA-enforced /cms/login gate with a single forged header\n(GHSA-4v3g-mcmj-83fp).\n\nRead the pre-rewrite peer address the valve stashes in its own\naccess-log request attribute instead - populated straight from the TCP\nconnection, so it can never be influenced by a header.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: ship loginGate.trustForwardedFor=false by default, harden e2e coverage\n\nThe SEC-135 fix (PR #69) changed the Java code''s in-memory default for\nloginGate.trustForwardedFor to false, but never touched the actual shipped\norg.jahia.modules.mfa.extensions.cfg resource — which still set\nloginGate.trustForwardedFor=true with the old pre-fix rationale. Since\nKaraf''s ConfigurationAdmin always applies every key from the deployed\ndefault file, every fresh install was actually running with the\npre-SEC-135, directly XFF-trusting default the whole time, independent of\nthe RemoteIpValve nuance in GHSA-4v3g-mcmj-83fp.\n\nAlso extend the http.loginGate.cy.ts e2e spec: several existing assertions\nimplicitly relied on that stale default to pass (sending a forged,\nwhitelisted X-Forwarded-For and expecting 200). They now explicitly opt\ninto trustForwardedFor for the cases that genuinely test that behavior,\nand a new test reproduces the GHSA-4v3g-mcmj-83fp bypass directly - this\nsuite''s own Jahia container ships Tomcat''s RemoteIpValve enabled by\ndefault, and the cypress container''s docker-network peer already falls\ninside its default trusted range, so the existing harness exercises the\nreal topology with no extra proxy setup needed.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: harden tests/set-env.sh against comment lines in .env(.example)\n\nexport $(cat .env | sed ''s/=.*//g'' | xargs) chokes on comment/blank lines\nin .env.example (e.g. \"# Compose project name...\"), which sed leaves\nuntouched and xargs then splits into invalid export identifiers, aborting\nthe script under `set -e`. Filter comments and blank lines before the\nsed/xargs pipeline so ci.build.sh/ci.startup.sh actually run.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: correct the RemoteIpValve mitigation - Tomcat never exposes the pre-rewrite peer\n\nRunning the new e2e regression test end-to-end against the real Jahia EE\ndev image (Tomcat 9.0.120) proved the previous fix (reading\norg.apache.catalina.AccessLog.RemoteAddr as a \"pre-rewrite\" address) was a\nno-op: decompiling RemoteIpValve.class shows it sets that attribute to\nrequest.getRemoteAddr() AFTER already overwriting it from\nX-Forwarded-For, so the attribute holds the same spoofed value, not the\noriginal. Tomcat does not preserve the true pre-rewrite peer anywhere\naccessible once this valve has run.\n\nFixed MfaLoginGateDecision to detect the rewrite itself instead of trying\nto undo it: Tomcat sets org.apache.tomcat.request.forwarded=true\nprecisely when it resolved the address from a header. With\nloginGate.trustForwardedFor=false, that flag now makes the gate fail\nCLOSED (never whitelisted) rather than trust an address it cannot verify.\n\nCorrected the unit tests, README, and Cypress spec comments that\ndescribed the disproven \"recover the raw peer\" mechanism. Also fixed\nui.admin.extensionsConfig.cy.ts, which asserted the OLD pre-SEC-135\ndefault (trustForwardedFor checked/true) for the admin UI toggle - the\nsame class of stale-default bug as the previously-fixed\nhttp.loginGate.cy.ts.\n\nVerified: full Cypress suite (21 specs / 72 tests) green against\nghcr.io/jahia/jahia-ee-dev:8-SNAPSHOT, including the GHSA-4v3g-mcmj-83fp\nregression test reproducing the real RemoteIpValve topology.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore(deps): bump pinned Node to v22.20.0 across JS-frontend modules\n\neslint-visitor-keys@5.0.1 (a transitive lint-only devDependency) now\nrequires Node ^20.19.0 || ^22.13.0 || >=24, so a clean `mvn package` on\nextensions/totp/webauthn (pinned v22.9.0) and login-ui (pinned v22.12.0)\nfailed yarn install outright with an engine-incompatibility error before\nany of our code ever built. Bump all four to v22.20.0 (latest Node 22\nLTS, satisfies the ^22.13.0 range) so the frontend-maven-plugin\ninstall-node-and-yarn step succeeds without workarounds.\n\nVerified: clean rebuild of all four modules succeeds with no\n--ignore-engines workaround; extensions unit tests still pass\n(33+9+7 tests).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"11edc421d094f60948304a0e8c79b02a89d52f4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/11edc421d094f60948304a0e8c79b02a89d52f4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/8ebb38d2198127ec860974039e13f700572c259f","verification":{"payload":"tree 11edc421d094f60948304a0e8c79b02a89d52f4d\nparent bc81d9757b43ba3fb228b9e2ef652419079137d7\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1783704417 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783704417 +0200\n\nfix: MFA /cms/login gate ipWhitelist bypass behind Tomcat RemoteIpValve (GHSA-4v3g-mcmj-83fp) (#71)\n\n* fix: resolve raw TCP peer for MFA login-gate whitelist, not getRemoteAddr()\n\nrequest.getRemoteAddr() is not a spoof-proof client IP when Tomcat''s\nRemoteIpValve is in the chain (enabled by default on the Jahia EE image):\nthe valve itself rewrites getRemoteAddr() from X-Forwarded-For before this\ncode runs whenever the immediate TCP peer falls in its (permissive by\ndefault) internalProxies range. That made the SEC-135 fix''s\n\"safe\" fallback (loginGate.trustForwardedFor=false) just as spoofable as\ntrusting the header directly, letting an unauthenticated attacker bypass\nthe MFA-enforced /cms/login gate with a single forged header\n(GHSA-4v3g-mcmj-83fp).\n\nRead the pre-rewrite peer address the valve stashes in its own\naccess-log request attribute instead - populated straight from the TCP\nconnection, so it can never be influenced by a header.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: ship loginGate.trustForwardedFor=false by default, harden e2e coverage\n\nThe SEC-135 fix (PR #69) changed the Java code''s in-memory default for\nloginGate.trustForwardedFor to false, but never touched the actual shipped\norg.jahia.modules.mfa.extensions.cfg resource — which still set\nloginGate.trustForwardedFor=true with the old pre-fix rationale. Since\nKaraf''s ConfigurationAdmin always applies every key from the deployed\ndefault file, every fresh install was actually running with the\npre-SEC-135, directly XFF-trusting default the whole time, independent of\nthe RemoteIpValve nuance in GHSA-4v3g-mcmj-83fp.\n\nAlso extend the http.loginGate.cy.ts e2e spec: several existing assertions\nimplicitly relied on that stale default to pass (sending a forged,\nwhitelisted X-Forwarded-For and expecting 200). They now explicitly opt\ninto trustForwardedFor for the cases that genuinely test that behavior,\nand a new test reproduces the GHSA-4v3g-mcmj-83fp bypass directly - this\nsuite''s own Jahia container ships Tomcat''s RemoteIpValve enabled by\ndefault, and the cypress container''s docker-network peer already falls\ninside its default trusted range, so the existing harness exercises the\nreal topology with no extra proxy setup needed.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: harden tests/set-env.sh against comment lines in .env(.example)\n\nexport $(cat .env | sed ''s/=.*//g'' | xargs) chokes on comment/blank lines\nin .env.example (e.g. \"# Compose project name...\"), which sed leaves\nuntouched and xargs then splits into invalid export identifiers, aborting\nthe script under `set -e`. Filter comments and blank lines before the\nsed/xargs pipeline so ci.build.sh/ci.startup.sh actually run.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: correct the RemoteIpValve mitigation - Tomcat never exposes the pre-rewrite peer\n\nRunning the new e2e regression test end-to-end against the real Jahia EE\ndev image (Tomcat 9.0.120) proved the previous fix (reading\norg.apache.catalina.AccessLog.RemoteAddr as a \"pre-rewrite\" address) was a\nno-op: decompiling RemoteIpValve.class shows it sets that attribute to\nrequest.getRemoteAddr() AFTER already overwriting it from\nX-Forwarded-For, so the attribute holds the same spoofed value, not the\noriginal. Tomcat does not preserve the true pre-rewrite peer anywhere\naccessible once this valve has run.\n\nFixed MfaLoginGateDecision to detect the rewrite itself instead of trying\nto undo it: Tomcat sets org.apache.tomcat.request.forwarded=true\nprecisely when it resolved the address from a header. With\nloginGate.trustForwardedFor=false, that flag now makes the gate fail\nCLOSED (never whitelisted) rather than trust an address it cannot verify.\n\nCorrected the unit tests, README, and Cypress spec comments that\ndescribed the disproven \"recover the raw peer\" mechanism. Also fixed\nui.admin.extensionsConfig.cy.ts, which asserted the OLD pre-SEC-135\ndefault (trustForwardedFor checked/true) for the admin UI toggle - the\nsame class of stale-default bug as the previously-fixed\nhttp.loginGate.cy.ts.\n\nVerified: full Cypress suite (21 specs / 72 tests) green against\nghcr.io/jahia/jahia-ee-dev:8-SNAPSHOT, including the GHSA-4v3g-mcmj-83fp\nregression test reproducing the real RemoteIpValve topology.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore(deps): bump pinned Node to v22.20.0 across JS-frontend modules\n\neslint-visitor-keys@5.0.1 (a transitive lint-only devDependency) now\nrequires Node ^20.19.0 || ^22.13.0 || >=24, so a clean `mvn package` on\nextensions/totp/webauthn (pinned v22.9.0) and login-ui (pinned v22.12.0)\nfailed yarn install outright with an engine-incompatibility error before\nany of our code ever built. Bump all four to v22.20.0 (latest Node 22\nLTS, satisfies the ^22.13.0 range) so the frontend-maven-plugin\ninstall-node-and-yarn step succeeds without workarounds.\n\nVerified: clean rebuild of all four modules succeeds with no\n--ignore-engines workaround; extensions unit tests still pass\n(33+9+7 tests).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUSthCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAku0QABG3NbeopSrwl1wXh55FXTjJ\nJi5FTDnKwi2p7YakV9IlpOIhVtTBZxt265YhrQEULFzNHreGHQoy+wva552I1saf\nvs8WJWS8XDMhWC5EMXmUHgjKOgzuO00ZsB3tczVlUyJHEg6tPy5OXjYBda3ke1Rg\nPztWFFJQf0YvndkY76TOdPcxyYjTUq+8Ef4CMwYO8NflXxIoCAwvIQD0zPH