rl":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/8f2f8ac8317f6c09563633774ba7b9d6c055c373/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-28T05:47:07Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-28T06:11:24Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"message":"fix: space the OTP digit boxes from the error/button below them\n\nThe error message (e.g. \"User ''anne'' does not have an email address\nconfigured.\") sat flush against the segmented digit boxes. Add margin-bottom\nto .otpGroup so the boxes are separated from the error/submit below, matching\nthe existing margin-top above. Applies to all OTP forms (login verify, email\ncode, enrollment).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"21bbff3c0f24f606b869c24d155ddad61fac343d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/21bbff3c0f24f606b869c24d155ddad61fac343d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/8f2f8ac8317f6c09563633774ba7b9d6c055c373","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/8f2f8ac8317f6c09563633774ba7b9d6c055c373","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDhmMmY4YWM4MzE3ZjZjMDk1NjM2MzM3NzRiYTdiOWQ2YzA1NWMzNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/e67b437ef3a9881f733f122f2ef7adac193ce068","sha":"e67b437ef3a9881f733f122f2ef7adac193ce068","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/e67b437ef3a9881f733f122f2ef7adac193ce068"}],"sha":"8f2f8ac8317f6c09563633774ba7b9d6c055c373","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/8f2f8ac8317f6c09563633774ba7b9d6c055c373"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/e67b437ef3a9881f733f122f2ef7adac193ce068/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-28T05:38:08Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-28T06:11:24Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"message":"fix: render ''Send a new code'' as a button, not a link\n\nThe email-code resend control was an underlined .toggleMode link. Render it as\nthe outlined .secondaryButton (matching the change-method control), so it reads\nas a clear action while staying subordinate to the primary verify button. It\nalready sits on its own line above the change-method button, so the two stack\ncleanly. No behavioral or testid change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"30357455abffc32432efac10881da63a97cc8eb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/30357455abffc32432efac10881da63a97cc8eb4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/e67b437ef3a9881f733f122f2ef7adac193ce068","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/e67b437ef3a9881f733f122f2ef7adac193ce068","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKGU2N2I0MzdlZjNhOTg4MWY3MzNmMTIyZjJlZjdhZGFjMTkzY2UwNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/08c48cbc071d1b4b74ab1930ac30635488e48bfd","sha":"08c48cbc071d1b4b74ab1930ac30635488e48bfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/08c48cbc071d1b4b74ab1930ac30635488e48bfd"}],"sha":"e67b437ef3a9881f733f122f2ef7adac193ce068","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/e67b437ef3a9881f733f122f2ef7adac193ce068"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/08c48cbc071d1b4b74ab1930ac30635488e48bfd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T21:06:41Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-28T05:35:16Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"message":"fix: enlarge shared login helper text to 1.125rem\n\n1rem still read as too small for the instructional sentences (scan QR, enter\nsecret manually, enter the 6-digit code, webauthn ''your browser will ask...'').\nBump the shared .helpText to 1.125rem with line-height 1.5 so every step''s\ninstructions are comfortably readable; #555-on-white stays AAA (7.46:1).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"872b9bbcbb70a880dc9a5a176693db9dd6512535","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/872b9bbcbb70a880dc9a5a176693db9dd6512535"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/08c48cbc071d1b4b74ab1930ac30635488e48bfd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/08c48cbc071d1b4b74ab1930ac30635488e48bfd","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDA4YzQ4Y2JjMDcxZDFiNGI3NGFiMTkzMGFjMzA2MzU0ODhlNDhiZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/d0cbf0e1feec9713ba434777f682d1d73e972057","sha":"d0cbf0e1feec9713ba434777f682d1d73e972057","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/d0cbf0e1feec9713ba434777f682d1d73e972057"}],"sha":"08c48cbc071d1b4b74ab1930ac30635488e48bfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/08c48cbc071d1b4b74ab1930ac30635488e48bfd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/d0cbf0e1feec9713ba434777f682d1d73e972057/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T20:53:42Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-28T05:35:16Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"message":"fix: render the change-method control as a button, not a link\n\n''Choose a different setup method'' (and the verify-screen ''Use a different\nmethod'') was an underlined .toggleMode link. Render it as an outlined\nsecondary button (.secondaryButton): clearly a button, but visually\nsubordinate to each form''s primary submit. Blue-on-white stays AAA (8.05:1)\nfor label and border; it joins the focus-visible group.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"13b1196d06aa6760cd2c16bbe76213fa4241de48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/13b1196d06aa6760cd2c16bbe76213fa4241de48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/d0cbf0e1feec9713ba434777f682d1d73e972057","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/d0cbf0e1feec9713ba434777f682d1d73e972057","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKGQwY2JmMGUxZmVlYzk3MTNiYTQzNDc3N2Y2ODJkMWQ3M2U5NzIwNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/9f526bf05862d686e5651234916297babfd37331","sha":"9f526bf05862d686e5651234916297babfd37331","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/9f526bf05862d686e5651234916297babfd37331"}],"sha":"d0cbf0e1feec9713ba434777f682d1d73e972057","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/d0cbf0e1feec9713ba434777f682d1d73e972057"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/9f526bf05862d686e5651234916297babfd37331/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T20:51:30Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-28T05:35:16Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"message":"fix: bump login helper text from 0.9rem to 1rem\n\nThe instructional sentences under each step heading (e.g. ''Your account must\nbe protected by a second factor...'') used the shared .helpText at 0.9rem,\nwhich read as too small. Use the standard 1rem body size; the #555-on-white\ncontrast stays AAA (7.46:1, size-independent).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e89112ba2ac0ab9adffa9e8c32a2abe082c3697","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/0e89112ba2ac0ab9adffa9e8c32a2abe082c3697"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/9f526bf05862d686e5651234916297babfd37331","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/9f526bf05862d686e5651234916297babfd37331","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDlmNTI2YmYwNTg2MmQ2ODZlNTY1MTIzNDkxNjI5N2JhYmZkMzczMzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/19a27b403cd61c4b738a8ac20a3cd1005f6c0fb4","sha":"19a27b403cd61c4b738a8ac20a3cd1005f6c0fb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/19a27b403cd61c4b738a8ac20a3cd1005f6c0fb4"}],"sha":"9f526bf05862d686e5651234916297babfd37331","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/9f526bf05862d686e5651234916297babfd37331"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/19a27b403cd61c4b738a8ac20a3cd1005f6c0fb4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T20:50:19Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-28T05:35:16Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"message":"fix: remove the stray focus box around the login step headings\n\nEach step moves focus to its <h2> for step-change focus management (WCAG\n2.4.3). The heading is tabIndex=-1 (programmatic focus only, never\nkeyboard-reachable), so the browser''s default focus ring drew a box around the\ntitle (e.g. ''Set up two-factor authentication''). Suppress the outline on\n.main h2:focus. Keyboard-focusable controls (buttons, links) keep their\nvisible focus styles, so WCAG 2.4.7 is unaffected.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"0fd0ab9aa50ce4726c0a01c6d81e1efd2d6691fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/0fd0ab9aa50ce4726c0a01c6d81e1efd2d6691fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/19a27b403cd61c4b738a8ac20a3cd1005f6c0fb4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/19a27b403cd61c4b738a8ac20a3cd1005f6c0fb4","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDE5YTI3YjQwM2NkNjFjNGI3MzhhOGFjMjBhM2NkMTAwNWY2YzBmYjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/68635bb6f839bc71a511894d467eedfc6b208594","sha":"68635bb6f839bc71a511894d467eedfc6b208594","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/68635bb6f839bc71a511894d467eedfc6b208594"}],"sha":"19a27b403cd61c4b738a8ac20a3cd1005f6c0fb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/19a27b403cd61c4b738a8ac20a3cd1005f6c0fb4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/68635bb6f839bc71a511894d467eedfc6b208594/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T20:31:40Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T20:47:16Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"message":"fix: MFA audit page - contain the table and restore vertical page scroll\n\nOn /jahia/administration/<site>/mfa-community-audit two layout bugs combined\nonce events were loaded:\n\n1. Horizontal: the events table was width:100% with auto layout, so a single\n   long, unbreakable detail value (IP, user agent, message) pushed the whole\n   table - and the admin window - past the viewport. Fixed with\n   table-layout:fixed + an explicit colgroup (the free-form detail column takes\n   the remainder) and cell wrapping (overflowWrap/word-break); the timestamp\n   stays one line. Deliberately NOT an overflow-x:auto wrapper: overflow-x:auto\n   forces overflow-y to compute as auto, which inside the admin panel created a\n   nested scroll container.\n\n2. Vertical: moonstone-alpha ContentLayout stacks flex:1/min-height:0 layers\n   with NO overflow, so content taller than the panel (a loaded 50-row table)\n   was clipped with no scrollbar - ''no vertical elevator''. The audit page now\n   gives its content slot a full-width outer scroll container\n   (flex:1 1 0; min-height:0; overflow-y:auto) so the scrollbar sits at the\n   window''s right edge, with an inner div capping the readable content width.\n\nApplied to both the totp and webauthn audit pages and sections.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"741bd4aac230d8d274055f58759e4a5324ef5e33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/741bd4aac230d8d274055f58759e4a5324ef5e33"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/68635bb6f839bc71a511894d467eedfc6b208594","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/68635bb6f839bc71a511894d467eedfc6b208594","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDY4NjM1YmI2ZjgzOWJjNzFhNTExODk0ZDQ2N2VlZGZjNmIyMDg1OTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/342cca6b10cc930b6159348b76ab46401f4cf28a","sha":"342cca6b10cc930b6159348b76ab46401f4cf28a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/342cca6b10cc930b6159348b76ab46401f4cf28a"}],"sha":"68635bb6f839bc71a511894d467eedfc6b208594","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/68635bb6f839bc71a511894d467eedfc6b208594"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/342cca6b10cc930b6159348b76ab46401f4cf28a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T20:25:10Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T20:47:13Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"message":"fix: red alert style for sign-in errors and a button for Restart login\n\n- Error messages now render in a red alert box (light-red background + red\n  border around the dark-red text) so a sign-in problem reads clearly as an\n  error. Styled on the inner <p> so the always-present outer div never shows\n  an empty box; #a00000 on #fff5f5 stays AAA (~7.9:1).\n- The fatal-error screen''s Restart login control now uses the primary\n  .submitButton style instead of the underlined .toggleMode link, matching the\n  buttons on the other screens.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"425a9be6fd561e7973e32370c821075bc077afb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/425a9be6fd561e7973e32370c821075bc077afb9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/342cca6b10cc930b6159348b76ab46401f4cf28a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/342cca6b10cc930b6159348b76ab46401f4cf28a","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDM0MmNjYTZiMTBjYzkzMGI2MTU5MzQ4Yjc2YWI0NjQwMWY0Y2YyOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/5f73aa26c54472ddf352419f26df024fbb2e7d86","sha":"5f73aa26c54472ddf352419f26df024fbb2e7d86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/5f73aa26c54472ddf352419f26df024fbb2e7d86"}],"sha":"342cca6b10cc930b6159348b76ab46401f4cf28a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/342cca6b10cc930b6159348b76ab46401f4cf28a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/5f73aa26c54472ddf352419f26df024fbb2e7d86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T20:25:10Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T20:47:13Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"message":"fix: center the Login button in the sign-in form\n\nThe submit button sat left-aligned because, unlike the other forms, it was\nnot wrapped in a centering container. Wrap it in a text-align:center div\n(same pattern as the TOTP enrollment form) so the inline-block button centers\nhorizontally.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"e969ab0236cb2501db534e26bf55285eee325b7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/e969ab0236cb2501db534e26bf55285eee325b7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/5f73aa26c54472ddf352419f26df024fbb2e7d86","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/5f73aa26c54472ddf352419f26df024fbb2e7d86","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDVmNzNhYTI2YzU0NDcyZGRmMzUyNDE5ZjI2ZGYwMjRmYmIyZTdkODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/31d015a7a93d94c507d0e4deeb85190e7a046505","sha":"31d015a7a93d94c507d0e4deeb85190e7a046505","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/31d015a7a93d94c507d0e4deeb85190e7a046505"}],"sha":"5f73aa26c54472ddf352419f26df024fbb2e7d86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/5f73aa26c54472ddf352419f26df024fbb2e7d86"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/31d015a7a93d94c507d0e4deeb85190e7a046505/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T20:20:08Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T20:47:13Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"message":"fix: add spacing between the OTP instruction text and the digit boxes\n\nThe segmented OTP boxes sat flush against the instruction line above them\n(most visible on the TOTP enrollment screen). Add margin-top to .otpGroup so\nthe boxes have clear separation from the preceding text, consistently across\nthe login-verification, email-code and enrollment forms.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"5299a83affb28647465387ccd839e3a3beba1133","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/5299a83affb28647465387ccd839e3a3beba1133"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/31d015a7a93d94c507d0e4deeb85190e7a046505","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/31d015a7a93d94c507d0e4deeb85190e7a046505","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDMxZDAxNWE3YTkzZDk0YzUwN2QwZTRkZWViODUxOTBlN2EwNDY1MDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/851c4ba1738bb2a88de5c93bbd8b1a7faf973597","sha":"851c4ba1738bb2a88de5c93bbd8b1a7faf973597","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/851c4ba1738bb2a88de5c93bbd8b1a7faf973597"}],"sha":"31d015a7a93d94c507d0e4deeb85190e7a046505","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/31d015a7a93d94c507d0e4deeb85190e7a046505"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/851c4ba1738bb2a88de5c93bbd8b1a7faf973597/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T20:11:58Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T20:13:20Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"message":"fix: block password-only /cms/login MFA bypass via auth valve\n\nA POST to the legacy /cms/login endpoint with only username/password\nauthenticated the session, fully bypassing MFA on a site that enforces\nenrollment. Jahia authenticates that POST inside its authentication\npipeline, which runs BEFORE module servlet filters, so the existing\nMfaLoginGateFilter could only redirect the response after the session was\nalready authenticated (it appeared to gate GET only because a GET carries\nno credentials).\n\nClose it at the root with a Jahia auth valve inserted immediately before\nLoginEngineAuthValve:\n\n- MfaLoginGateAuthValve (Declarative Services; the module has no Spring\n  context) resolves the authPipeline bean via SpringContextSingleton and\n  registers/unregisters itself on @Activate/@Deactivate. It short-circuits\n  a gated, non-whitelisted password-login attempt BEFORE authentication,\n  redirecting to the configured MFA login page (or 403 when none is\n  distinct). The IP whitelist remains the operator''s emergency door.\n- Extract the shared whitelist/gating/URL-resolution logic into\n  MfaLoginGateDecision, consumed by both the valve and the (now thin)\n  servlet filter so the two never drift.\n- The hard gate now reroutes a blocked client to the configured login URL\n  instead of always returning 403.\n\nCypress: http.loginGate asserts a password POST is rerouted before auth\n(no jid cookie issued) and the whitelist escape hatch still works.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"261f1a8d2035b8949f2f3a6e76429402aa29264c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/261f1a8d2035b8949f2f3a6e76429402aa29264c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/851c4ba1738bb2a88de5c93bbd8b1a7faf973597","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/851c4ba1738bb2a88de5c93bbd8b1a7faf973597","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDg1MWM0YmExNzM4YmIyYTg4ZGU1YzkzYmJkOGIxYTdmYWY5NzM1OTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/f2805699abc4f9a8413e125630af92eb60fc33b7","sha":"f2805699abc4f9a8413e125630af92eb60fc33b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/f2805699abc4f9a8413e125630af92eb60fc33b7"}],"sha":"851c4ba1738bb2a88de5c93bbd8b1a7faf973597","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/851c4ba1738bb2a88de5c93bbd8b1a7faf973597"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/f2805699abc4f9a8413e125630af92eb60fc33b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T20:11:41Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T20:13:20Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"message":"feat: segmented per-digit OTP input with paste and auto-verify\n\nThe single OTP text field was too narrow for six digits and required a\nmanual submit. Introduce a reusable segmented OtpInput (one box per digit)\nused across the login verification, email-code and login-time enrollment\nforms:\n\n- one <input> per digit inside a labelled role=\"group\"; left-packed digit\n  model; auto-advance on entry, Backspace/Arrow navigation, and full\n  paste support (drop 6 digits anywhere, fills from the first box);\n- auto-verifies once the last digit is entered (no submit click);\n- autoComplete=\"one-time-code\" on the first box; WCAG per-digit labels\n  (factor.otp.digitLabel) and a 44px min touch target.\n\nThe TOTP-dashboard EnrollDialog keeps its single Moonstone input + explicit\nconfirm button (separate module, not the login-ui surface).\n\nCypress: new fillOtp/pasteOtp helpers; login/enroll/email specs drive the\nsegmented field; added a paste-6-digits test.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"a37845de7fed2cf9c0fbdf163747821cb373b26e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/a37845de7fed2cf9c0fbdf163747821cb373b26e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/f2805699abc4f9a8413e125630af92eb60fc33b7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/f2805699abc4f9a8413e125630af92eb60fc33b7","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKGYyODA1Njk5YWJjNGY5YTg0MTNlMTI1NjMwYWY5MmViNjBmYzMzYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/ef17e35b03a19f0854ae54729c551b355824d6bf","sha":"ef17e35b03a19f0854ae54729c551b355824d6bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/ef17e35b03a19f0854ae54729c551b355824d6bf"}],"sha":"f2805699abc4f9a8413e125630af92eb60fc33b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/f2805699abc4f9a8413e125630af92eb60fc33b7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/ef17e35b03a19f0854ae54729c551b355824d6bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T18:08:37Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T18:08:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: harden MFA module from blind multi-dimensional review (#22)\n\n* fix: harden MFA module from blind multi-dimensional review\n\nAddresses findings from a blind review across architecture, security, code\nquality, ergonomy, accessibility (AAA), test coverage and documentation.\n\nArchitecture / security (extensions):\n- Close the startup fail-OPEN window: MfaSiteConfigService eagerly + synchronously\n  scans karaf.etc on @Activate and exposes isReady(); the /cms/login gate fails\n  CLOSED on the no-site path while not ready (was a second-factor bypass during boot).\n- Reject config injection: per-site group names are validated (no CR/LF/comma/''=''/''#'')\n  at the single chokepoint before they reach the shared .cfg.\n- Synchronize updated()/deleted() on the same writeLock as save() (lost-update window).\n- Guard global loginUrl/logoutUrl against dangerous schemes on both write\n  (MfaExtensionsConfigSupport) and read (MfaLoginLogoutProvider).\n- Add loginGate.trustForwardedFor (default true) so operators can disable XFF trust.\n- Fix PID-rename stale entry; reserved-key guard in parse(); orphan-group warning.\n\nData integrity (totp):\n- TotpSiteSettings save now does a true partial URL update (null arg = keep,\n  \"\" = clear, \"/path\" = set), fixing silent erasure of per-site URLs on a\n  factor-only update.\n\nAccessibility - WCAG 2.2 AAA (login-ui + admin UIs):\n- aria-hidden on decorative <hr>; focus management on WebauthnRegistrationForm;\n  aria-busy on the login submit; :focus-visible for injected anchor links and all\n  admin native inputs; lang attribute from the request locale; humanised factor\n  labels; aria-describedby on dialog inputs.\n\nErgonomy:\n- Audit/report sections get empty + error + loading states; contrast-safe disabled\n  fields; backup codes require an explicit \"I have saved them\" acknowledgement before\n  dismissal (+ non-color copy cue); per-dialog error scoping; reset in-flight label.\n\nTests:\n- New MfaSiteConfigService concurrency/readiness/path-traversal/karaf.base/url-only\n  tests; TotpSiteSettingsStoreTest + WebAuthnSiteSettingsStoreTest; gate XFF + not-ready\n  tests; global-URL guard tests; Cypress now asserts the per-site .cfg is created and\n  deleted, and that omitted URLs are preserved.\n\nDocumentation:\n- README updated for the file-backed per-site config (removed stale JCR mixin\n  references, added the per-site .cfg schema); CND deprecation notes expanded.\n\nVerified: full GraalVM build + all unit tests green; SonarQube quality gate PASSED\n(0 issues); Cypress 62/62.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR blind-review findings (round 2)\n\nFrom an adversarial review of the PR diff:\n\n- totp: per-site URL update now tracks loginUrl/logoutUrl INDEPENDENTLY (provided\n  field = set/clear, omitted field = keep) - fixes the residual data-loss where\n  supplying one URL silently erased the sibling. New regression tests.\n- gate: hoist the MfaSiteConfigService.isReady() fail-CLOSED guard above site-key\n  resolution so BOTH the site-resolved and no-site /cms/login paths fail closed\n  during the startup window (was only the no-site path).\n- config service: eager-scan map mutation now under writeLock; pid-mapping deferral\n  documented.\n- global URL validation: single shared MfaUrls.isSafeGlobalRedirectUrl used by both\n  the write (GraphQL) and read (provider) paths (was drifting heuristics).\n- accessibility (AAA): focus placement on WebAuthn verify unsupported branch;\n  aria-busy on the TOTP verify submit; removed role=alert double-announce race on the\n  backup-codes heading; aria-describedby on both WebAuthn forms'' errors; clearer\n  backup-codes acknowledgement label.\n- tests: true read-modify-write concurrency + updated()/save() lock-serialization\n  tests; gate stands-down-when-ready test; getSiteConfigFile now asserts HTTP 200 and\n  throws on parse failure (no vacuous pass); Cypress asserts both URLs survive a\n  partial update.\n\nBuild + all unit tests green; SonarQube gate PASSED (0 issues); CodeQL PASSED;\nCypress 62/62.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: complete login-ui AAA error-association + focus parity\n\nDelta-review follow-ups (no regressions found in round 2; these are pre-existing\nparity gaps, fixed because AAA is required):\n\n- TotpCodeVerificationForm / EmailCodeVerificationForm submit buttons now carry\n  aria-describedby to their error containers (and email also aria-busy), matching\n  the WebAuthn forms (WCAG 4.1.3 / 1.3.1).\n- FatalErrorScreen restart button stays mounted and disabled+aria-busy during the\n  in-flight state instead of unmounting (keeps keyboard focus; WCAG 2.4.3).\n- WebauthnRegistrationForm mount-focus effect: documented why [supported] is the\n  correct, exhaustive dependency.\n\nBuild + all unit tests green; SonarQube gate PASSED (0 issues); Cypress 62/62.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"8e3766530b1e62a171bb38df652f34455fd39e5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/8e3766530b1e62a171bb38df652f34455fd39e5f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/ef17e35b03a19f0854ae54729c551b355824d6bf","verification":{"payload":"tree 8e3766530b1e62a171bb38df652f34455fd39e5f\nparent d877fe4df0423f808b49210f23d0a2bb5b2f1742\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1782583717 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782583717 +0200\n\nfix: harden MFA module from blind multi-dimensional review (#22)\n\n* fix: harden MFA module from blind multi-dimensional review\n\nAddresses findings from a blind review across architecture, security, code\nquality, ergonomy, accessibility (AAA), test coverage and documentation.\n\nArchitecture / security (extensions):\n- Close the startup fail-OPEN window: MfaSiteConfigService eagerly + synchronously\n  scans karaf.etc on @Activate and exposes isReady(); the /cms/login gate fails\n  CLOSED on the no-site path while not ready (was a second-factor bypass during boot).\n- Reject config injection: per-site group names are validated (no CR/LF/comma/''=''/''#'')\n  at the single chokepoint before they reach the shared .cfg.\n- Synchronize updated()/deleted() on the same writeLock as save() (lost-update window).\n- Guard global loginUrl/logoutUrl against dangerous schemes on both write\n  (MfaExtensionsConfigSupport) and read (MfaLoginLogoutProvider).\n- Add loginGate.trustForwardedFor (default true) so operators can disable XFF trust.\n- Fix PID-rename stale entry; reserved-key guard in parse(); orphan-group warning.\n\nData integrity (totp):\n- TotpSiteSettings save now does a true partial URL update (null arg = keep,\n  \"\" = clear, \"/path\" = set), fixing silent erasure of per-site URLs on a\n  factor-only update.\n\nAccessibility - WCAG 2.2 AAA (login-ui + admin UIs):\n- aria-hidden on decorative <hr>; focus management on WebauthnRegistrationForm;\n  aria-busy on the login submit; :focus-visible for injected anchor links and all\n  admin native inputs; lang attribute from the request locale; humanised factor\n  labels; aria-describedby on dialog inputs.\n\nErgonomy:\n- Audit/report sections get empty + error + loading states; contrast-safe disabled\n  fields; backup codes require an explicit \"I have saved them\" acknowledgement before\n  dismissal (+ non-color copy cue); per-dialog error scoping; reset in-flight label.\n\nTests:\n- New MfaSiteConfigService concurrency/readiness/path-traversal/karaf.base/url-only\n  tests; TotpSiteSettingsStoreTest + WebAuthnSiteSettingsStoreTest; gate XFF + not-ready\n  tests; global-URL guard tests; Cypress now asserts the per-site .cfg is created and\n  deleted, and that omitted URLs are preserved.\n\nDocumentation:\n- README updated for the file-backed per-site config (removed stale JCR mixin\n  references, added the per-site .cfg schema); CND deprecation notes expanded.\n\nVerified: full GraalVM build + all unit tests green; SonarQube quality gate PASSED\n(0 issues); Cypress 62/62.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR blind-review findings (round 2)\n\nFrom an adversarial review of the PR diff:\n\n- totp: per-site URL update now tracks loginUrl/logoutUrl INDEPENDENTLY (provided\n  field = set/clear, omitted field = keep) - fixes the residual data-loss where\n  supplying one URL silently erased the sibling. New regression tests.\n- gate: hoist the MfaSiteConfigService.isReady() fail-CLOSED guard above site-key\n  resolution so BOTH the site-resolved and no-site /cms/login paths fail closed\n  during the startup window (was only the no-site path).\n- config service: eager-scan map mutation now under writeLock; pid-mapping deferral\n  documented.\n- global URL validation: single shared MfaUrls.isSafeGlobalRedirectUrl used by both\n  the write (GraphQL) and read (provider) paths (was drifting heuristics).\n- accessibility (AAA): focus placement on WebAuthn verify unsupported branch;\n  aria-busy on the TOTP verify submit; removed role=alert double-announce race on the\n  backup-codes heading; aria-describedby on both WebAuthn forms'' errors; clearer\n  backup-codes acknowledgement label.\n- tests: true read-modify-write concurrency + updated()/save() lock-serialization\n  tests; gate stands-down-when-ready test; getSiteConfigFile now asserts HTTP 200 and\n  throws on parse failure (no vacuous pass); Cypress asserts both URLs survive a\n  partial update.\n\nBuild + all unit tests green; SonarQube gate PASSED (0 issues); CodeQL PASSED;\nCypress 62/62.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: complete login-ui AAA error-association + focus parity\n\nDelta-review follow-ups (no regressions found in round 2; these are pre-existing\nparity gaps, fixed because AAA is required):\n\n- TotpCodeVerificationForm / EmailCodeVerificationForm submit buttons now carry\n  aria-describedby to their error containers (and email also aria-busy), matching\n  the WebAuthn forms (WCAG 4.1.3 / 1.3.1).\n- FatalErrorScreen restart button stays mounted and disabled+aria-busy during the\n  in-flight state instead of unmounting (keeps keyboard focus; WCAG 2.4.3).\n- WebauthnRegistrationForm mount-focus effect: documented why [supported] is the\n  correct, exhaustive dependency.\n\nBuild + all unit tests green; SonarQube gate PASSED (0 issues); Cypress 62/62.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQBGlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoL8QAI4YNzOYkEVv3uV8PE82mt94\nFO21kkv8+j9YIXQ+DSj8my/3TL9Otymm45v0Od8PGbHs/FWt3ut9ye1TBED3UV6q\nW2F3LvFmpcKQcI7GfHUV8sjQ07mJQs6RnTIultLkjshKdFN2lBcG0b3c0OPEe5sT\nvf4+fS70LNTzrU4PLMmzaE6Em0d9OIMmyU/hhYKrXdE5mpSJa/HjQ3aOMA+U2Ifg\nr1/FrfmBODcN/X+h5Cy67NC2cbu/WaO5L3QYxteFVGI7RMEyz2oMjCxCB6/5ChVE\nriqFp1z7kU3czBAdSSxUqRSXp546jV8XNjlDKqEsEL+xGwIndaHsm5OD864f/kin\nScsYU57GVzHMp7rJgsF2Ox3H450YoW9YkokVKt3IjOwKAEelC1FDilVHwxERup0o\nImXKHqcp1zUcr8fqvf5jA/ZB3Pvy6+sD+D4Ei0WzECmMerdhVSYhRGuUmfZfKJiJ\neMxSIEdWiqUPsrKsqcUNH8Mqta8NO+PPIWsIL/Ym87iqsMnfdfOxUzA6ZLFakOBX\nvhaKaOSHrOBBoZ4uwiyWJ7wB7rvGqPc4NR+kK/gkP4rFXtudJKHpUaV4nLrEJ/uB\nNGIyck5NpVbr+NTZTjcV+3jdkJvJlZGhpPenXGRlQ+7yxzgTAtCzgHq550Fa9MHy\n4nWpTOj7h0wf+eLh1i3T\n=S8mM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-27T18:08:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/ef17e35b03a19f0854ae54729c551b355824d6bf","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKGVmMTdlMzViMDNhMTlmMDg1NGFlNTQ3MjljNTUxYjM1NTgyNGQ2YmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/d877fe4df0423f808b49210f23d0a2bb5b2f1742","sha":"d877fe4df0423f808b49210f23d0a2bb5b2f1742","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/d877fe4df0423f808b49210f23d0a2bb5b2f1742"}],"sha":"ef17e35b03a19f0854ae54729c551b355824d6bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/ef17e35b03a19f0854ae54729c551b355824d6bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/d877fe4df0423f808b49210f23d0a2bb5b2f1742/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T15:42:11Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T15:42:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: store per-site MFA settings in file-backed OSGi factory config (#21)\n\nPer-site MFA settings (loginUrl, logoutUrl, per-factor enabled/enabledGroups) were\nstored as JCR mixins on each site node, so operators could not see or manage them as\nfiles in karaf/etc, and the login/logout URLs were awkwardly TOTP-owned despite being\nfactor-agnostic.\n\nMove all per-site settings into a single file-backed OSGi factory configuration, one\n.cfg per site, owned by the extensions bundle:\n\n- MfaSiteConfig: immutable per-site snapshot (URLs + Map<factorType, {enabled, groups}>)\n  with copy-on-write withUrls()/withFactor() merge primitives.\n- MfaSiteConfigService: a ManagedServiceFactory (factory PID\n  org.jahia.modules.mfa.extensions.site). Felix FileInstall delivers each\n  org.jahia.modules.mfa.extensions.site-<siteKey>.cfg to updated(); save() merges only\n  the calling factor''s slice (so TOTP and WebAuthn never clobber each other in the\n  shared file), updates the in-memory map synchronously for immediate read-after-write,\n  and writes the file atomically (temp in the same dir + ATOMIC_MOVE). All-default\n  config deletes the file. siteKey is validated as a safe single path segment before\n  building the filename (path-traversal guard). Never uses\n  ConfigurationAdmin.createFactoryConfiguration (bundle-scoped, orphaned on reinstall);\n  the file is the source of truth.\n\n- MfaLoginLogoutProvider reads the per-site URLs straight from MfaSiteConfigService\n  (URLs are factor-agnostic); the SPI loses getLoginUrl/getLogoutUrl. MfaSiteProvider\n  keeps only the activation/configured queries.\n- Totp/WebAuthnSiteSettingsStore drop JCR and delegate to MfaSiteConfigService, keeping\n  their snapshot DTOs and the GraphQL/UI contract unchanged (setSiteSettings still gates\n  on requireSiteAdmin — the sole write-authz barrier now that JCR ACLs are gone).\n- MfaSiteSettingsStoreBase (JCR base) deleted. CND *:siteSettings mixins kept but marked\n  deprecated so existing site nodes stay valid (no migration — handled manually).\n\nNote: enabledGroups is a comma-separated string in the .cfg (an OSGi String[] cannot be\nexpressed reliably in a .cfg), owned-split like the global enforcedFactors.\n\nTests: new MfaSiteConfigServiceTest (parse/merge/atomic-write/all-default-delete/\npath-traversal/anySiteEnabled round-trips) + two per-site MfaLoginLogoutProvider tests.\nBuild (JDK 17) + all unit tests green; Sonar gate PASSED (0 issues); Cypress 59/59;\nverified live on :9080 (GraphQL write -> .cfg in karaf/etc -> /start redirects to the\nper-site /login.html).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"c26f2c0005779944d27df1b125c208f539a9a423","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/c26f2c0005779944d27df1b125c208f539a9a423"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/d877fe4df0423f808b49210f23d0a2bb5b2f1742","verification":{"payload":"tree c26f2c0005779944d27df1b125c208f539a9a423\nparent cd81abce392ad6ec8f34f6b9d1393c31e06ad755\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1782574931 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782574931 +0200\n\nfeat: store per-site MFA settings in file-backed OSGi factory config (#21)\n\nPer-site MFA settings (loginUrl, logoutUrl, per-factor enabled/enabledGroups) were\nstored as JCR mixins on each site node, so operators could not see or manage them as\nfiles in karaf/etc, and the login/logout URLs were awkwardly TOTP-owned despite being\nfactor-agnostic.\n\nMove all per-site settings into a single file-backed OSGi factory configuration, one\n.cfg per site, owned by the extensions bundle:\n\n- MfaSiteConfig: immutable per-site snapshot (URLs + Map<factorType, {enabled, groups}>)\n  with copy-on-write withUrls()/withFactor() merge primitives.\n- MfaSiteConfigService: a ManagedServiceFactory (factory PID\n  org.jahia.modules.mfa.extensions.site). Felix FileInstall delivers each\n  org.jahia.modules.mfa.extensions.site-<siteKey>.cfg to updated(); save() merges only\n  the calling factor''s slice (so TOTP and WebAuthn never clobber each other in the\n  shared file), updates the in-memory map synchronously for immediate read-after-write,\n  and writes the file atomically (temp in the same dir + ATOMIC_MOVE). All-default\n  config deletes the file. siteKey is validated as a safe single path segment before\n  building the filename (path-traversal guard). Never uses\n  ConfigurationAdmin.createFactoryConfiguration (bundle-scoped, orphaned on reinstall);\n  the file is the source of truth.\n\n- MfaLoginLogoutProvider reads the per-site URLs straight from MfaSiteConfigService\n  (URLs are factor-agnostic); the SPI loses getLoginUrl/getLogoutUrl. MfaSiteProvider\n  keeps only the activation/configured queries.\n- Totp/WebAuthnSiteSettingsStore drop JCR and delegate to MfaSiteConfigService, keeping\n  their snapshot DTOs and the GraphQL/UI contract unchanged (setSiteSettings still gates\n  on requireSiteAdmin — the sole write-authz barrier now that JCR ACLs are gone).\n- MfaSiteSettingsStoreBase (JCR base) deleted. CND *:siteSettings mixins kept but marked\n  deprecated so existing site nodes stay valid (no migration — handled manually).\n\nNote: enabledGroups is a comma-separated string in the .cfg (an OSGi String[] cannot be\nexpressed reliably in a .cfg), owned-split like the global enforcedFactors.\n\nTests: new MfaSiteConfigServiceTest (parse/merge/atomic-write/all-default-delete/\npath-traversal/anySiteEnabled round-trips) + two per-site MfaLoginLogoutProvider tests.\nBuild (JDK 17) + all unit tests green; Sonar gate PASSED (0 issues); Cypress 59/59;\nverified live on :9080 (GraphQL write -> .cfg in karaf/etc -> /start redirects to the\nper-site /login.html).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqP+9TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9iEQAAQwfvcvlJG8ZQAR6w+JaYhg\nSY+teqUfCRgz3dFqtboohBLscrDFE66pbi9W7E4lLywGQ2finAFHZdpcLQxYhZtS\n8+8noOwt2SZOMHiHt1Cumw9C264REqAYTwFlMH3rWDC3Cl4LvhwVY7sXU7ZCaNqS\nhoOtpr8KjMdAIXp88yoBl5IQgoIzgFfn/PXR/UVk0fyj13CMFzqD7K/4ARC7RUrs\ngmpU/6MMS5kS5vTeGgni2w1oD8A6jWPl4JJh5EPhkgy4tbYZoJph9B1PHXkdWUyK\nbaRvdz0QH6dwRtpQVUW8mzzhcHVlJxsbpe4eVJoUEXhJsDe3BYPHHyOb1Y1pbKWA\ntjll9swpMkjAqFtcyyESVV45MYUaivB6g+PIOAT5BtGcpBWt3wJtrzBzdGVfAMlx\nstD8/4GwC5E0C/CsZPFJYwMq4y6MngwEqjT6EFRyzLdid+dUAR5la7aoXM3qGqEv\nOOTOmc6lTXbnd8IfQJ13NYpw94/FbENDryg6A0DyHOFMU0gHNHZjb9U5gV2EXQUL\nh+iptQkmFECXeaWnaV1xftBj7L/ZYsJES/CT4TUHE3SK/ZXod1LRTMIboV0Qobtz\noe+LoWdRO0/3XtWQi/dp+SSQLyVx4lGQBpt1xWKZGU3E5xRhcxviNStuul5KRGuM\nm8Ob731edJ+Z33MHg02F\n=feI5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-27T15:42:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/d877fe4df0423f808b49210f23d0a2bb5b2f1742","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKGQ4NzdmZTRkZjA0MjNmODA4YjQ5MjEwZjIzZDBhMmJiNWIyZjE3NDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/cd81abce392ad6ec8f34f6b9d1393c31e06ad755","sha":"cd81abce392ad6ec8f34f6b9d1393c31e06ad755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/cd81abce392ad6ec8f34f6b9d1393c31e06ad755"}],"sha":"d877fe4df0423f808b49210f23d0a2bb5b2f1742","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/d877fe4df0423f808b49210f23d0a2bb5b2f1742"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/cd81abce392ad6ec8f34f6b9d1393c31e06ad755/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T14:18:21Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T14:18:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: never use a /modules resource URI as the login/logout redirect target (#20)\n\nconfig.logoutUrl (and loginUrl) is baked into the per-request\n/modules/jahia-user-entries/configs/jahiaUserEntries.js config asset. When Jahia\ngenerates that asset the current request IS the asset, so redirectTarget() captured\nits URL as the post-logout destination; /cms/logout then honored that dead-end\n.js URL instead of the real page, stranding the user on it.\n\nBroaden the request-URI guard (renamed isAuthOrErrorEndpoint ->\nisNonRedirectableEndpoint) to also reject /modules/... URIs: module resources\n(static assets, GraphQL, the provisioning API, and the jahiaUserEntries.js config\nitself) are never a renderable page the user could have been on. redirectTarget now\nreturns null for them, leaving config.logoutUrl as a clean /cms/logout that only\ncarries Jahia core''s own redirect to the current page.\n\nVerified on the local :9080 instance (config.logoutUrl went from\n/cms/logout?redirect=%2Fmodules%2F...jahiaUserEntries.js...&redirect=/start to\n/cms/logout?redirect=/start) and Cypress 59/59.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"18f94d0f08d67e3d4a1013b8cd926f6f39b6d2ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/18f94d0f08d67e3d4a1013b8cd926f6f39b6d2ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/cd81abce392ad6ec8f34f6b9d1393c31e06ad755","verification":{"payload":"tree 18f94d0f08d67e3d4a1013b8cd926f6f39b6d2ef\nparent bceb4ba9a49137e07089d8bae8fe00608d21f732\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1782569901 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782569901 +0200\n\nfix: never use a /modules resource URI as the login/logout redirect target (#20)\n\nconfig.logoutUrl (and loginUrl) is baked into the per-request\n/modules/jahia-user-entries/configs/jahiaUserEntries.js config asset. When Jahia\ngenerates that asset the current request IS the asset, so redirectTarget() captured\nits URL as the post-logout destination; /cms/logout then honored that dead-end\n.js URL instead of the real page, stranding the user on it.\n\nBroaden the request-URI guard (renamed isAuthOrErrorEndpoint ->\nisNonRedirectableEndpoint) to also reject /modules/... URIs: module resources\n(static assets, GraphQL, the provisioning API, and the jahiaUserEntries.js config\nitself) are never a renderable page the user could have been on. redirectTarget now\nreturns null for them, leaving config.logoutUrl as a clean /cms/logout that only\ncarries Jahia core''s own redirect to the current page.\n\nVerified on the local :9080 instance (config.logoutUrl went from\n/cms/logout?redirect=%2Fmodules%2F...jahiaUserEntries.js...&redirect=/start to\n/cms/logout?redirect=/start) and Cypress 59/59.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqP9utCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsSMQAGEYLYpj1bvfg9VcQ7qUhlDa\nyAiF8k8RKepNWPh0ZyIK2dViD1YU4dYs9ddW9guw1GL8VzhoD7IR4JJhuRlBBKoE\nVQxmlfpiH6tfotb2/OzsuHBrKN4c+Uo5sOKyJdKW5MLh/tjwXTyzoMs59Rh7J7ZB\nA5BSqVRMJiRKXRAc+daABU+mBtYuR4uNRIwc0iayHfBtp8G7s6/LncYN86HVrLzR\nIV20ClHMUQWOTOzOizXfB24o9mZ5mo0rvr2lFuOEZD+/6eoxhIXj0qmp7hAqeOZW\nZwVJ6eCPabOhFveU15BC6+mgp9wQ2Lzg7+iDAu/PyzH+7cbxRmHkNHwL/PHezUbc\ngDUdj7sBfGlkd2LJqcq7