755"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/bceb4ba9a49137e07089d8bae8fe00608d21f732/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T13:37:33Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T13:37:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: make MFA modules per-site activatable and scope the admin menu to them (#19)\n\nTwo related defects meant the \"MFA Community\" site-administration menu showed on\nevery site regardless of whether the modules were active there:\n\n1. jahia-module-type was \"system\" on extensions/totp/webauthn. A system module is\n   always-on platform-wide and is NOT site-assignable, so it could never be enabled\n   per site (and requireModuleInstalledOnSite could never resolve). Change all three\n   to \"module\"; their global services (GraphQL, the /cms/login gate, the factor SPI)\n   still register on bundle start - per-site enablement is an additional layer.\n\n2. The per-site admin routes had no site scoping. Add requireModuleInstalledOnSite\n   so each route appears only where its module is installed on the site: the per-factor\n   settings pages gate on their own factor module; the shared group / Extensions / Audit\n   entries gate on mfa-factors-extensions, which jcontent resolves against\n   installedModulesWithAllDependencies - present whenever any factor is enabled.\n\n   NOTE: jcontent expects requireModuleInstalledOnSite as a STRING (it does\n   installedModulesWithAllDependencies.indexOf(value)); an array never matches and\n   hides the menu everywhere, so the value is a plain string, not a list.\n\nTests: ui.admin.mfaCommunity now enables both factors on its test site so the\n(now site-scoped) menu is present. Cypress 59/59; verified on the local :9080\ninstance (menu shows on a site with the modules enabled, hidden on one without).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"2e795209815e96459284e8def60820ba73a29f03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/2e795209815e96459284e8def60820ba73a29f03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/bceb4ba9a49137e07089d8bae8fe00608d21f732","verification":{"payload":"tree 2e795209815e96459284e8def60820ba73a29f03\nparent 30f1c2748fa934c4d7850ec0d122c0716e1f520e\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1782567453 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782567453 +0200\n\nfix: make MFA modules per-site activatable and scope the admin menu to them (#19)\n\nTwo related defects meant the \"MFA Community\" site-administration menu showed on\nevery site regardless of whether the modules were active there:\n\n1. jahia-module-type was \"system\" on extensions/totp/webauthn. A system module is\n   always-on platform-wide and is NOT site-assignable, so it could never be enabled\n   per site (and requireModuleInstalledOnSite could never resolve). Change all three\n   to \"module\"; their global services (GraphQL, the /cms/login gate, the factor SPI)\n   still register on bundle start - per-site enablement is an additional layer.\n\n2. The per-site admin routes had no site scoping. Add requireModuleInstalledOnSite\n   so each route appears only where its module is installed on the site: the per-factor\n   settings pages gate on their own factor module; the shared group / Extensions / Audit\n   entries gate on mfa-factors-extensions, which jcontent resolves against\n   installedModulesWithAllDependencies - present whenever any factor is enabled.\n\n   NOTE: jcontent expects requireModuleInstalledOnSite as a STRING (it does\n   installedModulesWithAllDependencies.indexOf(value)); an array never matches and\n   hides the menu everywhere, so the value is a plain string, not a list.\n\nTests: ui.admin.mfaCommunity now enables both factors on its test site so the\n(now site-scoped) menu is present. Cypress 59/59; verified on the local :9080\ninstance (menu shows on a site with the modules enabled, hidden on one without).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqP9IdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACqoQACOK8sWZycFb4uiPvLapIztf\ndQzhgGvMI7rfOFzay89mkybchHTE37ZyqLXPsbNrrTgEVN/wIOC3AaTyUvdfcV9X\nrL7osuFsYzOLMxGrXWGqcsALQvxZTyE4ls4taqwSIVP4X9RBdsn4MHb3SpWiE/8L\ngHQjogNrsDmU5E5k0DVqBfRNVLM0P1VCUL9n22NiCOsuTTqYty8IKxd5eMYGDKZS\n53AGyUD7d5f79xKq5rG7SPfUeZPfysnudXJlxJDyrI/RPYwRcEPVAFGo0+zPPrdw\n+VdYiy1ekgiXzMdmAE88JHwSsyANJ5ovtC8BaF7rdgIYEVqi9KircX9/9siSzZ2S\n3Rhfb7FVHH9cmVsnXWdZp3XrnId0thF2qkIq+u3C9cqqjx07l1kq1ZJM+RdDvQkT\nP38xsVZ07qDJfZ7sCumy8c6/qDfWJFSfK46sLcZYRdFoFFc576ToUh1hT2nNd5LJ\nCKRbyIWNPWrkkezNzO8odSKnyAlFJXFebKrskCElSleMCWQk+uGd2d9lgbfXqV+a\nk0J7avDPRnW34KdR1vAVcfXOMlOGGjvywMD7chyFv47iDlixqwP2/MdP7y3e33u9\n0mtYape9EeyIr/DjtVa1KhQHKT4JzIsDy9hgjj2V3R+P0Z7BjzFp31zwe/4wgTbY\noJ2XD15SbeEDXG7kgEHZ\n=7zSy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-27T13:37:33Z"}},"