ity-parent/commit/02fb354b71099d1719799bbbd56c919b32b96ca1","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDAyZmIzNTRiNzEwOTlkMTcxOTc5OWJiYmQ1NmM5MTliMzJiOTZjYTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/4ae373ab83d647c12ec735ef0fa0fca24dca6d77","sha":"4ae373ab83d647c12ec735ef0fa0fca24dca6d77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/4ae373ab83d647c12ec735ef0fa0fca24dca6d77"}],"sha":"02fb354b71099d1719799bbbd56c919b32b96ca1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/02fb354b71099d1719799bbbd56c919b32b96ca1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/4ae373ab83d647c12ec735ef0fa0fca24dca6d77/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T09:34:25Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T09:34:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Blind-review hardening: architecture, security, a11y AAA, tests, docs (#1)\n\n* refactor: blind-review hardening across architecture, security, a11y, tests, docs\n\nMulti-dimensional blind review of the MFA community reactor with fixes applied\nby work-type:\n\n- Architecture/DRY: lift the duplicated per-factor logic into the shared\n  extensions bundle (MfaEnforcementDecider, MfaPreAuthGuard, MfaGraphqlAuth,\n  MfaAdminAccess, MfaManagementRateLimiterBase, MfaAuditLogBase,\n  MfaSiteSettingsStoreBase). SonarQube duplication 11.3% -> 1.3%, gate PASSED.\n- Java quality: S107 builders, catch GeneralSecurityException, Optional.orElseThrow,\n  TimeUnit.DAYS.toMillis, corrected/relocated javadoc, method references.\n- Security: defensive WebAuthn credential-owner post-condition; the client\n  open-redirect guard now mirrors the server (rejects /\\host, backslash, control\n  chars) instead of trusting URL() normalisation.\n- JS/TS: try/catch in every login service (no more unhandled rejections),\n  DOMPurify sanitisation of CMS-authored HTML, error handling on the dashboard\n  mutations, typed WebAuthn options (no any), removed console.log.\n- Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AAA): QR-code text alternative, button semantics for\n  the fatal-error restart, aria-describedby on the TOTP checkbox, AAA-compliant\n  disabled-button contrast, focus management on step transitions, meaningful logo alt.\n- Ergonomy: \"use a different method\" escape on verify/enroll, honest email\n  resend copy + aria-live confirmation, inline backup-code copy/download,\n  consistent per-factor terminology, friendly fallback for unmapped error codes.\n- Tests: new Java unit tests (anti-takeover ownership barrier, WebAuthn\n  clone-detection counter, pre-auth guard, AES secret cipher, rate limiter) and\n  a Vitest suite porting the open-redirect attack vectors to the client guard.\n- Docs: corrected GraphQL reference (secret field, full TOTP/WebAuthn\n  mutation+query surface), CND node-type inventory, authorization-grant wording.\n- Test harness: WebAuthn secure-context flag + run in Chrome, mail-service\n  activation for the email_code factor, login-redirect config isolation.\n\nVerification: SonarQube gate PASSED (0 issues), eslint + tsc clean,\n176 JUnit tests, Vitest 26 green, Cypress 59/59 (17/17 specs) green.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR-review findings (snapshot consistency, sign-count, GraphQL docs)\n\nAdversarial review of the PR diff surfaced regressions/issues introduced by the\nrefactor; all fixed and re-verified (build SUCCESS, SonarQube gate PASSED, Cypress 59/59):\n\n- Java HIGH: restore the single site-settings snapshot. The extraction had split the\n  one JCR load into two callbacks (isSiteEnabled + isInScope), a TOCTOU gap + double\n  read. Replaced with one isSiteApplicable(userId, siteKey) that loads once and checks\n  enabled + group scope against the same snapshot.\n- Java MED: WebAuthn sign-count is written only when it advances again (the refactor\n  had made the write unconditional, losing the clone-detection write signal).\n- Java MED: build the shared MfaEnforcementDecider once in @Activate instead of per\n  prepare() call (and not via a volatile field - Sonar S3077); enforcement unit tests\n  call activate() to mirror the DS lifecycle.\n- Java LOW: rate-limiter tests import the shared statics from MfaManagementRateLimiterBase.\n- Frontend HIGH: removed the dead .catch on enrollTotp() (it returns typed network\n  errors now, never rejects) handled in .then().\n- Frontend: kept client-side DOMPurify with the SSR window-guard and documented why -\n  sanitize-html / isomorphic-dompurify pull Node/jsdom deps that crash GraalVM SSR, and\n  emitting raw editor HTML on SSR would be an XSS window; SSR-empty + hydrate is the\n  security-first trade-off. Corrected the disabled-button contrast comment and the\n  server-only logoAlt typing note.\n- Docs HIGH: corrected the GraphQL reference - queries are flat root fields\n  (Query.mfaTotp / Query.mfaWebauthn), mutations nest under upa.mfaFactors (not\n  upa.mfa.factors), and result types use the Mfa-prefixed @GraphQLName values; AGENTS.md\n  query-graft wording fixed. Verified against the schema, the yml grants, and the specs.\n- Config LOW: sonar.cpd.exclusions scoped to totp/webauthn gql (extensions gql stays\n  under CPD); setupMail.groovy reads SMTP_SERVER_URL like the canonical script.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: outer-loop AAA accessibility + architecture polish\n\nFinal holistic blind review (security verified clean end-to-end) surfaced AAA\naccessibility gaps and two low architecture items; all fixed, re-verified\n(build SUCCESS, SonarQube gate PASSED, Cypress 59/59):\n\n- a11y (login-ui): i18n the TOTP/email verification input aria-labels (were raw\n  English); add aria-describedby linking each code input to its error region;\n  update the heading when the TOTP form switches to backup-code mode; give the\n  inline backup-codes block a region role + accessible name; add a visually\n  hidden h1 so the login page has a top-level heading.\n- a11y (admin React): replace the disabled-field opacity (which dropped help-text\n  contrast below AA) with explicit AAA-compliant colors across the totp/webauthn/\n  extensions site-settings panels; announce the backup-codes copy action via an\n  aria-live status region; add a caption + aria-labelledby to the audit table and\n  aria-hidden the decorative section icon.\n- architecture: make MfaEnforcementDecider.prepareForSite/prepareForGlobalOnly\n  private (only prepare() is the public entry point), tightening the exported SPI.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"a22cafdac8d8bfe0666e390f114cb0a19822e073","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/a22cafdac8d8bfe0666e390f114cb0a19822e073"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/4ae373ab83d647c12ec735ef0fa0fca24dca6d77","verification":{"payload":"tree a22cafdac8d8bfe0666e390f114cb0a19822e073\nparent ca1b4e7526a6e6a1050fc1579fe6c0d2e26b3f6d\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1782552865 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782552865 +0200\n\nBlind-review hardening: architecture, security, a11y AAA, tests, docs (#1)\n\n* refactor: blind-review hardening across architecture, security, a11y, tests, docs\n\nMulti-dimensional blind review of the MFA community reactor with fixes applied\nby work-type:\n\n- Architecture/DRY: lift the duplicated per-factor logic into the shared\n  extensions bundle (MfaEnforcementDecider, MfaPreAuthGuard, MfaGraphqlAuth,\n  MfaAdminAccess, MfaManagementRateLimiterBase, MfaAuditLogBase,\n  MfaSiteSettingsStoreBase). SonarQube duplication 11.3% -> 1.3%, gate PASSED.\n- Java quality: S107 builders, catch GeneralSecurityException, Optional.orElseThrow,\n  TimeUnit.DAYS.toMillis, corrected/relocated javadoc, method references.\n- Security: defensive WebAuthn credential-owner post-condition; the client\n  open-redirect guard now mirrors the server (rejects /\\host, backslash, control\n  chars) instead of trusting URL() normalisation.\n- JS/TS: try/catch in every login service (no more unhandled rejections),\n  DOMPurify sanitisation of CMS-authored HTML, error handling on the dashboard\n  mutations, typed WebAuthn options (no any), removed console.log.\n- Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AAA): QR-code text alternative, button semantics for\n  the fatal-error restart, aria-describedby on the TOTP checkbox, AAA-compliant\n  disabled-button contrast, focus management on step transitions, meaningful logo alt.\n- Ergonomy: \"use a different method\" escape on verify/enroll, honest email\n  resend copy + aria-live confirmation, inline backup-code copy/download,\n  consistent per-factor terminology, friendly fallback for unmapped error codes.\n- Tests: new Java unit tests (anti-takeover ownership barrier, WebAuthn\n  clone-detection counter, pre-auth guard, AES secret cipher, rate limiter) and\n  a Vitest suite porting the open-redirect attack vectors to the client guard.\n- Docs: corrected GraphQL reference (secret field, full TOTP/WebAuthn\n  mutation+query surface), CND node-type inventory, authorization-grant wording.\n- Test harness: WebAuthn secure-context flag + run in Chrome, mail-service\n  activation for the email_code factor, login-redirect config isolation.\n\nVerification: SonarQube gate PASSED (0 issues), eslint + tsc clean,\n176 JUnit tests, Vitest 26 green, Cypress 59/59 (17/17 specs) green.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR-review findings (snapshot consistency, sign-count, GraphQL docs)\n\nAdversarial review of the PR diff surfaced regressions/issues introduced by the\nrefactor; all fixed and re-verified (build SUCCESS, SonarQube gate PASSED, Cypress 59/59):\n\n- Java HIGH: restore the single site-settings snapshot. The extraction had split the\n  one JCR load into two callbacks (isSiteEnabled + isInScope), a TOCTOU gap + double\n  read. Replaced with one isSiteApplicable(userId, siteKey) that loads once and checks\n  enabled + group scope against the same snapshot.\n- Java MED: WebAuthn sign-count is written only when it advances again (the refactor\n  had made the write unconditional, losing the clone-detection write signal).\n- Java MED: build the shared MfaEnforcementDecider once in @Activate instead of per\n  prepare() call (and not via a volatile field - Sonar S3077); enforcement unit tests\n  call activate() to mirror the DS lifecycle.\n- Java LOW: rate-limiter tests import the shared statics from MfaManagementRateLimiterBase.\n- Frontend HIGH: removed the dead .catch on enrollTotp() (it returns typed network\n  errors now, never rejects) handled in .then().\n- Frontend: kept client-side DOMPurify with the SSR window-guard and documented why -\n  sanitize-html / isomorphic-dompurify pull Node/jsdom deps that crash GraalVM SSR, and\n  emitting raw editor HTML on SSR would be an XSS window; SSR-empty + hydrate is the\n  security-first trade-off. Corrected the disabled-button contrast comment and the\n  server-only logoAlt typing note.\n- Docs HIGH: corrected the GraphQL reference - queries are flat root fields\n  (Query.mfaTotp / Query.mfaWebauthn), mutations nest under upa.mfaFactors (not\n  upa.mfa.factors), and result types use the Mfa-prefixed @GraphQLName values; AGENTS.md\n  query-graft wording fixed. Verified against the schema, the yml grants, and the specs.\n- Config LOW: sonar.cpd.exclusions scoped to totp/webauthn gql (extensions gql stays\n  under CPD); setupMail.groovy reads SMTP_SERVER_URL like the canonical script.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: outer-loop AAA accessibility + architecture polish\n\nFinal holistic blind review (security verified clean end-to-end) surfaced AAA\naccessibility gaps and two low architecture items; all fixed, re-verified\n(build SUCCESS, SonarQube gate PASSED, Cypress 59/59):\n\n- a11y (login-ui): i18n the TOTP/email verification input aria-labels (were raw\n  English); add aria-describedby linking each code input to its error region;\n  update the heading when the TOTP form switches to backup-code mode; give the\n  inline backup-codes block a region role + accessible name; add a visually\n  hidden h1 so the login page has a top-level heading.\n- a11y (admin React): replace the disabled-field opacity (which dropped help-text\n  contrast below AA) with explicit AAA-compliant colors across the totp/webauthn/\n  extensions site-settings panels; announce the backup-codes copy action via an\n  aria-live status region; add a caption + aria-labelledby to the audit table and\n  aria-hidden the decorative section icon.\n- architecture: make MfaEnforcementDecider.prepareForSite/prepareForGlobalOnly\n  private (only prepare() is the public entry point), tightening the exported SPI.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n-