ptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/ca1b4e7526a6e6a1050fc1579fe6c0d2e26b3f6d","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKGNhMWI0ZTc1MjZhNmU2YTEwNTBmYzE1NzlmZTZjMGQyZTI2YjNmNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/655e72cca13b3446bc539ff969295b76a80a5dcf","sha":"655e72cca13b3446bc539ff969295b76a80a5dcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/655e72cca13b3446bc539ff969295b76a80a5dcf"}],"sha":"ca1b4e7526a6e6a1050fc1579fe6c0d2e26b3f6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/ca1b4e7526a6e6a1050fc1579fe6c0d2e26b3f6d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/655e72cca13b3446bc539ff969295b76a80a5dcf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T17:53:58Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T17:53:58Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"Bring every UI screen to WCAG 2.2 AAA\n\nAudit driven by computed contrast ratios, not estimates. Key failures fixed:\n\n- Action color #00a0e3 was 2.94:1 with white (below even AA) on every login\n  button and toggle link: replaced by #00538b (8.05:1, the existing focus-ring\n  color). Admin inline #c00 (5.89:1) and #080 (4.64:1) standardized to the\n  AAA pair #a00000 (8.42:1) / #006600 (7.24:1).\n- The login island renders inside arbitrary site templates — some paint\n  near-black page backgrounds and force white headings, wrecking every text\n  pair. The flow now owns a self-contained white card (background, #131c21\n  base text, heading/link overrides), making the ratios host-independent.\n- Input borders #ccc (1.6:1) -> #767676 (4.54:1, non-text boundary 1.4.11);\n  explicit ::placeholder at #555 (7.46:1) instead of the UA default.\n- Status messages (4.1.3): role=alert on the dashboard/dialog/reset errors\n  and the unsupported-browser notice; role=status aria-live=polite on reset\n  successes; the destructive-reset confirmation announces as an alert.\n- Accessible names: code inputs in CodePromptDialog/EnrollDialog and the\n  reset-user inputs gain aria-label; totp SiteSettings gains the\n  aria-describedby help wiring the sibling screens already had.\n- Pointer targets (2.5.5): 44px minimum on login buttons, toggle links and\n  inputs, admin text inputs, and the credential-table row actions (size=big).\n- Section headings (2.4.10): LoginForm and FatalErrorScreen open with an h2\n  like every other step; fixed-height error container now reflows.\n- README documents the conformance posture, the verified palette and the\n  essential-timing exception (2.2.3) covering OTP windows and lockouts.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"a81ef1e09f1fe4ac6ffd72072760bbd9e9f903dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/a81ef1e09f1fe4ac6ffd72072760bbd9e9f903dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/655e72cca13b3446bc539ff969295b76a80a5dcf","verification":{"payload":"tree a81ef1e09f1fe4ac6ffd72072760bbd9e9f903dc\nparent f526aa6e7c1a583edc64347c72e93f2e2dc9a40a\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780854838 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780854838 +0200\n\nBring every UI screen to WCAG 2.2 AAA\n\nAudit driven by computed contrast ratios, not estimates. Key failures fixed:\n\n- Action color #00a0e3 was 2.94:1 with white (below even AA) on every login\n  button and toggle link: replaced by #00538b (8.05:1, the existing focus-ring\n  color). Admin inline #c00 (5.89:1) and #080 (4.64:1) standardized to the\n  AAA pair #a00000 (8.42:1) / #006600 (7.24:1).\n- The login island renders inside arbitrary site templates — some paint\n  near-black page backgrounds and force white headings, wrecking every text\n  pair. The flow now owns a self-contained white card (background, #131c21\n  base text, heading/link overrides), making the ratios host-independent.\n- Input borders #ccc (1.6:1) -> #767676 (4.54:1, non-text boundary 1.4.11);\n  explicit ::placeholder at #555 (7.46:1) instead of the UA default.\n- Status messages (4.1.3): role=alert on the dashboard/dialog/reset errors\n  and the unsupported-browser notice; role=status aria-live=polite on reset\n  successes; the destructive-reset confirmation announces as an alert.\n- Accessible names: code inputs in CodePromptDialog/EnrollDialog and the\n  reset-user inputs gain aria-label; totp SiteSettings gains the\n  aria-describedby help wiring the sibling screens already had.\n- Pointer targets (2.5.5): 44px minimum on login buttons, toggle links and\n  inputs, admin text inputs, and the credential-table row actions (size=big).\n- Section headings (2.4.10): LoginForm and FatalErrorScreen open with an h2\n  like every other step; fixed-height error container now reflows.\n- README documents the conformance posture, the verified palette and the\n  essential-timing exception (2.2.3) covering OTP windows and lockouts.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmolsDYACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kCkQf/UlNBYGfk3CkZuihUA3NhyC4v2sAPpQXcce3+YLfkf4Hk2tzN+jq8cvv0\nClAHZyrQI1HEo0CRDy1SQAyn+uhNpSf4avJUUnxgvsy0GGzw80Be2fjGnWLpF0yp\nT5Gopr9sOXc6PNm+Fe3TGz4mae+8UUXkooSbeqTyp7mj1G4sUxArs6LWDTP4lN8Z\nG68egmegCuMWHchm4y/DrflFRe02e5/0rshdWIw5HCNpaNw/nGv31QlGl+BE61e5\nsTIt50jtAJ21B4cTmhgq9UZpVHeoUsijriJZSiAxkf111jJRFH6pmy/ycNyngEqh\nIXdRvCxzcRg0PvlZozQZVa/kUIvAzw==\n=bUSL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/655e72cca13b3446bc539ff969295b76a80a5dcf","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDY1NWU3MmNjYTEzYjM0NDZiYzUzOWZmOTY5Mjk1Yjc2YTgwYTVkY2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/f526aa6e7c1a583edc64347c72e93f2e2dc9a40a","sha":"f526aa6e7c1a583edc64347c72e93f2e2dc9a40a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/f526aa6e7c1a583edc64347c72e93f2e2dc9a40a"}],"sha":"655e72cca13b3446bc539ff969295b76a80a5dcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/655e72cca13b3446bc539ff969295b76a80a5dcf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/f526aa6e7c1a583edc64347c72e93f2e2dc9a40a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T17:32:58Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T17:32:58Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"Offer UPA''s built-in email_code factor as a pick-one sign-in alternative\n\nUPA ships an email one-time-code factor, but it could not coexist with the\ncommunity factors: UPA requires EVERY factor in mfaEnabledFactors to verify,\nits email provider never skips itself (it does not speak the pick-one skip\nprotocol), and shadowing it in the FactorRegistry would be a bind-order\nlottery (HashMap put/remove(key, value) semantics) on an authentication path.\n\n- EmailCodeFactorAdapter (MfaSiteProvider): chooser/directory visibility for\n  users with a j:email, enforcement option in the admin UI, sibling-skip row\n  participation; flagged NOT inline-enrollable and FOREIGN.\n- MfaForeignFactorDrain: wraps the totp/webauthn verify mutations — after a\n  genuine verification of an enforced factor it marks remaining enforced\n  FOREIGN factors verified (with a SkippablePreparation marker, preserving\n  the circular-drain protection) and completes authentication exactly like\n  UPA''s MfaServiceImpl. Choosing TOTP/WebAuthn therefore sends no email.\n- MfaSiteProvider gains isInlineEnrollable()/isForeignFactor() defaults;\n  inline-enrollment offers now exclude non-enrollable factors.\n- SkippablePreparation.isSkipDrained() centralizes the skip-drain test.\n- e2e: ui.emailFactor.cy.ts (chooser offers both, emailed code signs in via\n  Mailpit, TOTP path sends no email) + setUpaEnabledFactors helper writing a\n  REAL String[] through ConfigurationAdmin — first coverage of a multi-factor\n  UPA shape.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"f13b270a23e5ad521055d30755dcdadc83e0fbd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/f13b270a23e5ad521055d30755dcdadc83e0fbd3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/f526aa6e7c1a583edc64347c72e93f2e2dc9a40a","verification":{"payload":"tree f13b270a23e5ad521055d30755dcdadc83e0fbd3\nparent 432b0ea314881998021a12ba8e88d5cdba3da742\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780853578 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780853578 +0200\n\nOffer UPA''s built-in email_code factor as a pick-one sign-in alternative\n\nUPA ships an email one-time-code factor, but it could not coexist with the\ncommunity factors: UPA requires EVERY factor in mfaEnabledFactors to verify,\nits email provider never skips itself (it does not speak the pick-one skip\nprotocol), and shadowing it in the FactorRegistry would be a bind-order\nlottery (HashMap put/remove(key, value) semantics) on an authentication path.\n\n- EmailCodeFactorAdapter (MfaSiteProvider): chooser/directory visibility for\n  users with a j:email, enforcement option in the admin UI, sibling-skip row\n  participation; flagged NOT inline-enrollable and FOREIGN.\n- MfaForeignFactorDrain: wraps the totp/webauthn verify mutations — after a\n  genuine verification of an enforced factor it marks remaining enforced\n  FOREIGN factors verified (with a SkippablePreparation marker, preserving\n  the circular-drain protection) and completes authentication exactly like\n  UPA''s MfaServiceImpl. Choosing TOTP/WebAuthn therefore sends no email.\n- MfaSiteProvider gains isInlineEnrollable()/isForeignFactor() defaults;\n  inline-enrollment offers now exclude non-enrollable factors.\n- SkippablePreparation.isSkipDrained() centralizes the skip-drain test.\n- e2e: ui.emailFactor.cy.ts (chooser offers both, emailed code signs in via\n  Mailpit, TOTP path sends no email) + setUpaEnabledFactors helper writing a\n  REAL String[] through ConfigurationAdmin — first coverage of a multi-factor\n  UPA shape.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmolq0oACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3n+rggA02cBHGPUovPlKytqaTlTiYwvQYBLZICeJwjXGL15wtQ4Q76DmnatwDvD\nt3oz+13mRIlsymoNw59m8keoYZBfP+p6PEKj2LP3Z1GBuC0lMsqZ/iboc0LxxSar\nWA1I7XRy6fuDLtZEWCLOdZmfgiJku882yRH5si/5lajTbxey+QOIQOaMO5Z6jNuj\ne0KgAtWrQReiyQIUYgmItdkEA8P4KRaDubIjiGUvmF4NDZ/AFthYFPGgRGnAkqUI\nZkcEBzFFXXYw1qckZBbXElqbbq0yIXf2Ty5z8+RpmoiCgLSTfmSiLN1V0RORvbpe\nrNsqq5K/chomTuRxkXfQpozmPByTEA==\n=Eg7z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/f526aa6e7c1a583edc64347c72e93f2e2dc9a40a","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKGY1MjZhYTZlN2MxYTU4M2VkYzY0MzQ3YzcyZTkzZjJlMmRjOWE0MGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/432b0ea314881998021a12ba8e88d5cdba3da742","sha":"432b0ea314881998021a12ba8e88d5cdba3da742","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/432b0ea314881998021a12ba8e88d5cdba3da742"}],"sha":"f526aa6e7c1a583edc64347c72e93f2e2dc9a40a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/f526aa6e7c1a583edc64347c72e93f2e2dc9a40a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/432b0ea314881998021a12ba8e88d5cdba3da742/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T16:11:04Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T16:11:04Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"Identify each factor''s section on the Audit & reporting page\n\nBoth sections rendered the same generic ''Audit & reporting'' heading (and an\nidentical data-testid), so an administrator could not tell which table\nbelonged to which factor. Each section now opens with its factor''s name and\nicon — ''Two-factor authentication (TOTP)'' with the Password glyph,\n''Security keys & passkeys (WebAuthn)'' with the Key glyph, matching the\nadministration menu — and carries a data-factor marker attribute.\n\nThe shared data-testid stays (the page contract ''two sections compose'' is\nasserted on it); the admin UI spec additionally asserts each section is\nidentified by its factor.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"a688d71d8fac2effcbc6ac40338a6286395ee016","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/a688d71d8fac2effcbc6ac40338a6286395ee016"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/432b0ea314881998021a12ba8e88d5cdba3da742","verification":{"payload":"tree a688d71d8fac2effcbc6ac40338a6286395ee016\nparent 5374f52292250a3600703afa56d0ed5018499d25\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780848664 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780848664 +0200\n\nIdentify each factor''s section on the Audit & reporting page\n\nBoth sections rendered the same generic ''Audit & reporting'' heading (and an\nidentical data-testid), so an administrator could not tell which table\nbelonged to which factor. Each section now opens with its factor''s name and\nicon — ''Two-factor authentication (TOTP)'' with the Password glyph,\n''Security keys & passkeys (WebAuthn)'' with the Key glyph, matching the\nadministration menu — and carries a data-factor marker attribute.\n\nThe shared data-testid stays (the page contract ''two sections compose'' is\nasserted on it); the admin UI spec additionally asserts each section is\nidentified by its factor.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmolmBgACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mLTQf/aFdMJfpnieoskkm5MJ5vxiV/TDy0Ny1pImeFEbYy6vKKr+NKLCYLWApt\nI0XKoVCihV/jHC08VMSOzcbtJnUyVRMmGXILrSHRO0h8Zja2Q+OQJG+mMTZfKuRs\nA79vq+FniHMrufoCsmyZJjX5iEkvcUtX3x3sFBhIaWzb6lBH0fGJioaE2Kte12D/\nZ3yon/+LpEJqhUtPNMoK467kKfY9fz/u0qHt5B2W7N9m4NmfabFz3Iqui8x5cNFX\nPVJprll+8fHPam837f/h5m/+ec2fF1Pi6TWtdobKIS3y8Mn97FDK3KM+uno0EKOC\nAE2GN/dpfGepKBCeIWdKekQ8Zt3Dsg==\n=Tghk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","n