ype":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/5374f52292250a3600703afa56d0ed5018499d25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T16:11:04Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T16:11:04Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"Give each MFA administration menu entry its own icon\n\nEvery entry rendered the same Security shield. The MFA Community groups\n(site administration and dashboard) keep the shield as the family brand;\neach child now carries a glyph matching its purpose:\n\n - Two-factor authentication (TOTP)  -> Password (one-time codes)\n - Security keys and passkeys        -> Key\n - Extensions (login/logout routing) -> GlobalLink\n - Audit & reporting                 -> Report\n - Server administration global page -> Setting\n\nThe same icon follows each factor across surfaces (site administration and\nuser dashboard).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e9914d4588361ca6fd3f8d89d434671172f4ce5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/3e9914d4588361ca6fd3f8d89d434671172f4ce5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/5374f52292250a3600703afa56d0ed5018499d25","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e9914d4588361ca6fd3f8d89d434671172f4ce5\nparent 807efd44b2fb01349b8843d876bff7040b85aab4\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780848664 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780848664 +0200\n\nGive each MFA administration menu entry its own icon\n\nEvery entry rendered the same Security shield. The MFA Community groups\n(site administration and dashboard) keep the shield as the family brand;\neach child now carries a glyph matching its purpose:\n\n - Two-factor authentication (TOTP)  -> Password (one-time codes)\n - Security keys and passkeys        -> Key\n - Extensions (login/logout routing) -> GlobalLink\n - Audit & reporting                 -> Report\n - Server administration global page -> Setting\n\nThe same icon follows each factor across surfaces (site administration and\nuser dashboard).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmolmBgACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mpbggAmB/h33QmUp2CRig6ZqZErk0Yrl55FN4/oY820PAiUEDTY/P5fM6eOEbR\ndxVOyZXpgYpWXY3Jip1EWzX59SE/Ly4qdyajFEAyb971rKCFYbvFuQF+MUBZoUyV\nFvVxPSyIuiIY8ABPjf1rhwGvLnPYVAHNxMPtcs48GncrqjB/k2ENNM86IZISlrm3\nOExTOEdGtiAIOVJPSjIdXpG/mc9d/NDbhS8RsPCQzQ7OdPNtfOx5BUhBPeV97FIW\nHA5ou+g6u817QAwcs2N/irQ0xQ4DiVz1IwPwC9tJB9OI+mOhrUrLl+k5Dm2TUCrr\nQeSV2PggdeLXKEK+eoDfrg8zf5yPmg==\n=fcNf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/5374f52292250a3600703afa56d0ed5018499d25","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDUzNzRmNTIyOTIyNTBhMzYwMDcwM2FmYTU2ZDBlZDUwMTg0OTlkMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/807efd44b2fb01349b8843d876bff7040b85aab4","sha":"807efd44b2fb01349b8843d876bff7040b85aab4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/807efd44b2fb01349b8843d876bff7040b85aab4"}],"sha":"5374f52292250a3600703afa56d0ed5018499d25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/5374f52292250a3600703afa56d0ed5018499d25"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/807efd44b2fb01349b8843d876bff7040b85aab4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T14:22:51Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T14:22:51Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"Group the dashboard MFA pages under a shared ''MFA Community'' menu item\n\nThe user dashboard listed ''Two-factor authentication (TOTP)'' and ''Security\nkeys and passkeys (WebAuthn)'' as two flat top-level entries. They now sit\nunder one non-selectable ''MFA Community'' group, mirroring the structure\nalready used in site administration.\n\nSame defensive-registration pattern as the site-admin group: each factor\nbundle registers the parent only if absent (either may be installed alone,\nwhichever activates first wins), children attach through the\n''dashboard-mfa-community-dashboard'' target resolved by ui-extender''s\nadminRoute tree (children of key K under base target T live at T-K). The\nroute keys are unchanged, so deep links (/jahia/dashboard/mfa-factors-totp,\n.../mfa-factors-webauthn) keep working — covered by the existing dashboard\nspec (3/3 after the change).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"fffb5768019b0a36c402e124849d6d34dd52e7fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/fffb5768019b0a36c402e124849d6d34dd52e7fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/807efd44b2fb01349b8843d876bff7040b85aab4","verification":{"payload":"tree fffb5768019b0a36c402e124849d6d34dd52e7fb\nparent ebff23ea804025716c58b1ca131c13082bc7c2bd\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780842171 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780842171 +0200\n\nGroup the dashboard MFA pages under a shared ''MFA Community'' menu item\n\nThe user dashboard listed ''Two-factor authentication (TOTP)'' and ''Security\nkeys and passkeys (WebAuthn)'' as two flat top-level entries. They now sit\nunder one non-selectable ''MFA Community'' group, mirroring the structure\nalready used in site administration.\n\nSame defensive-registration pattern as the site-admin group: each factor\nbundle registers the parent only if absent (either may be installed alone,\nwhichever activates first wins), children attach through the\n''dashboard-mfa-community-dashboard'' target resolved by ui-extender''s\nadminRoute tree (children of key K under base target T live at T-K). The\nroute keys are unchanged, so deep links (/jahia/dashboard/mfa-factors-totp,\n.../mfa-factors-webauthn) keep working — covered by the existing dashboard\nspec (3/3 after the change).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmolfrsACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lGzQf+Lk6csISib+wMBzZRaQHBUIe9FbVr2m26taalnbe0Lak7rm6yrOK04ohZ\n1GA08fPAvs444SMff2sKV0ff6cPW1KFBgDwJNWhDTmYobIvM/pEqM/YRjVD+Y6Wu\nviQ3sylL2aLBpx84Mey9Kx2Ay0KVKxMnoT6NTJj1RFTJkJj6+y6aaK/cvCZm98IH\n88djNxh/hC/YxJCFdawm2QFJDoxjzr0s8TsUYG0IXymVLV4qUDlyoqqwAw6EYFtd\n9IXIcYiAeESrbtfheBqNBDDOBK3u0yVhygzOM8zqRVf5nIWT1EvipbkbdOj3PP1F\nwnmK7CQSOiDgVqwLVepKZk5fYekalw==\n=KhzW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/807efd44b2fb01349b8843d876bff7040b85aab4","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDgwN2VmZDQ0YjJmYjAxMzQ5Yjg4NDNkODc2YmZmNzA0MGI4NWFhYjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/ebff23ea804025716c58b1ca131c13082bc7c2bd","sha":"ebff23ea804025716c58b1ca131c13082bc7c2bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/ebff23ea804025716c58b1ca131c13082bc7c2bd"}],"sha":"807efd44b2fb01349b8843d876bff7040b85aab4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/807efd44b2fb01349b8843d876bff7040b85aab4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/ebff23ea804025716c58b1ca131c13082bc7c2bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T14:18:32Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T14:18:32Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"Gate /cms/login automatically while MFA enforcement is active\n\nThe /cms/login endpoint authenticates with the password alone — with factors\nenforced it is a complete second-factor bypass, and so far closing it\nrequired opting into the hard 403 gate (loginGate.enabled). The filter now\nalso acts WITHOUT that opt-in whenever enforcement is active: /cms/login\nstays reachable only when the operator explicitly configured it as the login\nURL (global or per-site).\n\n - custom MFA login page configured -> 302 there, carrying the redirect=\n   return-to-target (MfaLoginLogoutProvider resolves per-site vs global and\n   appends the param);\n - /cms/login configured as the login URL -> allowed (deliberate choice of\n   the default screen);\n - no login URL configured -> 403 with configuration guidance in the log\n   (silently serving the password-only screen would void the second factor).\n\nThe explicit hard gate keeps its unchanged always-403 contract, and the IP\nwhitelist (loginGate.ipWhitelist) is honoured by both modes as the\nbreak-glass door. The provider is additionally registered under its own\nclass so the filter can resolve the configured URL per request.\n\n6 new filter unit tests (23 total); http.loginGate e2e grows from 5 to 8\ntests covering the three automatic-mode outcomes. Full suite 56/56.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"38ec6df3df617555c867638c8ded46143b8f51ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/38ec6df3df617555c867638c8ded46143b8f51ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/ebff23ea804025716c58b1ca131c13082bc7c2bd","verification":{"payload":"tree 38ec6df3df617555c867638c8ded46143b8f51ed\nparent a3a83541a6ea2388a1fafb27fed20f2cbd7a81e9\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780841912 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780841912 +0200\n\nGate /cms/login automatically while MFA enforcement is active\n\nThe /cms/login endpoint authenticates with the password alone — with factors\nenforced it is a complete second-factor bypass, and so far closing it\nrequired opting into the hard 403 gate (loginGate.enabled). The filter now\nalso acts WITHOUT that opt-in whenever enforcement is active: /cms/login\nstays reachable only when the operator explicitly configured it as the login\nURL (global or per-site).\n\n - custom MFA login page configured -> 302 there, carrying the redirect=\n   return-to-target (MfaLoginLogoutProvider resolves per-site vs global and\n   appends the param);\n - /cms/login configured as the login URL -> allowed (deliberate choice of\n   the default screen);\n - no login URL configured -> 403 with configuration guidance in the log\n   (silently serving the password-only screen would void the second factor).\n\nThe explicit hard gate keeps its unchanged always-403 contract, and the IP\nwhitelist (loginGate.ipWhitelist) is honoured by both modes as the\nbreak-glass door. The provider is additionally registered under its own\nclass so the filter can resolve the configured URL per request.\n\n6 new filter unit tests (23 total); http.loginGate e2e grows from 5 to 8\ntests covering the three automatic-mode outcomes. Full suite 56/56.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmolfbgACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lyzAf/SCB3qE0czGh7sNgWX6jsol6+I7mPWcQDHzM+9Vosylsx5XSbBBJ/3mGo\nPDuZw6JntyJlR9I++6/swV+H3hI2DQaCzig2JiU6qYObtoczavhU0qCsQLWWNBiP\nrXoVowb28dW5bYFO/REN+No4VAqqWUp7nRSzDadYpJYyZ/iO+vZWmPBWGBg25QuF\nugxKeYEft/jIE9lf7be7o1sqgxB1ZshGTGZaPSaGEhFbSiz4BiQhVn9+i5RdzPcW\nnGPVS4KXFWwCfi7IhyJwDNU4CTGT7yRPkwApBmqpLjcmzQz09k4S6ZQ5Yo29WrlT\neO0u3XDmwSuSGXvBRwRlshp+GJcGUQ==\n=pOcx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/ebff23ea804025716c58b1ca131c13082bc7c2bd","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKGViZmYyM2VhODA0MDI1NzE2YzU4YjFjYTEzMWMxMzA4MmJjN2MyYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/a3a83541a6ea2388a1fafb27fed20f2cbd7a81e9","sha":"a3a83541a6ea2388a1fafb27fed20f2cbd7a81e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/a3a83541a6ea2388a1fafb27fed20f2cbd7a81e9"}],"sha":"ebff23ea804025716c58b1ca131c13082bc7c2bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/ebff23ea804025716c58b1ca131c13082bc7c2bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/a3a83541a6ea2388a1fafb27fed20f2cbd7a81e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T07:07:08Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T07:07:08Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"Carry the requested page through the login/logout URLs as redirect=\n\nThe custom login/logout URLs served by MfaLoginLogoutProvider dropped the\npage the user was after: a 401 on a protected URL landed on the login page,\nand a successful sign-in then dumped the user at the site root.\n\nThe provider now appends redirect=<original target> to the URL it serves.\nThe target is resolved in priority order: an explicit (validated) redirect\nparameter already on the request — Jahia core passes one on /cms/login and\n/cms/logout links and it must survive the hop to the custom page — then the\nservlet ERROR/FORWARD dispatch attributes (Jahia''s 401 handling forwards to\n/error before consulting the providers, so the request''s own URI is the\nerror servlet''s), then the request URI itself. The login UI already consumed\na redirect= param after authentication (services/redirect.tsx, same-origin\nvalidated); now the server actually sends one.\n\nBoth sides validate independently against open redirects through the shared\nMfaUrls chokepoint: a hostile redirect parameter is dropped server-side even\nthough the client would also reject it. Auth endpoints and the error servlet\nare never used as targets, a self-loop (target = the login page itself) is\nskipped, and an operator-hardcoded redirect= in the configured URL is left\nuntouched.\n\n10 new provider unit tests; new e2e spec covers the 401 round trip (302\nLocation carries redirect=) and the post-sign-in landing on the target.\nFull suite 16 specs / 53 tests green, Sonar 0 open issues.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"3426bcb04dacba0c34740ec595ed41a453793fb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/3426bcb04dacba0c34740ec595ed41a453793fb7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/a3a83541a6ea2388a1fafb27fed20f2cbd7a81e9","verification":{"payload":"tree 3426bcb04dacba0c34740ec595ed41a453793fb7\nparent 39a000a8bb487b3c5e6556040cd16c029ab7ed64\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780816028 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780816028 +0200\n\nCarry the requested page through the login/logout URLs as redirect=\n\nThe custom login/logout URLs served by MfaLoginLogoutProvider dropped the\npage the user was after: a 401 on a protected URL landed on the login page,\nand a successful sign-in then dumped the user at the site root.\n\nThe provider now appends redirect=<original target> to the URL it serves.\nThe target is resolved in priority order: an explicit (validated) redirect\nparameter already on the request — Jahia core passes one on /cms/login and\n/cms/logout links and it must survive the hop to the custom page — then the\nservlet ERROR/FORWARD dispatch attributes (Jahia''s 401 handling forwards to\n/error before consulting the providers, so the request''s own URI is the\nerror servlet''s), then the request URI itself. The login UI already consumed\na redirect= param after authentication (services/redirect.tsx, same-origin\nvalidated); now the server actually sends one.\n\nBoth sides validate independently against open redirects through the shared\nMfaUrls chokepoint: a hostile redirect parameter is dropped server-side even\nthough the client would also reject it. Auth endpoints and the error servlet\nare never used as targets, a self-loop (target = the login page itself) is\nskipped, and an operator-hardcoded redirect= in the configured URL is left\nuntouched.\n\n10 new provider unit tests; new e2e spec covers the 401 round trip (302\nLocation carries redirect=) and the post-sign-in landing on the target.\nFull suite 16 specs / 53 tests green, Sonar 0 open issues.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmolGJwACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nGmwf+KreGdkD50hX2owX/BjMF7wna8Nn1sjJ6b7usFXMxUPpXyBF4RVHRqqMV\nva8JgnAMfecsf+hp+Vd65j+nVadFeWcjqGjW0JylqXi2+IJewKEJjSmumWu4q920\nUKlbLTdze4aRqZo3S8QdMSdMzeBdDXr4W9lgHTy5mBsrnsiS1+Tq6w8Wzel5yazf\nRaEm2nSAZ7XAjwe7wFrFrMtqVr7GS7Cb12FHDnjwgltFP1elBi1o/HxaX22+lwbS\niqoA/gG5QQxnSKZq4o04ACV2DFih3mahu9ZzffCauD40yyhM3tW3LhDYjxV/kOc0\nfZtOHjOtlQKt54TquQMwF43zZDi4YA==\n=xuY0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/a3a83541a6ea2388a1fafb27fed20f2cbd7a81e9","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKGEzYTgzNTQxYTZlYTIzODhhMWZhZmIyN2ZlZDIwZjJjYmQ3YTgxZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/39a000a8bb487b3c5e6556040cd16c029ab7ed64","sha":"39a000a8bb487b3c5e6556040cd16c029ab7ed64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/39a000a8bb487b3c5e6556040cd16c029ab7ed64"}],"sha":"a3a83541a6ea2388a1fafb27fed20f2cbd7a81e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/a3a83541a6ea2388a1fafb27fed20f2cbd7a81e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/39a000a8bb487b3c5e6556040cd16c029ab7ed64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T20:27:26Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T20:27:26Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"Offer only the user''s configured factors in the sign-in factor chooser\n\nWith several factors in UPA''s mfaEnabledFactors, the post-password chooser was\nbuilt from that platform-wide list: it offered factors the user never set up,\nand picking one was a dead end — its pick-one row defers to the configured\nsibling, so the user who clicked TOTP landed on the security key screen.\n\nThe login UI now asks the server which factors the session''s user actually\nconfigured and filters the chooser to those: one configured factor goes\nstraight to its verification screen (no chooser), none falls through to\ninline enrollment as before, and the chooser only appears when there is a\nreal choice.\n\nThe new top-level mfaSessionFactors GraphQL query (extensions module, opened\nto the anonymous login UI by the shipped authorization yml) derives the\nsubject exclusively from the in-flight server-side MfaSession — no user\nargument, so a caller can only learn about the account whose password it\nalready proved. On any query failure the client falls back to the unfiltered\nlist: the chooser is cosmetic, verification stays enforced server-side.\n\nMfaFactorDirectory.configuredFactorsForUser also honors per-site activation\n(a factor disabled on the site would skip at prepare and recreate the same\ndead end). Covered by 5 new directory unit tests; full e2e suite 51/51.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"32b3f4c04a7e2df3e62664887837209ea2685577","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/32b3f4c04a7e2df3e62664887837209ea2685577"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/39a000a8bb487b3c5e6556040cd16c029ab7ed64","verification":{"payload":"tree 32b3f4c04a7e2df3e62664887837209ea2685577\nparent 02f8d8663edcce1d716508f989934e47c0a8a15f\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780777646 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780777646 +0200\n\nOffer only the user''s configured factors in the sign-in factor chooser\n\nWith several factors in UPA''s mfaEnabledFactors, the post-password chooser was\nbuilt from that platform-wide list: it offered factors the user never set up,\nand picking one was a dead end — its pick-one row defers to the configured\nsibling, so the user who clicked TOTP landed on the security key screen.\n\nThe login UI now asks the server which factors the session''s user actually\nconfigured and filters the chooser to those: one configured factor goes\nstraight to its verification screen (no chooser), none falls through to\ninline enrollment as before, and the chooser only appears when there is a\nreal choice.\n\nThe new top-level mfaSessionFactors GraphQL query (extensions module, opened\nto the anonymous login UI by the shipped authorization yml) derives the\nsubject exclusively from the in-flight server-side MfaSession — no user\nargument, so a caller can only learn about the account whose password it\nalready proved. On any query failure the client falls back to the unfiltered\nlist: the chooser is cosmetic, verification stays enforced server-side.\n\nMfaFactorDirectory.configuredFactorsForUser also honors per-site activation\n(a factor disabled on the site would skip at prepare and recreate the same\ndead end). Covered by 5 new directory unit tests; full e2e suite 51/51.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmokgq4ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kKqwgAzdTCR/6D2+CjCBcW0euPdea+Uqg0gRrYG/UfOw74jA5NIwMFhG+QHr/9\n2Dr/VUjW75V0+WGeiYurddfh/2LIVRs3MdgOX2XD2rlJ6+bwK4IoJ9qLdr1PA1M+\nFsZQIL7/liloG97LqQsdwNsZOXIy79GKaaWxGmOGKUMnQc9TknqZhjLeXyNPa5pR\nUD7BWsot5BJc7jZkr2bu21EivM3B+lXLOZJYXv/VgjSNSIPNl/hI3GbKMEM6Vnzr\n5In4QWls3ovBMgGVX4qxFMghgOv4SBeQM30b5L+E75DrpLO5MykB81UdgrenbRB6\nAz3wWh2KuoPU8pDepPdJVaRNmR23Dg==\n=94sq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/39a000a8bb487b3c5e6556040cd16c029ab7ed64","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDM5YTAwMGE4YmI0ODdiM2M1ZTY1NTYwNDBjZDE2YzAyOWFiN2VkNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/02f8d8663edcce1d716508f989934e47c0a8a15f","sha":"02f8d8663edcce1d716508f989934e47c0a8a15f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/02f8d8663edcce1d716508f989934e47c0a8a15f"}],"sha":"39a000a8bb487b3c5e6556040cd16c029ab7ed64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/39a000a8bb487b3c5e6556040cd16c029ab7ed64"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/02f8d8663edcce1d716508f989934e47c0a8a15f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T20:09:31Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T20:09:31Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"Fix circular pick-one skip completing sign-in with no challenge at all\n\nWith both factors in UPA''s mfaEnabledFactors, a user owning only ONE of them\ncould sign in with zero second-factor challenges: the unconfigured factor\nskipped via ''sibling factor is configured'' and was drained as verified by the\nclient, then the configured factor skipped via ''another enforced factor is\nalready verified'' — the two pick-one rows excused each other circularly, the\nsecond one trusting a verified flag that only recorded the drain of the first.\n\nA skip-drained factor was never actually challenged, so it must not satisfy\npick-one. The new SkippablePreparation interface (extensions) is the shared\nvocabulary: both preparation results implement it, and both providers''\nanotherEnforcedFactorVerified now requires the sibling''s preparation NOT to be\na skip marker. Users with a configured factor are challenged with it again;\nusers with none still reach inline enrollment.\n\nCovered by three new provider unit tests, including the reported scenario\n(passkey registered, no TOTP, user picks the TOTP step first).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"4ecf382e139eb71ff817232211feea80b2a12abc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/4ecf382e139eb71ff817232211feea80b2a12abc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/02f8d8663edcce1d716508f989934e47c0a8a15f","verification":{"payload":"tree 4ecf382e139eb71ff817232211feea80b2a12abc\nparent ce0e41349d367e4fb12082b2cf6790788d18aa91\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780776571 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780776571 +0200\n\nFix circular pick-one skip completing sign-in with no challenge at all\n\nWith both factors in UPA''s mfaEnabledFactors, a user owning only ONE of them\ncould sign in with zero second-factor challenges: the unconfigured factor\nskipped via ''sibling factor is configured'' and was drained as verified by the\nclient, then the configured factor skipped via ''another enforced factor is\nalready verified'' — the two pick-one rows excused each other circularly, the\nsecond one trusting a verified flag that only recorded the drain of the first.\n\nA skip-drained factor was never actually challenged, so it must not satisfy\npick-one. The new SkippablePreparation interface (extensions) is the shared\nvocabulary: both preparation results implement it, and both providers''\nanotherEnforcedFactorVerified now requires the sibling''s preparation NOT to be\na skip marker. Users with a configured factor are challenged with it again;\nusers with none still reach inline enrollment.\n\nCovered by three new provider unit tests, including the reported scenario\n(passkey registered, no TOTP, user picks the TOTP step first).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmokfnsACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3ngewf5Aaj6hBi6djXHb9EORw/jGa4hDu+k5WW5cbRXxFpXGw+z4V91Socpri6D\nJAgdmEWLtwuBIVb1TbNloGLGUcHa9mGemblGSE6uMEh2Hjan6JkRh5ne/HTTuc8i\njvj7UyfrMaiURr2Le+hPzRJ+RbZmHNT37khDkbyGnU8zsjt2scoH1v3h6JbrMGyA\nCHYIGIjPKlRkPCWwu/V92k6oV72HpFhvv+6f78Hdam1l9mhs2nAgxby58y66jAT2\nFk1uz+3j/EGCiaBZ1swlbb0z6D+lgWLRkFIKaqWjH2WL9fBKLlTnHlGt4dCzqzvZ\nt54GvmkFsrZo3ZQGQ78qdkUUgDjVAg==\n=cHYN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/02f8d8663edcce1d716508f989934e47c0a8a15f","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDAyZjhkODY2M2VkY2NlMWQ3MTY1MDhmOTg5OTM0ZTQ3YzBhOGExNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/ce0e41349d367e4fb12082b2cf6790788d18aa91","sha":"ce0e41349d367e4fb12082b2cf6790788d18aa91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/ce0e41349d367e4fb12082b2cf6790788d18aa91"}],"sha":"02f8d8663edcce1d716508f989934e47c0a8a15f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/02f8d8663edcce1d716508f989934e47c0a8a15f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/ce0e41349d367e4fb12082b2cf6790788d18aa91/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T19:47:49Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T19:47:49Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"Fix hasCredentials() counting unrelated user-node children as credentials\n\nAfter an admin reset (resetUserWebauthn) the upaWebauthn:userSettings mixin\nlegitimately stays on the user node (it still tracks the grace window), but\nhasCredentials() answered ''mixin present && any child node'' — and real user\nnodes always carry unrelated children (preferences, j:acl, files, ...). The\nfactor therefore still reported the user as registered: sign-in prepared an\nunsatisfiable passkey assertion instead of offering enrollment again.\n\nFilter the children by the upaWebauthn:credential node type, like every\nother iteration in the store already does. Adds an e2e regression test that\nplants a non-credential child under the test user before the admin reset\nand asserts the enrollment chooser (not the assertion form) is shown.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"be491c123356a8b84e5eebd087abeb0304b9d15e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/be491c123356a8b84e5eebd087abeb0304b9d15e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/ce0e41349d367e4fb12082b2cf6790788d18aa91","verification":{"payload":"tree be491c123356a8b84e5eebd087abeb0304b9d15e\nparent 9b0081224c10d3a4f9124c25cc1f7f95dcdb8442\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780775269 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780775269 +0200\n\nFix hasCredentials() counting unrelated user-node children as credentials\n\nAfter an admin reset (resetUserWebauthn) the upaWebauthn:userSettings mixin\nlegitimately stays on the user node (it still tracks the grace window), but\nhasCredentials() answered ''mixin present && any child node'' — and real user\nnodes always carry unrelated children (preferences, j:acl, files, ...). The\nfactor therefore still reported the user as registered: sign-in prepared an\nunsatisfiable passkey assertion instead of offering enrollment again.\n\nFilter the children by the upaWebauthn:credential node type, like every\nother iteration in the store already does. Adds an e2e regression test that\nplants a non-credential child under the test user before the admin reset\nand asserts the enrollment chooser (not the assertion form) is shown.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmokeWUACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3n6Iwf8DAryhhBGXw/ZuvdAtZgcg7wF/TJxU0BfptsWxhkZEOssAXYj+KouWfRK\nyWbUS1KAfydQsiQsG+vseipNo8qotGN6z1ESJq5QYFAQvMLQXBLzQUgWTCZiwy/j\nyFl1+b9kEFqZPLAi6CQBpmmzbzAConwoQmSc2HGGB+/SvnUHH6DPoYE06Zdlr5go\n6+6Og4o+5SN/M4hTO67CbmhF4Iy90nuYs3lQ3WP4X242JxCBxK6hT6AgkqMNz5he\npcbj1VfAir+rlSoJdbzM4aAYBMBwmQ8uRzTUZoDc63E7A8G/WR7ZIYDQpbAlLLMB\n59RGnNDA91+FMy1c06IYKH9xKsaJ/A==\n=ZrPW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/ce0e41349d367e4fb12082b2cf6790788d18aa91","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKGNlMGU0MTM0OWQzNjdlNGZiMTIwODJiMmNmNjc5MDc4OGQxOGFhOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/9b0081224c10d3a4f9124c25cc1f7f95dcdb8442","sha":"9b0081224c10d3a4f9124c25cc1f7f95dcdb8442","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/9b0081224c10d3a4f9124c25cc1f7f95dcdb8442"}],"sha":"ce0e41349d367e4fb12082b2cf6790788d18aa91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/ce0e41349d367e4fb12082b2cf6790788d18aa91"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/9b0081224c10d3a4f9124c25cc1f7f95dcdb8442/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T18:49:59Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T18:49:59Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"test(webauthn): inline registration e2e through a CDP virtual authenticator\n\nFirst e2e to drive the full WebAuthn ceremony: enrollment chooser ->\nattestation (navigator.credentials.create) -> immediate assertion ->\ntotp pick-one drain -> authenticated, on the suite''s own UPA shape\n(mfaEnabledFactors=totp). Second test proves the pre-auth door closes\nafter registration. Needs a Chromium secure context on http://jahia:8080:\nrun with\nELECTRON_EXTRA_LAUNCH_ARGS=--unsafely-treat-insecure-origin-as-secure=http://jahia:8080\nand the suite repoints rpId=jahia (restored in after()). The virtual\nauthenticator helper is idempotent: a second authenticator would race the\nfirst one''s credentials and fail assertions with NotAllowedError.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"de1c2de8499eb64cbc0b6a38965fe38941acbada","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/de1c2de8499eb64cbc0b6a38965fe38941acbada"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/9b0081224c10d3a4f9124c25cc1f7f95dcdb8442","verification":{"payload":"tree de1c2de8499eb64cbc0b6a38965fe38941acbada\nparent 374d66a83978b0d575c01a5e622fe4371e2a816e\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780771799 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780771799 +0200\n\ntest(webauthn): inline registration e2e through a CDP virtual authenticator\n\nFirst e2e to drive the full WebAuthn ceremony: enrollment chooser ->\nattestation (navigator.credentials.create) -> immediate assertion ->\ntotp pick-one drain -> authenticated, on the suite''s own UPA shape\n(mfaEnabledFactors=totp). Second test proves the pre-auth door closes\nafter registration. Needs a Chromium secure context on http://jahia:8080:\nrun with\nELECTRON_EXTRA_LAUNCH_ARGS=--unsafely-treat-insecure-origin-as-secure=http://jahia:8080\nand the suite repoints rpId=jahia (restored in after()). The virtual\nauthenticator helper is idempotent: a second authenticator would race the\nfirst one''s credentials and fail assertions with NotAllowedError.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmoka9cACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lHhgf/cTQyl9tyeTa854R97gxxh3csWChxR2SkexUQoZzwM6mQocAHplsT19hP\nb0AKrqV74GM0nL/MbYBON9aA1JowYmrcPAoVQl71feTwCqJVMgxbTbuRXRUsm8d3\nIJl5ROfjcPN9ZyHrVlm9/x4vZ4+o5F032qFY0v4dlOXucavioSTIV9O0C+YXXMgl\nZQCJBNIpjkzLPbyDIp2s8hQFfZSFerYWKMVGMJpVpsVfx6pZrtHq+yzfPG4s8wJA\n5Em0SSOKpbcnR5GXGLD71ZDEIqyXHuJtnpFYqQhabfZLs1QSo5qcRuFM8l2bh7OY\n4DkkEIMETMNw+RjKyqUuUdSe0dkYpQ==\n=I+5n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"h