url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/374d66a83978b0d575c01a5e622fe4371e2a816e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T18:49:59Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T18:49:59Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(login-ui): server-side webauthn failures rendered raw i18n keys\n\nfactor.webauthn.registration_failed / no_registration_state /\nnot_registered had no locale entry, so a server-rejected registration\nshowed the literal key instead of a message.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"40cd016ae779516699c1f099045e749076833afa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/40cd016ae779516699c1f099045e749076833afa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/374d66a83978b0d575c01a5e622fe4371e2a816e","verification":{"payload":"tree 40cd016ae779516699c1f099045e749076833afa\nparent 9ada4ad2ac44556d79a9cae61809e0027ce64c8e\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780771799 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780771799 +0200\n\nfix(login-ui): server-side webauthn failures rendered raw i18n keys\n\nfactor.webauthn.registration_failed / no_registration_state /\nnot_registered had no locale entry, so a server-rejected registration\nshowed the literal key instead of a message.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmoka9cACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3m9ygf+Mg++8fwchxR8FCKYkc9//4CxN/Vxa2heNMffeivCSNRfYcwfuR4QSfbt\nE+s4Bbr1fKxppaCfO8gaEBYMTO+oO6YuJIDvMRwCQvSmRc9Mp1KmmjWtpXLHNahX\nKRy0gPQVKvUcaiQ94C+mUeT8rwjW3tp5hoYdsZKh1WX7DrNrwyB8O81iPNyTmy2e\nilhwHcPqI9CYGdsXamb7ZQnnmmkAwxdarhy7wo4DGi3p3DOpSIlqciFix/FthN+/\n+mybu2FBgd88r9bDtWwkxB1pCcm6PC25pUKHXXY1KFUK7K0nyxvr9wAHrzdb/n1I\nuFmykT0UwbxPXWR1kV+EBpWMSCySNg==\n=JDKk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/374d66a83978b0d575c01a5e622fe4371e2a816e","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDM3NGQ2NmE4Mzk3OGIwZDU3NWMwMWE1ZTYyMmZlNDM3MWUyYTgxNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/9ada4ad2ac44556d79a9cae61809e0027ce64c8e","sha":"9ada4ad2ac44556d79a9cae61809e0027ce64c8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/9ada4ad2ac44556d79a9cae61809e0027ce64c8e"}],"sha":"374d66a83978b0d575c01a5e622fe4371e2a816e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/374d66a83978b0d575c01a5e622fe4371e2a816e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/9ada4ad2ac44556d79a9cae61809e0027ce64c8e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T18:49:45Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T18:49:45Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: warn loudly when pick-one skips for an enforced factor UPA never challenges\n\nPick-one assumed every factor in enforcedFactors is also in UPA''s\nmfaEnabledFactors. When it is not (e.g. mfaEnabledFactors=totp,\nenforcedFactors=totp,webauthn), a user who configured ONLY the not-required\nfactor satisfies enforcement via the sibling-configured skip while that\nfactor itself is never verified — the sign-in completes on password alone.\n\nBlocking would dead-end the user (pre-auth inline enrollment is closed once\nany enforced factor is owned), so the providers keep the skip but log an\nexplicit WARN naming the missing mfaEnabledFactors entry. README documents\nthe constraint; decision-table unit tests cover the new row, and the\nwebauthn inline-registration e2e exercises it live.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"ed97f1e75a3148237f019165f0cb6a2cc2cf912b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/ed97f1e75a3148237f019165f0cb6a2cc2cf912b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/9ada4ad2ac44556d79a9cae61809e0027ce64c8e","verification":{"payload":"tree ed97f1e75a3148237f019165f0cb6a2cc2cf912b\nparent 5270c87df71b02be80eccb3d2d50ebf07f0b53b2\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780771785 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780771785 +0200\n\nfix: warn loudly when pick-one skips for an enforced factor UPA never challenges\n\nPick-one assumed every factor in enforcedFactors is also in UPA''s\nmfaEnabledFactors. When it is not (e.g. mfaEnabledFactors=totp,\nenforcedFactors=totp,webauthn), a user who configured ONLY the not-required\nfactor satisfies enforcement via the sibling-configured skip while that\nfactor itself is never verified — the sign-in completes on password alone.\n\nBlocking would dead-end the user (pre-auth inline enrollment is closed once\nany enforced factor is owned), so the providers keep the skip but log an\nexplicit WARN naming the missing mfaEnabledFactors entry. README documents\nthe constraint; decision-table unit tests cover the new row, and the\nwebauthn inline-registration e2e exercises it live.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmoka8kACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3k0pAgAl0ChucjOY2Y0LkFeN58DWjoDz3YTMHztg5tyRFEbhtp+/VTHfyKO0FIe\nQb8mmf/6Uy36LR/6l0M0Mp4kvwSNg2NkRphn0D9XETPNO7cB82a5+oIkOs3fSbds\nVP/ctPO8756+bybDce/Prmgw+uoluwfiFoz1qL/UIYS8iRXHvOYF+HHN4ASTc2Hr\nmHOJurnCyvrHdnuh1/wD+g4MjCSqnWHydzYnUzIQwYpEElEpv56by3KTboc4cfmR\nmYqgaXYtmJ+2xCyqBJnrKmh2zytHXnqjwvZS+1X+HqEqfLWpvOevholQcADsxnkx\nt3cnXQtgfcNrlu+rBQdkjkY136HLsA==\n=rTtF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/9ada4ad2ac44556d79a9cae61809e0027ce64c8e","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDlhZGE0YWQyYWM0NDU1NmQ3OWE5Y2FlNjE4MDllMDAyN2NlNjRjOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/5270c87df71b02be80eccb3d2d50ebf07f0b53b2","sha":"5270c87df71b02be80eccb3d2d50ebf07f0b53b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/5270c87df71b02be80eccb3d2d50ebf07f0b53b2"}],"sha":"9ada4ad2ac44556d79a9cae61809e0027ce64c8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/9ada4ad2ac44556d79a9cae61809e0027ce64c8e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/5270c87df71b02be80eccb3d2d50ebf07f0b53b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T18:49:33Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T18:49:33Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(totp): the pick-one drain''s empty code never reached the provider\n\nThe client drains a SKIPPED totp preparation (pick-one satisfied by another\nfactor) with verify(''''), and TotpFactorProvider.verify accepts any\nsubmission for a skipped preparation — but the verify mutation''s code-length\nprecheck threw invalid_code before mfaService.verifyFactor ran, so the MFA\nsession never completed and the login UI dead-ended on ''An unexpected error\noccurred'' right after a successful inline webauthn registration.\n\nThe precheck now lets an unacceptable-length code through only when the\nfactor''s preparation is marked skipped; everything else keeps failing fast,\nshielding the rate limiter from garbage submissions.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"8de443fb669542edf0e5177990e1c0cdf44c6f57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/8de443fb669542edf0e5177990e1c0cdf44c6f57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/5270c87df71b02be80eccb3d2d50ebf07f0b53b2","verification":{"payload":"tree 8de443fb669542edf0e5177990e1c0cdf44c6f57\nparent a45e845eeac4edc2927c72b28b80e3e132515008\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780771773 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780771773 +0200\n\nfix(totp): the pick-one drain''s empty code never reached the provider\n\nThe client drains a SKIPPED totp preparation (pick-one satisfied by another\nfactor) with verify(''''), and TotpFactorProvider.verify accepts any\nsubmission for a skipped preparation — but the verify mutation''s code-length\nprecheck threw invalid_code before mfaService.verifyFactor ran, so the MFA\nsession never completed and the login UI dead-ended on ''An unexpected error\noccurred'' right after a successful inline webauthn registration.\n\nThe precheck now lets an unacceptable-length code through only when the\nfactor''s preparation is marked skipped; everything else keeps failing fast,\nshielding the rate limiter from garbage submissions.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmoka70ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3nM7Af/VnqZmpPjdWr4rbzRGxoOL4rZQhk+3SkZud0W0eM5hSyrbwHdEO4pZl5G\nGtMtlHM2ToKlrrI+eQ3Iom8Wz5w9IJ+/e6g+NI5BV9uWadqtbuRhHxYzkfK7m1ES\n3QSfA3H4qyVXwlRmKf3zcB0/X+TrJTTXITqyWnX0E45JuNfQM33c7POb7BiZF7ml\nbGfJhW0KFkjdZLx6dlyO/5FnPigqs1PR/d050AvC2OEys+jez9h+KMoTa4C1SLVd\nuB8s5/ewKbecmfIaJPvVRyTXsaCcLNtTaF1h7liop/0FP+0BQ+HvwJS3a4/4dN8S\nbT+iZT//7RH2UBqjTXAHmJa0IfKDtA==\n=pAeo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/5270c87df71b02be80eccb3d2d50ebf07f0b53b2","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDUyNzBjODdkZjcxYjAyYmU4MGVjY2IzZDJkNTBlYmYwN2YwYjUzYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/a45e845eeac4edc2927c72b28b80e3e132515008","sha":"a45e845eeac4edc2927c72b28b80e3e132515008","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/a45e845eeac4edc2927c72b28b80e3e132515008"}],"sha":"5270c87df71b02be80eccb3d2d50ebf07f0b53b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/5270c87df71b02be80eccb3d2d50ebf07f0b53b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/a45e845eeac4edc2927c72b28b80e3e132515008/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T18:49:23Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T18:49:23Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(webauthn): plain-http localhost deployments failed every ceremony at finish time\n\nWith no origins configured, the yubico RelyingParty defaults the allowed\norigins to https://<rpId> ONLY (scheme is never relaxed), so a browser on\nhttp://localhost:<port> always got ''incorrect origin'' from\nfinishRegistration/finishAssertion — surfacing in the login UI as ''Could\nnot register your authenticator''.\n\nWebAuthnConfig now derives BOTH https://<rpId> and http://<rpId> when no\norigins are set (browsers only allow WebAuthn without TLS on\nlocalhost-style hosts, so accepting the http form is safe), and self-parses\nthe origins property from the raw map: an OSGi String[] cannot be expressed\nin a .cfg file (a comma string coerces to one bogus element and the\ndocumented origins.N indexed keys never bound at all). Comma-separated and\nindexed forms are both accepted now, and the RelyingParty is always built\nwith explicit origins.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"ebff78e3eed0178425853fa48657d7245576dbdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/ebff78e3eed0178425853fa48657d7245576dbdd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/a45e845eeac4edc2927c72b28b80e3e132515008","verification":{"payload":"tree ebff78e3eed0178425853fa48657d7245576dbdd\nparent ae1816fc7e5de290d50e9711339535407414e071\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780771763 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780771763 +0200\n\nfix(webauthn): plain-http localhost deployments failed every ceremony at finish time\n\nWith no origins configured, the yubico RelyingParty defaults the allowed\norigins to https://<rpId> ONLY (scheme is never relaxed), so a browser on\nhttp://localhost:<port> always got ''incorrect origin'' from\nfinishRegistration/finishAssertion — surfacing in the login UI as ''Could\nnot register your authenticator''.\n\nWebAuthnConfig now derives BOTH https://<rpId> and http://<rpId> when no\norigins are set (browsers only allow WebAuthn without TLS on\nlocalhost-style hosts, so accepting the http form is safe), and self-parses\nthe origins property from the raw map: an OSGi String[] cannot be expressed\nin a .cfg file (a comma string coerces to one bogus element and the\ndocumented origins.N indexed keys never bound at all). Comma-separated and\nindexed forms are both accepted now, and the RelyingParty is always built\nwith explicit origins.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmoka7MACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lsfAf/blTD7qWqSdSZfrkZ7C3Tv1NEENxrAkr4iO2iLeFpAq6Ko8jY4yvs9Tqt\nkSpHKrxjTQIazksEh+pB0H942omkfjF9xfba0s6bZCBEpXp8i/FNdjwGBlYU0CBS\nT2tRfsXWdhJnMNE+jIZ+X5XXyETvU3JQFeIQW9wbjxH/awTIUFXew59w947kPTJk\n4bRtoyYpzZ0I2cdzljiAOocqKeBWw+LsvmTwlQCbXIXF02hkp1be1qYs1V1dBNnI\nnayqZpJRD9c0ye+l3kv33unI+aiEfWY8jFG3GezAptrZAWl1jXaRsb86SbKucGZ2\nSaPc6SK6YPtv1GXRYIzI2jGsuSmpiQ==\n=yxIG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/a45e845eeac4edc2927c72b28b80e3e132515008","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKGE0NWU4NDVlZWFjNGVkYzI5MjdjNzJiMjhiODBlM2UxMzI1MTUwMDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/ae1816fc7e5de290d50e9711339535407414e071","sha":"ae1816fc7e5de290d50e9711339535407414e071","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/ae1816fc7e5de290d50e9711339535407414e071"}],"sha":"a45e845eeac4edc2927c72b28b80e3e132515008","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/a45e845eeac4edc2927c72b28b80e3e132515008"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/ae1816fc7e5de290d50e9711339535407414e071/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T17:51:51Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T17:51:51Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: missing site context at sign-in broke inline enrollment on vanity URLs\n\nSigning in as an unconfigured user on a site served under a vanity/server-name URL showed\n\"Two-factor authentication is not configured for this account\" (not_enrolled) instead of the\ninline enrollment page: the login UI extracted the site key from the URL path with a\n/sites/<key> regex, which yields nothing on vanity URLs, so mfaInitiate ran without a site\nand the factor providers fell into the legacy no-site branch.\n\nFrontend: the server component now passes renderContext.getSite().getSiteKey() through the\ncomponent props — authoritative regardless of how the page URL is served; the URL heuristic\nremains as a fallback only.\n\nBackend (defense in depth): the no-site branch of both factor providers is now\nenforcement-aware (prepareForGlobalOnly): when the factor is globally enforced, the pick-one\nrows apply (another-factor-verified/configured skips, enrolled challenge, grace then\nenrollment_required carrying the offer — installed enforced factors, since per-site\nactivation cannot be evaluated without a site). Without enforcement the legacy behavior is\npreserved. +4 unit rows; live suite 14 specs 48/48.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"c42289378c4de57b29ad34a7234876e69cf7082c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/c42289378c4de57b29ad34a7234876e69cf7082c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/ae1816fc7e5de290d50e9711339535407414e071","verification":{"payload":"tree c42289378c4de57b29ad34a7234876e69cf7082c\nparent 51a3de6dd1dce900cf81467aef2844ae57780a6a\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780768311 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780768311 +0200\n\nfix: missing site context at sign-in broke inline enrollment on vanity URLs\n\nSigning in as an unconfigured user on a site served under a vanity/server-name URL showed\n\"Two-factor authentication is not configured for this account\" (not_enrolled) instead of the\ninline enrollment page: the login UI extracted the site key from the URL path with a\n/sites/<key> regex, which yields nothing on vanity URLs, so mfaInitiate ran without a site\nand the factor providers fell into the legacy no-site branch.\n\nFrontend: the server component now passes renderContext.getSite().getSiteKey() through the\ncomponent props — authoritative regardless of how the page URL is served; the URL heuristic\nremains as a fallback only.\n\nBackend (defense in depth): the no-site branch of both factor providers is now\nenforcement-aware (prepareForGlobalOnly): when the factor is globally enforced, the pick-one\nrows apply (another-factor-verified/configured skips, enrolled challenge, grace then\nenrollment_required carrying the offer — installed enforced factors, since per-site\nactivation cannot be evaluated without a site). Without enforcement the legacy behavior is\npreserved. +4 unit rows; live suite 14 specs 48/48.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmokXjcACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lWLwgAzW9n