a/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/65fd3fefb16e66a352eb20c3668576ac21ffc075","verification":{"payload":"tree cc32a5e80f48699b7c969a71b1d4bb0e6f0b1025\nparent 8f2fe0df82165c01703fea0600b4b82b96e68293\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780754959 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780754959 +0200\n\nrefactor(totp): clear SonarQube S107/S1128\n\nfinalizePreAuthEnrollment generates the backup codes itself (6 params instead of 8); drop an\nunused import in the enforcement test. SonarQube: 0 open issues; all new-code reliability and\nsecurity conditions green.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmokKg8ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lNuAgAwfqNZxiph/0O+nTe0fOqC7VLNXIcNvYGbFdKv81bLWiFusfn9TjYlEgw\nA8Z7LbOGTcxXdguKQZDZi5N9Wnbs2aiHwO7TyrTn1nSzk0NdtDCRZVSgO85L8a07\nJI5a3cbZoc6VX1ZCMLcoAQ3V4icxwwt8Lx8uOpnkQSDy63aLAyfH5B9NtwTpuHTr\nDeIIsDBKzW9OD9rW41kIB2XvEs1RIWT96QjpYM/1/RxRf6o7FTvl+DrG5+GkCGrX\n6/KNxn6W7spJkbb7Plc6lPxPamcLIrtdK6CxbGAXDNy32TfFexTrPFoYJ1kx3CTw\ni04Amlvx/R840j0ZjhrRyBMlLEi2zw==\n=27e9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/65fd3fefb16e66a352eb20c3668576ac21ffc075","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDY1ZmQzZmVmYjE2ZTY2YTM1MmViMjBjMzY2ODU3NmFjMjFmZmMwNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/8f2fe0df82165c01703fea0600b4b82b96e68293","sha":"8f2fe0df82165c01703fea0600b4b82b96e68293","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/8f2fe0df82165c01703fea0600b4b82b96e68293"}],"sha":"65fd3fefb16e66a352eb20c3668576ac21ffc075","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/65fd3fefb16e66a352eb20c3668576ac21ffc075"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/8f2fe0df82165c01703fea0600b4b82b96e68293/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T14:05:12Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T14:05:12Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix+test: guest-aware identity resolution + enforcement e2e coverage\n\nSECURITY FIX found by the new e2e spec: Jahia resolves unauthenticated GraphQL requests to\nthe GUEST user, not to null, so the previous user==null checks treated anonymous callers as\nauthenticated \"guest\" — the inline-enrollment pre-auth branch never fired and the flow\nsilently enrolled the literal guest account (the same latent flaw existed in the pre-change\nself-service mutations: disable/regenerate/status would have operated on guest). All identity\nresolutions now go through currentNonGuestUser()/guest-aware checks in both factor mutations\nand status queries; the pre-auth guard fires correctly for anonymous callers.\n\nCypress: setSiteTotpSettings drops the enforced parameter; new setGlobalEnforcement helper\n(editConfiguration on org.jahia.modules.mfa.extensions, reverted in after());\ngraphQL.totp/webauthn.adminPolicy updated to the enabled/enabledGroups surface (grace-clamp\ncoverage lives in MfaGlobalPolicyTest now); http.loginGate arms via global enforcedFactors +\nper-site enabled. NEW ui.totp.enrollAtLogin.cy.ts: full inline enrollment at sign-in\n(password -> QR -> code -> backup codes -> authenticated) plus the anti-takeover regression\ncheck (a configured user is challenged, never offered enrollment).\n\nREADME: documents the verified Felix typed .config route for multi-factor UPA config\n(mfaEnabledFactors=[\"totp\",\"webauthn\"] yields both factors; comma/.cfg silently breaks).\n\nFull suite green: 12 specs, 39/39 on the live stack.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"2e5273f48fa76cd57ca38447c2fb9ae9c190331b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/2e5273f48fa76cd57ca38447c2fb9ae9c190331b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/8f2fe0df82165c01703fea0600b4b82b96e68293","verification":{"payload":"tree 2e5273f48fa76cd57ca38447c2fb9ae9c190331b\nparent b447aff597d6b3897f08c8faead23f71ea9dfaf9\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780754712 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780754712 +0200\n\nfix+test: guest-aware identity resolution + enforcement e2e coverage\n\nSECURITY FIX found by the new e2e spec: Jahia resolves unauthenticated GraphQL requests to\nthe GUEST user, not to null, so the previous user==null checks treated anonymous callers as\nauthenticated \"guest\" — the inline-enrollment pre-auth branch never fired and the flow\nsilently enrolled the literal guest account (the same latent flaw existed in the pre-change\nself-service mutations: disable/regenerate/status would have operated on guest). All identity\nresolutions now go through currentNonGuestUser()/guest-aware checks in both factor mutations\nand status queries; the pre-auth guard fires correctly for anonymous callers.\n\nCypress: setSiteTotpSettings drops the enforced parameter; new setGlobalEnforcement helper\n(editConfiguration on org.jahia.modules.mfa.extensions, reverted in after());\ngraphQL.totp/webauthn.adminPolicy updated to the enabled/enabledGroups surface (grace-clamp\ncoverage lives in MfaGlobalPolicyTest now); http.loginGate arms via global enforcedFactors +\nper-site enabled. NEW ui.totp.enrollAtLogin.cy.ts: full inline enrollment at sign-in\n(password -> QR -> code -> backup codes -> authenticated) plus the anti-takeover regression\ncheck (a configured user is challenged, never offered enrollment).\n\nREADME: documents the verified Felix typed .config route for multi-factor UPA config\n(mfaEnabledFactors=[\"totp\",\"webauthn\"] yields both factors; comma/.cfg silently breaks).\n\nFull suite green: 12 specs, 39/39 on the live stack.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFi