/api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/8f2fe0df82165c01703fea0600b4b82b96e68293"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/b447aff597d6b3897f08c8faead23f71ea9dfaf9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T13:33:34Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T13:33:34Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"refactor!: drop the per-site enforced/graceDays model\n\nEnforcement (and its grace window) is now exclusively the global extensions policy\n(enforcedFactors + graceDays under PID org.jahia.modules.mfa.extensions). Per-site keeps\nenabled + enabledGroups (+ the TOTP login/logout URLs).\n\nBackend: both site-settings stores stop reading/writing the enforced/graceDays properties\n(snapshots and constructors lose the fields; saves and logs trimmed); the setSiteSettings\nmutations drop the enforced/graceDays parameters (and the invalid_grace_days error - the\ngrace clamp lives in MfaGlobalPolicy now); the siteSettings query results lose the fields.\nThe CND properties are RETAINED with a deprecation comment so existing repositories need no\nnode migration - the values simply become inert.\n\nAdmin UI: the Enforce checkbox and grace-period field are removed from both factor panels;\nthe page descriptions point to the global enforcedFactors setting; the Extensions page\nround-trips only enabled/enabledGroups; locales and mapAdminError cleaned.\n\nREADME documents the global enforcement semantics (at-least-one, inline enrollment after\ngrace) and the migration note (existing per-site enforced values stop having any effect;\noperators must opt in via enforcedFactors).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"cdcad555311a5f5a2226a38834c9e42934c1133b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/cdcad555311a5f5a2226a38834c9e42934c1133b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/b447aff597d6b3897f08c8faead23f71ea9dfaf9","verification":{"payload":"tree cdcad555311a5f5a2226a38834c9e42934c1133b\nparent 7d001da4321957ca06591841b31599498e67884b\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780752814 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780752814 +0200\n\nrefactor!: drop the per-site enforced/graceDays model\n\nEnforcement (and its grace window) is now exclusively the global extensions policy\n(enforcedFactors + graceDays under PID org.jahia.modules.mfa.extensions). Per-site keeps\nenabled + enabledGroups (+ the TOTP login/logout URLs).\n\nBackend: both site-settings stores stop reading/writing the enforced/graceDays properties\n(snapshots and constructors lose the fields; saves and logs trimmed); the setSiteSettings\nmutations drop the enforced/graceDays parameters (and the invalid_grace_days error - the\ngrace clamp lives in MfaGlobalPolicy now); the siteSettings query results lose the fields.\nThe CND properties are RETAINED with a deprecation comment so existing repositories need no\nnode migration - the values simply become inert.\n\nAdmin UI: the Enforce checkbox and grace-period field are removed from both factor panels;\nthe page descriptions point to the global enforcedFactors setting; the Extensions page\nround-trips only enabled/enabledGroups; locales and mapAdminError cleaned.\n\nREADME documents the global enforcement semantics (at-least-one, inline enrollment after\ngrace) and the migration note (existing per-site enforced values stop having any effect;\noperators must opt in via enforcedFactors).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmokIa4ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kTQAf/SIMGCHG4XorDNQk0AB/vJowdoyjdbFa4C+caDatx3ksNaBWfDth4d1EH\nbv5FX8H4rgTZVRe3hCYIl0OSaAjFpMOqySbDMZFjLs4f/sbwE2WkwgAo+KMAwKXb\ndcqOVLfWG0pJ9i1dy5iXuYTbBrTzryz2VGHhbRQFwmZPmTR9ZkbkD6tpfG/2Ee3x\nJkMhuDN9f8WstybiCwZVhpmLZKmVqsD7805TpIgSwSxDOnuVzz9hXKF3u0tjHq0H\nOPhBWR8fJn4hWQGVgBUPlkly0m2DWU99uhfBuKzW2xUca0DHNx4K1r18IYdIux+i\nOZtJtQLnpHzY16K2Stnf6mdVXvXL1A==\n=2ESa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/b447aff597d6b3897f08c8faead23f71ea9dfaf9","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKGI0NDdhZmY1OTdkNmIzODk3ZjA4YzhmYWVhZDIzZjcxZWE5ZGZhZjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/7d001da4321957ca06591841b31599498e67884b","sha":"7d001da4321957ca06591841b31599498e67884b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/7d001da4321957ca06591841b31599498e67884b"}],"sha":"b447aff597d6b3897f08c8faead23f71ea9dfaf9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/b447aff597d6b3897f08c8faead23f71ea9dfaf9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/7d001da4321957ca06591841b31599498e67884b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T13:19:38Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T13:19:38Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"feat(login-ui): inline enrollment step + multi-factor flow\n\nNew Step.ENROLL in the authentication flow: when enforcement is active and the signing-in\nuser has no enforced factor configured, the enrollment_required/registration_required error\n(carrying the enrollableFactors offer from the server) switches the page to inline\nenrollment instead of the old dead-end dashboard redirect:\n - EnrollmentChooser when several factors are offered;\n - TotpEnrollmentForm: enroll -> QR (qrcode.react) + secret -> first authenticator code ->\n   server persists AND verifies in one request -> one-shot backup codes acknowledgement;\n - WebauthnRegistrationForm: register the passkey (navigator.credentials.create via the new\n   createCredential helper) then immediately run the standard assertion to finish signing in.\n\nMulti-factor completion: onSuccess callbacks now carry remainingFactors and the flow\ncontinues to the next factor instead of redirecting blindly; factors that do not apply\n(pick-one enforcement satisfied, site disabled) report skipped=true from prepare and are\ndrained automatically with an empty verify.\n\nNew services (enrollTotp, confirmEnrollTotp, startRegistrationWebauthn,\nfinishRegistrationWebauthn) + topLevelError helper for DataFetchingException codes; locales\ngain the enroll.* keys. tsc + vite build green.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"4095b46c1c46b9d63939df0fb006f4dde7df7b19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/4095b46c1c46b9d63939df0fb006f4dde7df7b19"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/7d001da4321957ca06591841b31599498e67884b","verification":{"payload":"tree 4095b46c1c46b9d63939df0fb006f4dde7df7b19\nparent 52bb0a0001f6ca3504c0a504fc2a7e62ee79415b\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780751978 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780751978 +0200\n\nfeat(login-ui): inline enrollment step + multi-factor flow\n\nNew Step.ENROLL in the authentication flow: when enforcement is active and the signing-in\nuser has no enforced factor configured, the enrollment_required/registration_required error\n(carrying the enrollableFactors offer from the server) switches the page to inline\nenrollment instead of the old dead-end dashboard redirect:\n - EnrollmentChooser when several factors are offered;\n - TotpEnrollmentForm: enroll -> QR (qrcode.react) + secret -> first authenticator code ->\n   server persists AND verifies in one request -> one-shot backup codes acknowledgement;\n - WebauthnRegistrationForm: register the passkey (navigator.credentials.create via the new\n   createCredential helper) then immediately run the standard assertion to finish signing in.\n\nMulti-factor completion: onSuccess callbacks now carry remainingFactors and the flow\ncontinues to the next factor instead of redirecting blindly; factors that do not apply\n(pick-one enforcement satisfied, site disabled) report skipped=true from prepare and are\ndrained automatically with an empty verify.\n\nNew services (enrollTotp, confirmEnrollTotp, startRegistrationWebauthn,\nfinishRegistrationWebauthn) + topLevelError helper for DataFetchingException codes; locales\ngain the enroll.* keys. tsc + vite build green.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmokHmoACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lvoQf+I16VoO4DW7sAXSxES28IJAwDDIffcftHnxdhsbAQl7o8ShoDohIkzZZ5\nTLXG6uk4Z9pUUZ/fCMWjk/WO6rr278eSJVOXFJevWcibFJ8gbH6c+0Ayrewv8Tco\naAccjWbabHlwbwOEVYhChEZJv4gc5iGo8yJxxzkg593/Lq4gZNHXHtJjLjTsPQQi\nRzJ3Po1yrRkJHY3Uco64tfVbm6oelbD4OcLcCvkFUbhzVcrODnOAgTH1GaSmdvkt\n7pei/kiej/ZZVHxd+33sY7y03OX8V8e9wq8ZRexG1uJ3e2LfMUi1BzD0yu0x/v4o\n9PsGAIYFKChmezfG9Azr5+gJYpRAYw==\n=QWwH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/7d001da4321957ca06591841b31599498e67884b","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDdkMDAxZGE0MzIxOTU3Y2EwNjU5MTg0MWIzMTU5OTQ5OGU2Nzg4NGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/52bb0a0001f6ca3504c0a504fc2a7e62ee79415b","sha":"52bb0a0001f6ca3504c0a504fc2a7e62ee79415b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/52bb0a0001f6ca3504c0a504fc2a7e62ee79415b"}],"sha":"7d001da4321957ca06591841b31599498e67884b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/7d001da4321957ca06591841b31599498e67884b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/52bb0a0001f6ca3504c0a504fc2a7e62ee79415b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T13:07:36Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T13:07:36Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"feat: pre-authentication inline enrollment mutations (security-guarded)\n\nBoth factor mutation surfaces gain a pre-auth path for inline enrollment during sign-in,\nallowed ONLY when ALL of these hold (fail closed on any doubt):\n 1. no authenticated Jahia user (the authenticated self-service path is unchanged);\n 2. an initiated, error-free MFA session exists - the password was already validated;\n 3. the factor is part of the global enforcement policy;\n 4. the session user owns NO globally enforced factor (anti-takeover barrier: a stolen\n    password must never be able to add a factor to an account that already has one) -\n    checked through the new extensions MfaFactorDirectory aggregator, whose errors\n    propagate so the guard refuses rather than assumes.\n\nTOTP: enroll() resolves the subject from the MFA session (force rejected pre-auth);\nconfirmEnroll() persists the enrollment with lastUsedCounter = -1 (NOT consuming the\nmatched counter) and immediately delegates to mfaService.verifyFactor, so the standard\nverifyAndConsumeTotp chokepoint consumes the code atomically, marks the factor verified\nand - once every required factor is done - authenticates the user in the same request.\nBackup codes are returned as usual.\n\nWebAuthn: startRegistration/finishRegistration accept the guarded pre-auth subject; the\nsession is NOT completed at registration (attestation is not an assertion) - the client\nruns the standard assert+verify right after. New JCR-backed WebAuthnManagementRateLimiter\n(upaWebauthn:lockout mixin, mirrors the TOTP limiter) throttles the pre-auth registration\nsurface.\n\nAGENTS.md: chokepoint invariant updated for the delegated consume; new pre-auth guard\ninvariant documented.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"1d3212da76b466ce7f3904bfb64fe6a300ba126e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/1d3212da76b466ce7f3904bfb64fe6a300ba126e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/52bb0a0001f6ca3504c0a504fc2a7e62ee79415b","verification":{"payload":"tree 1d3212da76b466ce7f3904bfb64fe6a300ba126e\nparent e441a764f18e787a95b6a031564009b3d370aa68\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780751256 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780751256 +0200\n\nfeat: pre-authentication inline enrollment mutations (security-guarded)\n\nBoth factor mutation surfaces gain a pre-auth path for inline enrollment during sign-in,\nallowed ONLY when ALL of these hold (fail closed on any doubt):\n 1. no authenticated Jahia user (the authenticated self-service path is unchanged);\n 2. an initiated, error-free MFA session exists - the password was already validated;\n 3. the factor is part of the global enforcement policy;\n 4. the session user owns NO globally enforced factor (anti-takeover barrier: a stolen\n    password must never be able to add a factor to an account that already has one) -\n    checked through the new extensions MfaFactorDirectory aggregator, whose errors\n    propagate so the guard refuses rather than assumes.\n\nTOTP: enroll() resolves the subject from the MFA session (force rejected pre-auth);\nconfirmEnroll() persists the enrollment with lastUsedCounter = -1 (NOT consuming the\nmatched counter) and immediately delegates to mfaService.verifyFactor, so the standard\nverifyAndConsumeTotp chokepoint consumes the code atomically, marks the factor verified\nand - once every required factor is done - authenticates the user in the same request.\nBackup codes are returned as usual.\n\nWebAuthn: startRegistration/finishRegistration accept the guarded pre-auth subject; the\nsession is NOT completed at registration (attestation is not an assertion) - the client\nruns the standard assert+verify right after. New JCR-backed WebAuthnManagementRateLimiter\n(upaWebauthn:lockout mixin, mirrors the TOTP limiter) throttles the pre-auth registration\nsurface.\n\nAGENTS.md: chokepoint invariant updated for the delegated consume; new pre-auth guard\ninvariant documented.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmokG5gACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mjYwf9E95uKBh8NJB9JLzZ70YPc3dJDEXii51PrYCF+kLYrLQWv0LEvhgrFC0Q\nf9NlppQ3YzSEuNFBHMm94Gg7KSvLEg8g57s6j06qb+m5xeZnSk/PpIL6S1SrMvi+\nzE4mNeDs7ccYyQPxxotEAGVyxD+5qR0zma6PDeoOsAX5IRnRFsA+7aVZJQ3+znAF\niXUHWZEBmlxVDtmgcV7Pr/h0rx3M2aKH/U4P6AFCE3ZWXIdJi0Sdg3S4JEB9iI+M\nnKLTxOkjoIpktoMncZtJu2Jtvhev9TrvXeyeuyU7ZJ0l84L3E8hHASiPwB0I9A8x\neME8UNK9LjYi25NISMvo0fLYSW41WQ==\n=Ygcw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/52bb0a0001f6ca3504c0a504fc2a7e62ee79415b","node_id":"C_kwDOSkCe6NoAKDUyYmIwYTAwMDFmNmNhMzUwNGMwYTUwNGZjMmE3ZTYyZWU3OTQxNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commit/e441a764f18e787a95b6a031564009b3d370aa68","sha":"e441a764f18e787a95b6a031564009b3d370aa68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/e441a764f18e787a95b6a031564009b3d370aa68"}],"sha":"52bb0a0001f6ca3504c0a504fc2a7e62ee79415b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/52bb0a0001f6ca3504c0a504fc2a7e62ee79415b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/commits/e441a764f18e787a95b6a031564009b3d370aa68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T12:59:07Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T12:59:26Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"feat: global MFA enforcement policy with cross-factor pick-one semantics\n\nPart A — extensions gains MfaGlobalPolicy (PID org.jahia.modules.mfa.extensions):\nenforcedFactors (comma string parsed by our code — an OSGi String[] cannot be expressed\nreliably in a .cfg, SCR coerces a comma string to one bogus element) + global graceDays\n(clamped 0..365). The MfaSiteProvider SPI evolves to activation semantics: getFactorType(),\nisEnabledForSite / isAnySiteEnabled (renamed from the enforced variants), and a new\nisConfiguredForUser(userId) for the cross-factor check. The /cms/login gate now gates iff\nenforcement is active AND an enforced factor is enabled on the site (fail-closed preserved).\n\nPart B — both factor providers implement the pick-one decision table: enforcement is global\nand a user satisfies it with AT LEAST ONE enforced factor. prepare() skips when another\nenforced factor is already verified in this MFA session (read via MfaService.getMfaSession)\nor is configured for the user (via the sibling MfaSiteProviders); challenges an enrolled\nuser; and for a user with NO enforced factor configured applies the global grace window then\nthrows enrollment_required/registration_required carrying the enrollableFactors offer\n(enforced ∩ enabled-on-site) for the login UI. Site stores'' isAnySiteEnforcing() becomes\nisAnySiteEnabled(); adapters expose enrollment/registration state fail-closed. Both prepare\nGraphQL payloads expose ''skipped'' so the client can drain non-applicable factors with an\nempty verify.\n\nTests: MfaGlobalPolicyTest (parsing/clamping), gate decision tests (policy ∩ enabled,\nfail-closed), and the 9-row decision table per factor. extensions 45, totp 38, webauthn 10\ntests green.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4bae843f8d94d08c260ebf61cce8f198b64cf6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/trees/e4bae843f8d94d08c260ebf61cce8f198b64cf6f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/mfa-community-parent/git/commits/e441a764f18e787a95b6a031564009b3d370aa68","verification":{"payload":"tree e4bae843f8d94d08c260ebf61cce8f198b64cf6f\nparent 64bc5a8dccdbef3fc0f8a5fe055e987f76ce0457\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780750747 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1780750766 +0200\n\nfeat: global MFA enforcement policy with cross-factor pick-one semantics\n\nPart A — extensions gains MfaGlobalPolicy (PID org.jahia.modules.mfa.extensions):\nenforcedFactors (comma string parsed by our code — an OSGi String[] cannot be expressed\nreliably in a .cfg, SCR coerces a comma string to one bogus element) + global graceDays\n(clamped 0..365). The MfaSiteProvider SPI evolves to activation semantics: getFactorType(),\nisEnabledForSite / isAnySiteEnabled (renamed from the enforced variants), and a new\nisConfiguredForUser(userId) for the cross-factor check. The /cms/login gate now gates iff\nenforcement is active AND an enforced factor is enabled on the site (fail-closed preserved).\n\nPart B — both factor providers implement the pick-one decision table: enforcement is global\nand a user satisfies it with AT LEAST ONE enforced factor. prepare() skips when another\nenforced factor is already verified in this MFA session (read via MfaService.getMfaSession)\nor is configured for the user (via the sibling MfaSiteProviders); challenges an enrolled\nuser; and for a user with NO enforced factor configured applies the global grace window then\nthrows enrollment_required/registration_required carrying the enrollableFactors offer\n(enforced ∩ enabled-on-site) for the login UI. Site stores'' isAnySiteEnforcing() becomes\nisAnySiteEnabled(); adapters expose enrollment/registration state fail-closed. Both prepare\nGraphQL payloads expose ''skipped'' so the client can drain non-applicable factors with an\nempty verify.\n\nTests: MfaGlobalPolicyTest (parsing/clamping), gate decision tests (policy ∩ enabled,\nfail-closed), and the 9-row decision table per factor. extensions 45, totp 38, webauthn 10\ntests green.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmokGa4ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mwagf+IDO8vkQJvEf277QKYBd1ASDl450TV+2oVlB21nXw5s0D09bamyUk+ddW\nAJyVhmRg5DW5CnC46PLs6qSPMJwd00SaaUJC5+izmc0V+GbqgWdvpsi6kdoOZ/oM\nZW6t4sFXFQCaGfpBFqT4CVPI9m7/P4kZVNNiijMKjimcGvKF3jlrBLHoKSP5LEcx\nn5G3QjdSDzOz8V1SmDBvf8/hvAWjpkElSx9zrnmJ6TX4uU1Ksc+7OIsEKi6dAgnA\nzIHE4NalsjBp4OQqeyu4VWGJemgFOoqY6Yv0NxKbqBuLMbRmYwkjf+KSB50OqL2L\np8ENGxmbUiT+wkPJYdGC7vOFKVCZ7w==\n=6Wbb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"htt